    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41BD What is a medical device",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.23",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A medical device is:\n(a) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article (whether used alone or in\ncombination, and including the software necessary for its\nproper application) intended, by the person under whose\nname it is or is to be supplied, to be used for human beings\nfor the purpose of one or more of the following:\n(i) diagnosis, prevention, monitoring, prediction,\nprognosis, treatment or alleviation of disease;\n(ii) diagnosis, monitoring, treatment, alleviation of or\ncompensation for an injury or disability;\n(iii) investigation, replacement or modification of the\nanatomy or of a physiological or pathological process or\nstate;\n(iv) control or support of conception;\n(v) in vitro examination of a specimen derived from the\nhuman body for a specific medical purpose;\nand that does not achieve its principal intended action in or\non the human body by pharmacological, immunological or\nmetabolic means, but that may be assisted in its function by\nsuch means; or\n(aa) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article specified under\nsubsection (2A); or\n(ab) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article that is included in a class of\ninstruments, apparatus, appliances, software, implants,\nreagents, materials or other articles specified under\nsubsection (2B); or\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A medical device is:\n(a) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article (whether used alone or in\ncombination, and including the software necessary for its\nproper application) intended, by the person under whose\nname it is or is to be supplied, to be used for human beings\nfor the purpose of one or more of the following:\n(i) diagnosis, prevention, monitoring, prediction,\nprognosis, treatment or alleviation of disease;\n(ii) diagnosis, monitoring, treatment, alleviation of or\ncompensation for an injury or disability;\n(iii) investigation, replacement or modification of the\nanatomy or of a physiological or pathological process or\nstate;\n(iv) control or support of conception;\n(v) in vitro examination of a specimen derived from the\nhuman body for a specific medical purpose;\nand that does not achieve its principal intended action in or\non the human body by pharmacological, immunological or\nmetabolic means, but that may be assisted in its function by\nsuch means; or\n(aa) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article specified under\nsubsection (2A); or\n(ab) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article that is included in a class of\ninstruments, apparatus, appliances, software, implants,\nreagents, materials or other articles specified under\nsubsection (2B); or\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bd-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ea979964f89afcf338e8d56ef3a09e11a8a3a1e450d0d0ff4e34dcc53b39b30",
      "skos:note": "Defines what constitutes a medical device."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41BD What is a medical device",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 23,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A medical device is:\n(a) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article (whether used alone or in\ncombination, and including the software necessary for its\nproper application) intended, by the person under whose\nname it is or is to be supplied, to be used for human beings\nfor the purpose of one or more of the following:\n(i) diagnosis, prevention, monitoring, prediction,\nprognosis, treatment or alleviation of disease;\n(ii) diagnosis, monitoring, treatment, alleviation of or\ncompensation for an injury or disability;\n(iii) investigation, replacement or modification of the\nanatomy or of a physiological or pathological process or\nstate;\n(iv) control or support of conception;\n(v) in vitro examination of a specimen derived from the\nhuman body for a specific medical purpose;\nand that does not achieve its principal intended action in or\non the human body by pharmacological, immunological or\nmetabolic means, but that may be assisted in its function by\nsuch means; or\n(aa) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article specified under\nsubsection (2A); or\n(ab) any instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, implant,\nreagent, material or other article that is included in a class of\ninstruments, apparatus, appliances, software, implants,\nreagents, materials or other articles specified under\nsubsection (2B); or\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bd-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bd"
