    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bf",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41BF System or procedure packs",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bf"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "Two or more goods (including at least one medical device) are a\nsystem or procedure pack if:\n(a) all of the goods are to be interconnected or combined for use\nin a medical or surgical procedure; or\n(b) all of the goods are packaged together for use in a medical or\nsurgical procedure.",
      "skos:definition": "Two or more goods (including at least one medical device) are a\nsystem or procedure pack if:\n(a) all of the goods are to be interconnected or combined for use\nin a medical or surgical procedure; or\n(b) all of the goods are packaged together for use in a medical or\nsurgical procedure.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bf-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b657e94d26791d98c791bec283cfd331c76b343a6df57548bb80ea0dc9dad9b3",
      "skos:note": "Goods are a system or procedure pack if they are interconnected or combined for use in a medical or surgical procedure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bf",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41BF System or procedure packs",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "Two or more goods (including at least one medical device) are a\nsystem or procedure pack if:\n(a) all of the goods are to be interconnected or combined for use\nin a medical or surgical procedure; or\n(b) all of the goods are packaged together for use in a medical or\nsurgical procedure."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bf-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bf"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41BG Manufacturers of medical devices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The manufacturer of a medical device is the person who is\nresponsible for the design, production, packaging and labelling of\nthe device before it is supplied under the person’s name, whether\nor not it is the person, or another person acting on the person’s\nbehalf, who carries out those operations.\n(2) If subsection (1) does not apply to a medical device, the\nmanufacturer of the device is the person who, with a view to\nsupplying the device under the person’s name, does one or more of\nthe following using ready-made products:\n(a) assembles the device;\n(b) packages the device;\n(c) processes the device;\n(d) fully refurbishes the device;\n(e) labels the device;\n(f) assigns to the device its purpose by means of information\nsupplied, by the person, on or in any one or more of the\nfollowing:\n(i) the labelling on the device;\n(ii) the instructions for using the device;\n(iii) any advertising material relating to the device;\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIntroduction  Part 4-1\nInterpretation  Division 2\nSection 41BH\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(iv) technical documentation describing the mechanism of\naction of the device.\n(3) However, a person is not the manufacturer of a medical device if:\n(a) the person assembles or adapts the device for an individual\npatient; and\n(b) the device has already been supplied by another person; and\n(c) the assembly or adaptation does not change the purpose\nintended for the device by means of information supplied by\nthat other person, on or in any one or more of the following:\n(i) the labelling on the device;\n(ii) the instructions for using the device;\n(iii) any advertising material relating to the device;\n(iv) technical documentation describing the mechanism of\naction of the device.\n(4) A person is not the manufacturer of a medical device if the person\nis included in a class of persons prescribed by the regulations for\nthe purposes of this subsection.\nNote:\nThis section applies in relation to vaping goods that are a medical\ndevice.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The manufacturer of a medical device is the person who is\nresponsible for the design, production, packaging and labelling of\nthe device before it is supplied under the person’s name, whether\nor not it is the person, or another person acting on the person’s\nbehalf, who carries out those operations.\n(2) If subsection (1) does not apply to a medical device, the\nmanufacturer of the device is the person who, with a view to\nsupplying the device under the person’s name, does one or more of\nthe following using ready-made products:\n(a) assembles the device;\n(b) packages the device;\n(c) processes the device;\n(d) fully refurbishes the device;\n(e) labels the device;\n(f) assigns to the device its purpose by means of information\nsupplied, by the person, on or in any one or more of the\nfollowing:\n(i) the labelling on the device;\n(ii) the instructions for using the device;\n(iii) any advertising material relating to the device;\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIntroduction  Part 4-1\nInterpretation  Division 2\nSection 41BH\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(iv) technical documentation describing the mechanism of\naction of the device.\n(3) However, a person is not the manufacturer of a medical device if:\n(a) the person assembles or adapts the device for an individual\npatient; and\n(b) the device has already been supplied by another person; and\n(c) the assembly or adaptation does not change the purpose\nintended for the device by means of information supplied by\nthat other person, on or in any one or more of the following:\n(i) the labelling on the device;\n(ii) the instructions for using the device;\n(iii) any advertising material relating to the device;\n(iv) technical documentation describing the mechanism of\naction of the device.\n(4) A person is not the manufacturer of a medical device if the person\nis included in a class of persons prescribed by the regulations for\nthe purposes of this subsection.\nNote:\nThis section applies in relation to vaping goods that are a medi",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bg-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bg-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "60f0bee624dc8ac77831bb871915ed6a8e80e6b4af7f6c117bafabe299fdebfb"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41BG Manufacturers of medical devices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The manufacturer of a medical device is the person who is\nresponsible for the design, production, packaging and labelling of\nthe device before it is supplied under the person’s name, whether\nor not it is the person, or another person acting on the person’s\nbehalf, who carries out those operations.\n(2) If subsection (1) does not apply to a medical device, the\nmanufacturer of the device is the person who, with a view to\nsupplying the device under the person’s name, does one or more of\nthe following using ready-made products:\n(a) assembles the device;\n(b) packages the device;\n(c) processes the device;\n(d) fully refurbishes the device;\n(e) labels the device;\n(f) assigns to the device its purpose by means of information\nsupplied, by the person, on or in any one or more of the\nfollowing:\n(i) the labelling on the device;\n(ii) the instructions for using the device;\n(iii) any advertising material relating to the device;\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIntroduction  Part 4-1\nInterpretation  Division 2\nSection 41BH\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(iv) technical documentation describing the mechanism of\naction of the device.\n(3) However, a person is not the manufacturer of a medical device if:\n(a) the person assembles or adapts the device for an individual\npatient; and\n(b) the device has already been supplied by another person; and\n(c) the assembly or adaptation does not change the purpose\nintended for the device by means of information supplied by\nthat other person, on or in any one or more of the following:\n(i) the labelling on the device;\n(ii) the instructions for using the device;\n(iii) any advertising material relating to the device;\n(iv) technical documentation describing the mechanism of\naction of the device.\n(4) A person is not the manufacturer of a medical device if the person\nis included in a class of persons prescribed by the regulations for\nthe purposes of this subsection.\nNote:\nThis section applies in relation to vaping goods that are a medical\ndevice."
    },
