    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41BH(2) Meaning of compliance with essential principles",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bh-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a medical device is also taken, for the purposes of this\nChapter (other than Part 4-11), to comply with the essential\nprinciples if:\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device contravenes the essential principles only\nin respect of a part or parts of the essential principles to\nwhich that medical device standard, or one or more of those\nmedical device standards, relate.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, a medical device is also taken, for the purposes of this\nChapter (other than Part 4-11), to comply with the essential\nprinciples if:\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device contravenes the essential principles only\nin respect of a part or parts of the essential principles to\nwhich that medical device standard, or one or more of those\nmedical device standards, relate.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bh-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bh-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7ed323b589b283d900b869a93c9759043e6aeea3b057cbdd9992f4dfa60da8b3",
      "skos:note": "Compliance with medical device standards is sufficient for compliance with essential principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bh-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41BH(2) Meaning of compliance with essential principles",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, a medical device is also taken, for the purposes of this\nChapter (other than Part 4-11), to comply with the essential\nprinciples if:\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device contravenes the essential principles only\nin respect of a part or parts of the essential principles to\nwhich that medical device standard, or one or more of those\nmedical device standards, relate.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bh-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bh-ss-2"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
