      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A requirement that is comparable to a conformity assessment\nprocedure is taken, for the purposes of this Chapter, not to have\nbeen applied to a medical device by the manufacturer of the device\nif:\n(a) there has been a contravention of the requirement; and\n(b) the contravention relates, wholly or partly, to that device or\nits manufacture.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIntroduction  Part 4-1\nInterpretation  Division 2\nSection 41BIB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A requirement that is comparable to a conformity assessment\nprocedure is taken, for the purposes of this Chapter, not to have\nbeen applied to a medical device by the manufacturer of the device\nif:\n(a) there has been a contravention of the requirement; and\n(b) the contravention relates, wholly or partly, to that device or\nits manufacture.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIntroduction  Part 4-1\nInterpretation  Division 2\nSection 41BIB\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
