    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bi-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41BI(2) Meaning of non-application of conformity assessment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bi-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Secretary may, by notifiable instrument, determine a body for\nthe purposes of subsection (1). The Secretary must be satisfied that\nthe body:\n(a) is established outside Australia; and\n(b) is empowered to issue certificates or other documents to the\neffect that the body is satisfied that requirements, comparable\nto the conformity assessment procedures, have been applied\nto medical devices by the manufacturers of the devices.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Secretary may, by notifiable instrument, determine a body for\nthe purposes of subsection (1). The Secretary must be satisfied that\nthe body:\n(a) is established outside Australia; and\n(b) is empowered to issue certificates or other documents to the\neffect that the body is satisfied that requirements, comparable\nto the conformity assessment procedures, have been applied\nto medical devices by the manufacturers of the devices.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bi"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bi-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bi-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d2ed811c0d8c04d387fe3897330a16172068874086513aaa37c6a8e7b74af708",
      "skos:note": "The Secretary may determine a body for the purposes of subsection (1). Exemptions from conformity assessment requirements"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41bi-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41BI(2) Meaning of non-application of conformity assessment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Secretary may, by notifiable instrument, determine a body for\nthe purposes of subsection (1). The Secretary must be satisfied that\nthe body:\n(a) is established outside Australia; and\n(b) is empowered to issue certificates or other documents to the\neffect that the body is satisfied that requirements, comparable\nto the conformity assessment procedures, have been applied\nto medical devices by the manufacturers of the devices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bi-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41bi-ss-2"
