    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41CB Medical device standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41cb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make an order\ndetermining that:\n(a) matters specified in the order constitute a medical device\nstandard for kinds of medical devices identified in the order;\nand\n(b) medical devices of those kinds that comply with the standard\nare to be treated as complying with those parts of the\nessential principles specified in the standard.\nNote:\nSection 12 of the Legislation Act 2003 deals with when a legislative\ninstrument commences.\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary or revoke an\norder made under subsection (1).\n(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make an order\ndetermining that:\n(a) matters specified in the order constitute a medical device\nstandard for kinds of medical devices identified in the order;\nand\n(b) medical devices of those kinds that comply with the standard\nare to be treated as complying with those parts of the\nessential principles specified in the standard.\nNote:\nSection 12 of the Legislation Act 2003 deals with when a legislative\ninstrument commences.\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary or revoke an\norder made under subsection (1).\n(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cb-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fa09e7c4a595ca64a2d0d34a3a7db4f56277e488c45222ce76f92c800b0fd54c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41cb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41CB Medical device standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make an order\ndetermining that:\n(a) matters specified in the order constitute a medical device\nstandard for kinds of medical devices identified in the order;\nand\n(b) medical devices of those kinds that comply with the standard\nare to be treated as complying with those parts of the\nessential principles specified in the standard.\nNote:\nSection 12 of the Legislation Act 2003 deals with when a legislative\ninstrument commences.\n(2) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary or revoke an\norder made under subsection (1).\n(3) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41cb-ss-1",
