    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41DC Conformity assessment standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41dc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make an order\ndetermining that:\n(a) matters specified in the order constitute a conformity\nassessment standard for quality management systems\nidentified in the order; and\n(b) a quality management system that complies with the standard\nis to be treated as having had applied to it those parts of the\nconformity assessment procedures specified in the standard.\nNote:\nSection 12 of the Legislation Act 2003 deals with when a legislative\ninstrument commences.\n(2) A conformity assessment standard may be limited to particular\nkinds of medical devices.\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary or revoke an\norder made under subsection (1).\n(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make an order\ndetermining that:\n(a) matters specified in the order constitute a conformity\nassessment standard for quality management systems\nidentified in the order; and\n(b) a quality management system that complies with the standard\nis to be treated as having had applied to it those parts of the\nconformity assessment procedures specified in the standard.\nNote:\nSection 12 of the Legislation Act 2003 deals with when a legislative\ninstrument commences.\n(2) A conformity assessment standard may be limited to particular\nkinds of medical devices.\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary or revoke an\norder made under subsection (1).\n(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a3019b72c3f7a945b2c3c9558ecd605619242517dae46fb4a722b6b628e4fd2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41dc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41DC Conformity assessment standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make an order\ndetermining that:\n(a) matters specified in the order constitute a conformity\nassessment standard for quality management systems\nidentified in the order; and\n(b) a quality management system that complies with the standard\nis to be treated as having had applied to it those parts of the\nconformity assessment procedures specified in the standard.\nNote:\nSection 12 of the Legislation Act 2003 deals with when a legislative\ninstrument commences.\n(2) A conformity assessment standard may be limited to particular\nkinds of medical devices.\n(3) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, vary or revoke an\norder made under subsection (1).\n(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time."
    },
