    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41DC(4) Conformity assessment standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41dc-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f204e87118e03f338d8f942622e13fe7aa873a32b3d50a0b171d99f2a5c0c077",
      "skos:note": "Allows for provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating an existing instrument or writing."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41dc-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41DC(4) Conformity assessment standards",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an order\nunder subsection (1) of this section, or a variation of such an order,\nmay make provision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting\nor incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dc-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41DD Content of conformity assessment standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41dd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.41",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Without limiting the scope of section 41DC, an order establishing a\nconformity assessment standard for a kind of medical device may\nbe specified by reference to:\n(a) procedures to be carried out under the quality management\nsystems for the design, manufacture and final inspection of\nthe devices; or\n(b) a standard published by a standards organisation; or\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Without limiting the scope of section 41DC, an order establishing a\nconformity assessment standard for a kind of medical device may\nbe specified by reference to:\n(a) procedures to be carried out under the quality management\nsystems for the design, manufacture and final inspection of\nthe devices; or\n(b) a standard published by a standards organisation; or\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dd-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c1703b55d1ca02420abfffb5cf8f3460e9e414c159b6d8d591aaca8a4001ca82",
      "skos:note": "Specifies how an order establishing a conformity assessment standard for a kind of medical device may be specified."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41dd",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41DD Content of conformity assessment standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Without limiting the scope of section 41DC, an order establishing a\nconformity assessment standard for a kind of medical device may\nbe specified by reference to:\n(a) procedures to be carried out under the quality management\nsystems for the design, manufacture and final inspection of\nthe devices; or\n(b) a standard published by a standards organisation; or\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dd-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41dd"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41de",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41DE Inconsistencies between conformity assessment standards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41de"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.42",
      "values:originalText": "A conformity assessment standard that:\n(a) identifies quality management systems to which it applies;\nand\n(b) is inconsistent with another conformity assessment standard\nthat applies only to particular kinds of medical devices;\nis, to the extent of the inconsistency, of no effect in relation to the\ndevices referred to in paragraph (b).\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\n\nSection 41E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "A conformity assessment standard that:\n(a) identifies quality management systems to which it applies;\nand\n(b) is inconsistent with another conformity assessment standard\nthat applies only to particular kinds of medical devices;\nis, to the extent of the inconsistency, of no effect in relation to the\ndevices referred to in paragraph (b).\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\n\nSection 41E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41de-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41de-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "20dc965ccfe51ffcf7503baf65b1bc6a34539833a496d0f97f6a6d07bad08194",
      "skos:note": "Inconsistencies between conformity assessment standards are of no effect."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41de",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41DE Inconsistencies between conformity assessment standards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 42,
      "values:originalText": "A conformity assessment standard that:\n(a) identifies quality management systems to which it applies;\nand\n(b) is inconsistent with another conformity assessment standard\nthat applies only to particular kinds of medical devices;\nis, to the extent of the inconsistency, of no effect in relation to the\ndevices referred to in paragraph (b).\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\n\nSection 41E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41de-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41de"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41de-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibits inconsistency between conformity assessment standards.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41E What this Part is about",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.43",
      "values:originalText": "The Secretary can issue a conformity assessment certificate (which\nmay be limited to some medical devices) in respect of a\nmanufacturer of medical devices, signifying one or more of these:\n(a)\nthat relevant quality management systems have been\napplied to the device;\n(b)\nthe essential principles for the device have been\ncomplied with;\n(c)\nother certification requirements of the conformity\nassessment procedures have been met.\nNote:\nA conformity assessment certificate may be required for an\napplication to include a kind of medical device in the Register to pass\npreliminary assessment: see paragraph 41FDB(2)(e).\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "The Secretary can issue a conformity assessment certificate (which\nmay be limited to some medical devices) in respect of a\nmanufacturer of medical devices, signifying one or more of these:\n(a)\nthat relevant quality management systems have been\napplied to the device;\n(b)\nthe essential principles for the device have been\ncomplied with;\n(c)\nother certification requirements of the conformity\nassessment procedures have been met.\nNote:\nA conformity assessment certificate may be required for an\napplication to include a kind of medical device in the Register to pass\npreliminary assessment: see paragraph 41FDB(2)(e).\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41e-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cfc3e5bf72bdd4739a2981ce5d04cb0b3806bdc6bf78e08dbe8cf53253ad0b83",
      "skos:note": "Secretary can issue conformity assessment certificate for medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41e",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41E What this Part is about",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 43,
      "values:originalText": "The Secretary can issue a conformity assessment certificate (which\nmay be limited to some medical devices) in respect of a\nmanufacturer of medical devices, signifying one or more of these:\n(a)\nthat relevant quality management systems have been\napplied to the device;\n(b)\nthe essential principles for the device have been\ncomplied with;\n(c)\nother certification requirements of the conformity\nassessment procedures have been met.\nNote:\nA conformity assessment certificate may be required for an\napplication to include a kind of medical device in the Register to pass\npreliminary assessment: see paragraph 41FDB(2)(e).\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41e-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41e"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EB Applications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41eb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.44",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An application for a conformity assessment certificate must:\n(a) be made in accordance with a form approved, in writing, by\nthe Secretary or in such other manner as is approved, in\nwriting, by the Secretary; and\n(b) be delivered to an office of the Department specified by the\nSecretary.\nNote:\nA conformity assessment fee is payable under section 41LA for\nconsideration of the application.\n(2) An application is not effective if:\n(a) the prescribed application fee has not been paid; or\n(b) the application contains information that is false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA person might also commit an offence, or contravene a civil penalty\nprovision, if the person makes a statement in an application that is\nfalse or misleading in a material particular: see sections 41EI and\n41EIA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\nIssuing conformity assessment certificates  Division 1\nSection 41EC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(3) An approval of a form may require or permit an application or\ninformation to be given in accordance with specified software\nrequirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.\n(4) The Secretary may, by written notice given to an applicant for a\nconformity assessment certificate, require the applicant to allow an\nauthorised person, at any reasonable time specified in the notice, to\ninspect:\n(a) the premises (including premises outside Australia) and\nequipment, processes and facilities that are being or will be\nused to manufacture medical devices of the kind in question;\nand\n(b) any other kinds of medical devices on those premises.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An application for a conformity assessment certificate must:\n(a) be made in accordance with a form approved, in writing, by\nthe Secretary or in such other manner as is approved, in\nwriting, by the Secretary; and\n(b) be delivered to an office of the Department specified by the\nSecretary.\nNote:\nA conformity assessment fee is payable under section 41LA for\nconsideration of the application.\n(2) An application is not effective if:\n(a) the prescribed application fee has not been paid; or\n(b) the application contains information that is false or\nmisleading in a material particular.\nNote:\nA person might also commit an offence, or contravene a civil penalty\nprovision, if the person makes a statement in an application that is\nfalse or misleading in a material particular: see sections 41EI and\n41EIA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\nIssuing conformity assessment certificates  Division 1\nSection 41EC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(3) An approval of a form may require or permit an application or\ninformation to be given in accordance with specified software\nrequirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.\n(4) The Secretary may, by written notice given to an applicant for a\nconformity assessment certificate, require the applicant to allow an\nauthorised person, at any reasonable time specified in the notice, to\ninspect:\n(a) the premises (including premises outside Australia) and\nequipment, processes and facilities that are being or will be\nused to manufacture medical devices of the kind in question;\nand\n(b) any other kinds of medical devices on those premises.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eb-ss-2"
        },
