    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EF Duration of certificate",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ef"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.50",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The conformity assessment certificate commences on the day\nspecified for the purpose in the certificate. The certificate must\nspecify the period for which it is to be in force (which must be no\nlonger than 5 years).\n(2) A conformity assessment certificate has effect at all times:\n(a) unless the certificate is suspended under Division 3; or\n(b) until the end of the period specified in the certificate, or if the\nSecretary extends that period, until the end of that extended\nperiod; or\n(c) until the certificate is revoked under Division 4.\nExtensions\n(3) The Secretary may, in writing and on his or her own initiative,\nextend the period for which a conformity assessment certificate is\nin force.\n(4) An extension must be no longer than 12 months.\n(5) Only one extension may be given.\n(6) The Secretary:\n(a) must give notice of an extension to the manufacturer in\nrelation to whom the certificate was issued; and\n(b) may give notice of an extension to the applicant for the\ncertificate (if the applicant is not the manufacturer).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The conformity assessment certificate commences on the day\nspecified for the purpose in the certificate. The certificate must\nspecify the period for which it is to be in force (which must be no\nlonger than 5 years).\n(2) A conformity assessment certificate has effect at all times:\n(a) unless the certificate is suspended under Division 3; or\n(b) until the end of the period specified in the certificate, or if the\nSecretary extends that period, until the end of that extended\nperiod; or\n(c) until the certificate is revoked under Division 4.\nExtensions\n(3) The Secretary may, in writing and on his or her own initiative,\nextend the period for which a conformity assessment certificate is\nin force.\n(4) An extension must be no longer than 12 months.\n(5) Only one extension may be given.\n(6) The Secretary:\n(a) must give notice of an extension to the manufacturer in\nrelation to whom the certificate was issued; and\n(b) may give notice of an extension to the applicant for the\ncertificate (if the applicant is not the manufacturer).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ef-ss-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "be9e3aebdb9ece0b37a6e14b351db525654c42575e4a179a0e71a4aa2c314ce6"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ef",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EF Duration of certificate",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The conformity assessment certificate commences on the day\nspecified for the purpose in the certificate. The certificate must\nspecify the period for which it is to be in force (which must be no\nlonger than 5 years).\n(2) A conformity assessment certificate has effect at all times:\n(a) unless the certificate is suspended under Division 3; or\n(b) until the end of the period specified in the certificate, or if the\nSecretary extends that period, until the end of that extended\nperiod; or\n(c) until the certificate is revoked under Division 4.\nExtensions\n(3) The Secretary may, in writing and on his or her own initiative,\nextend the period for which a conformity assessment certificate is\nin force.\n(4) An extension must be no longer than 12 months.\n(5) Only one extension may be given.\n(6) The Secretary:\n(a) must give notice of an extension to the manufacturer in\nrelation to whom the certificate was issued; and\n(b) may give notice of an extension to the applicant for the\ncertificate (if the applicant is not the manufacturer)."
    },
