        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: Agent"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eg-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Failure to comply with requirements.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Lapse of application."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eg-logic-descriptionlogic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:DescriptionLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Classify",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classification of applications based on compliance",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::dl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Applications are classified as compliant or non-compliant.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Lapse of application if non-compliant."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EH Treating applications as having been refused",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41eh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for an application for a conformity assessment\ncertificate may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant\nwishes to treat the application as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the applicant has not been notified of\na decision whether to issue the certificate.\n(2) The notice may be given at any time before the applicant is notified\nof the decision.\n(3) If a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to issue the certificate; and\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The applicant for an application for a conformity assessment\ncertificate may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant\nwishes to treat the application as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the applicant has not been notified of\na decision whether to issue the certificate.\n(2) The notice may be given at any time before the applicant is notified\nof the decision.\n(3) If a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to issue the certificate; and\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07a1f024e116e6afd57c879fe9c4baa9e3086dffa9c8d2b66a49e735347ea1d8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41eh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EH Treating applications as having been refused",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for an application for a conformity assessment\ncertificate may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant\nwishes to treat the application as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the applicant has not been notified of\na decision whether to issue the certificate.\n(2) The notice may be given at any time before the applicant is notified\nof the decision.\n(3) If a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to issue the certificate; and\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
