      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for an application for a conformity assessment\ncertificate may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant\nwishes to treat the application as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the applicant has not been notified of\na decision whether to issue the certificate.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The applicant for an application for a conformity assessment\ncertificate may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant\nwishes to treat the application as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the applicant has not been notified of\na decision whether to issue the certificate.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41eh-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "75009c47e7d13c6494a39c6ce44ce9957f923ce17d4b0094127703568d4405c4",
      "skos:note": "Applicant may treat application as refused if no decision is made within a period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41eh-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EH(1) Treating applications as having been refused",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for an application for a conformity assessment\ncertificate may give the Secretary written notice that the applicant\nwishes to treat the application as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the applicant has not been notified of\na decision whether to issue the certificate."
    },
