    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ei-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EI(6) Criminal offences for making a false statement",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ei-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.52",
      "values:originalText": "(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.\n41EIA  Civil penalty for making a false statement\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person makes a statement (whether orally, in a document\nor in any other way); and\n(b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(c) the statement is in or in connection with an application for a\nconformity assessment certificate.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.\n41EIA  Civil penalty for making a false statement\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person makes a statement (whether orally, in a document\nor in any other way); and\n(b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(c) the statement is in or in connection with an application for a\nconformity assessment certificate.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ei"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ei-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ei-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8aca9f6b9929541ce9832f9c101208b6939102829c3a414562388d34ea7e6fc7",
      "skos:note": "Making a false statement in an application for conformity assessment certificate is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ei-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EI(6) Criminal offences for making a false statement",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 52,
      "values:originalText": "(6) An offence against subsection (5) is an offence of strict liability.\n41EIA  Civil penalty for making a false statement\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person makes a statement (whether orally, in a document\nor in any other way); and\n(b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular;\nand\n(c) the statement is in or in connection with an application for a\nconformity assessment certificate.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
