    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41em",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EM Suspension of conformity assessment certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41em"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, suspend the\ncertificate if the Secretary is satisfied that it is likely that there are\ngrounds for revoking the certificate under section 41ET.\n(2) The suspension may be limited to some medical devices of that\nkind, as specified in the notice.\n(3) The notice must specify the period of the suspension. The period\nmust not exceed 6 months.\nNote:\nThe period of the suspension may be extended under section 41EO.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, suspend the\ncertificate if the Secretary is satisfied that it is likely that there are\ngrounds for revoking the certificate under section 41ET.\n(2) The suspension may be limited to some medical devices of that\nkind, as specified in the notice.\n(3) The notice must specify the period of the suspension. The period\nmust not exceed 6 months.\nNote:\nThe period of the suspension may be extended under section 41EO.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41em-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41em-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41em-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "791ed762b50a8c0fb3e3614d252d8b76e74f6b12ef56455175358fd6e5858d3b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41em",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EM Suspension of conformity assessment certificates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued, suspend the\ncertificate if the Secretary is satisfied that it is likely that there are\ngrounds for revoking the certificate under section 41ET.\n(2) The suspension may be limited to some medical devices of that\nkind, as specified in the notice.\n(3) The notice must specify the period of the suspension. The period\nmust not exceed 6 months.\nNote:\nThe period of the suspension may be extended under section 41EO."
    },
