    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41en",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EN Notice of proposed suspension",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41en"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.58",
      "values:originalText": "(1) However, before suspending a conformity assessment certificate,\nthe Secretary must:\n(a) inform the person in writing that the Secretary proposes the\nsuspension and set out the reasons for it; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make\nsubmissions to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nsuspension.\n(2) The Secretary is not to make a decision relating to the proposed\nsuspension until the Secretary has had regard to any submissions\nthe person makes under paragraph (1)(b).\n(3) This section does not apply if the notice under section 41EM states\nthat the suspension is necessary to prevent imminent risk of death,\nserious illness or serious injury.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\nSuspension of conformity assessment certificates  Division 3\nSection 41EO\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) However, before suspending a conformity assessment certificate,\nthe Secretary must:\n(a) inform the person in writing that the Secretary proposes the\nsuspension and set out the reasons for it; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make\nsubmissions to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nsuspension.\n(2) The Secretary is not to make a decision relating to the proposed\nsuspension until the Secretary has had regard to any submissions\nthe person makes under paragraph (1)(b).\n(3) This section does not apply if the notice under section 41EM states\nthat the suspension is necessary to prevent imminent risk of death,\nserious illness or serious injury.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\nSuspension of conformity assessment certificates  Division 3\nSection 41EO\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41en-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41en-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41en-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c3260d0b6fc45880858b4e379a6ab3978457e48d52690b71166837c4ecf7d652"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41en",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EN Notice of proposed suspension",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 58,
      "values:originalText": "(1) However, before suspending a conformity assessment certificate,\nthe Secretary must:\n(a) inform the person in writing that the Secretary proposes the\nsuspension and set out the reasons for it; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make\nsubmissions to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nsuspension.\n(2) The Secretary is not to make a decision relating to the proposed\nsuspension until the Secretary has had regard to any submissions\nthe person makes under paragraph (1)(b).\n(3) This section does not apply if the notice under section 41EM states\nthat the suspension is necessary to prevent imminent risk of death,\nserious illness or serious injury.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nConformity assessment certificates  Part 4-4\nSuspension of conformity assessment certificates  Division 3\nSection 41EO\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
