    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ep",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EP Revocation of suspension",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ep"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.59",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must revoke the suspension if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the conformity assessment certificate\nwas suspended no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the certificate.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary must revoke the suspension if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the conformity assessment certificate\nwas suspended no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the certificate.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ep-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ep-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c14b17c16df9f5a641036717f24e00fb166071772851529b63c0500adfd545cd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ep",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EP Revocation of suspension",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 59,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must revoke the suspension if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the conformity assessment certificate\nwas suspended no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the certificate.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
