      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41ES Immediate revocation of conformity assessment certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41es"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the manufacturer in\nrelation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued,\nrevoke the certificate if the manufacturer requests in writing the\nrevocation of the certificate.\n(2) If:\n(a) the Secretary revokes a certificate under subsection (1); and\n(b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day\nthe certificate was revoked, the manufacturer requests, in\nwriting, the Secretary to withdraw the revocation; and\n(c) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee\n(if any);\nthe Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the manufacturer,\nwithdraw the revocation.\n(3) If the revocation is withdrawn, the revocation is taken never to\nhave occurred.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the manufacturer in\nrelation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued,\nrevoke the certificate if the manufacturer requests in writing the\nrevocation of the certificate.\n(2) If:\n(a) the Secretary revokes a certificate under subsection (1); and\n(b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day\nthe certificate was revoked, the manufacturer requests, in\nwriting, the Secretary to withdraw the revocation; and\n(c) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee\n(if any);\nthe Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the manufacturer,\nwithdraw the revocation.\n(3) If the revocation is withdrawn, the revocation is taken never to\nhave occurred.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41es-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f017e3a21dc97f41aad2a8c9a48226fcf5935578016a140bfe5a6c02efde8a93"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41es",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41ES Immediate revocation of conformity assessment certificates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the manufacturer in\nrelation to whom a conformity assessment certificate is issued,\nrevoke the certificate if the manufacturer requests in writing the\nrevocation of the certificate.\n(2) If:\n(a) the Secretary revokes a certificate under subsection (1); and\n(b) before the end of the period of 90 days beginning on the day\nthe certificate was revoked, the manufacturer requests, in\nwriting, the Secretary to withdraw the revocation; and\n(c) the request is accompanied by the prescribed application fee\n(if any);\nthe Secretary may, by notice in writing given to the manufacturer,\nwithdraw the revocation.\n(3) If the revocation is withdrawn, the revocation is taken never to\nhave occurred.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
