      "cml:integrityHash": "a7ccd73a8675309cd6c7c0f38f97b0efd07695c3922c0869794b1e062c9952ee",
      "skos:note": "A reference to a person convicted of an offence includes a reference to a person in respect of whom an order has been made relating to the offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41et-ss-1a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41ET(1A) Revocation of conformity assessment certificates after notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) A reference in paragraph (1)(e) to a person convicted of an offence\nincludes a reference to a person in respect of whom an order has\nbeen made relating to the offence under:\n(a) section 19B of the Crimes Act 1914; or\n(b) a corresponding provision of a law of a State or Territory.\nNote:\nSection 19B of the Crimes Act 1914 empowers a court that has found\na person to have committed an offence to take action without\nproceeding to record a conviction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41et-ss-1a-norm",
