      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, before revoking the certificate, the Secretary must:\n(a) inform the person in writing that the Secretary proposes the\nrevocation and set out the reasons for it; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make\nsubmissions to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nrevocation.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(2) However, before revoking the certificate, the Secretary must:\n(a) inform the person in writing that the Secretary proposes the\nrevocation and set out the reasons for it; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make\nsubmissions to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nrevocation.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41et"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41et-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41et-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41et-ss-2-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "83eea9b42b8271bc3c73f69e60f5f4ce4ae1b1ca7d2fb3573c8c6bf291504e6e",
      "skos:note": "Secretary must inform and give opportunity to make submissions before revoking conformity assessment certificate."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41et-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41ET(2) Revocation of conformity assessment certificates after notice",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 62,
      "values:originalText": "(2) However, before revoking the certificate, the Secretary must:\n(a) inform the person in writing that the Secretary proposes the\nrevocation and set out the reasons for it; and\n(b) give the person a reasonable opportunity to make\nsubmissions to the Secretary in relation to the proposed\nrevocation.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
