    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ew",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41EW Date of effect of revocation etc. of conformity assessment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ew"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "certificates\nIf the Secretary revokes a conformity assessment certificate, or\nvaries a conformity assessment certificate under\nsubsection 41EU(2), the revocation or variation has effect:\n(a) if the revocation is under section 41ER or 41ES, or the\nvariation relates to a ground of revocation in section 41ER or\n41ES—on the day on which the notice of revocation or\nvariation is given to the person in relation to whom the\ncertificate was issued; or\n(b) in any other case—on such later day as is specified in the\nnotice.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "certificates\nIf the Secretary revokes a conformity assessment certificate, or\nvaries a conformity assessment certificate under\nsubsection 41EU(2), the revocation or variation has effect:\n(a) if the revocation is under section 41ER or 41ES, or the\nvariation relates to a ground of revocation in section 41ER or\n41ES—on the day on which the notice of revocation or\nvariation is given to the person in relation to whom the\ncertificate was issued; or\n(b) in any other case—on such later day as is specified in the\nnotice.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ew-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5af45a80c2bae6b70c6569e91b434873a690d63e59bf4b21f5f0caae7c906dff",
      "skos:note": "Date of effect for revocation or variation of conformity assessment certificate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ew",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41EW Date of effect of revocation etc. of conformity assessment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "certificates\nIf the Secretary revokes a conformity assessment certificate, or\nvaries a conformity assessment certificate under\nsubsection 41EU(2), the revocation or variation has effect:\n(a) if the revocation is under section 41ER or 41ES, or the\nvariation relates to a ground of revocation in section 41ER or\n41ES—on the day on which the notice of revocation or\nvariation is given to the person in relation to whom the\ncertificate was issued; or\n(b) in any other case—on such later day as is specified in the\nnotice.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ew-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ew"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41F What this Part is about",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "Kinds of medical devices can be included in the Register if they\ncomply with the essential principles, and conformity assessment\nprocedures have been applied to the kinds of devices or\nrequirements, comparable to those procedures, have been applied\nto the kinds of devices (and certain other requirements are\ncomplied with).\nInclusions in the Register are subject to certain automatic\nconditions and the Secretary may impose further conditions.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIncluding medical devices in the Register  Part 4-5\nIncluding medical devices in the Register  Division 1\nSection 41FA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "Kinds of medical devices can be included in the Register if they\ncomply with the essential principles, and conformity assessment\nprocedures have been applied to the kinds of devices or\nrequirements, comparable to those procedures, have been applied\nto the kinds of devices (and certain other requirements are\ncomplied with).\nInclusions in the Register are subject to certain automatic\nconditions and the Secretary may impose further conditions.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIncluding medical devices in the Register  Part 4-5\nIncluding medical devices in the Register  Division 1\nSection 41FA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41f-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41f-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "31cfed3971b7703e206891fb100d673a48d9b4cb7fc4c66b937209bf54730f61",
      "skos:note": "Medical devices must comply with certain principles and requirements to be included in the Register."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41f",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41F What this Part is about",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "Kinds of medical devices can be included in the Register if they\ncomply with the essential principles, and conformity assessment\nprocedures have been applied to the kinds of devices or\nrequirements, comparable to those procedures, have been applied\nto the kinds of devices (and certain other requirements are\ncomplied with).\nInclusions in the Register are subject to certain automatic\nconditions and the Secretary may impose further conditions.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nIncluding medical devices in the Register  Part 4-5\nIncluding medical devices in the Register  Division 1\nSection 41FA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41f-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41f"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41f-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Must comply with principles and requirements",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41FA What this Division is about",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41fa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.73",
      "values:originalText": "Kinds of medical devices are usually included in the Register once\nan application is made, together with the required certification and\nthe application passes preliminary assessment. However,\napplications may be selected for audit, which involves checking\nsome or all aspects of the application and certification.\nNote 1:\nIn some cases, an application relating to a kind of medical device will\nnot pass preliminary assessment unless that kind of device is covered\nby a conformity assessment certificate under Part 4-4: see\nparagraph 41FDB(2)(e).\nNote 2:\nDealing in medical devices of a kind not included in the Register may\nbe an offence or may contravene a civil penalty provision: see\nDivision 3 of Part 4-11.\nSubdivision A—Applications",
      "skos:definition": "Kinds of medical devices are usually included in the Register once\nan application is made, together with the required certification and\nthe application passes preliminary assessment. However,\napplications may be selected for audit, which involves checking\nsome or all aspects of the application and certification.\nNote 1:\nIn some cases, an application relating to a kind of medical device will\nnot pass preliminary assessment unless that kind of device is covered\nby a conformity assessment certificate under Part 4-4: see\nparagraph 41FDB(2)(e).\nNote 2:\nDealing in medical devices of a kind not included in the Register may\nbe an offence or may contravene a civil penalty provision: see\nDivision 3 of Part 4-11.\nSubdivision A—Applications",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fa-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fa-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fa-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1e1d20f72fd61bf6562686ba308318d4ccdd13a027c62d7104a08dc512864d12",
      "skos:note": "Applications for medical devices must pass preliminary assessment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41fa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41FA What this Division is about",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 73,
      "values:originalText": "Kinds of medical devices are usually included in the Register once\nan application is made, together with the required certification and\nthe application passes preliminary assessment. However,\napplications may be selected for audit, which involves checking\nsome or all aspects of the application and certification.\nNote 1:\nIn some cases, an application relating to a kind of medical device will\nnot pass preliminary assessment unless that kind of device is covered\nby a conformity assessment certificate under Part 4-4: see\nparagraph 41FDB(2)(e).\nNote 2:\nDealing in medical devices of a kind not included in the Register may\nbe an offence or may contravene a civil penalty provision: see\nDivision 3 of Part 4-11.\nSubdivision A—Applications"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fa-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
