    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41FH Selecting applications for auditing",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41fh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.81",
      "values:originalText": "(1A) This section applies to applications that have passed preliminary\nassessment.\n(1) The Secretary:\n(a) must select for auditing any application for a kind of medical\ndevice to be included in the Register that is an application of\nthe kind prescribed by the regulations; and\n(b) may select for auditing any other application for a kind of\nmedical device to be included in the Register.\nNote:\nAn application audit assessment fee is payable in respect of any\napplication that the Secretary must select for auditing: see Part 4-10.\n(2) If an application is selected for auditing:\n(a) the Secretary must give the applicant a written notice (the\nselection notice) that:\n(i) informs the applicant of the selection; and\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1A) This section applies to applications that have passed preliminary\nassessment.\n(1) The Secretary:\n(a) must select for auditing any application for a kind of medical\ndevice to be included in the Register that is an application of\nthe kind prescribed by the regulations; and\n(b) may select for auditing any other application for a kind of\nmedical device to be included in the Register.\nNote:\nAn application audit assessment fee is payable in respect of any\napplication that the Secretary must select for auditing: see Part 4-10.\n(2) If an application is selected for auditing:\n(a) the Secretary must give the applicant a written notice (the\nselection notice) that:\n(i) informs the applicant of the selection; and\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fh-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fh-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41fh-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "66457122c5f630cf409ba72872c27541259e1e4820b24b39c55633f62b256101"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41fh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41FH Selecting applications for auditing",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 81,
      "values:originalText": "(1A) This section applies to applications that have passed preliminary\nassessment.\n(1) The Secretary:\n(a) must select for auditing any application for a kind of medical\ndevice to be included in the Register that is an application of\nthe kind prescribed by the regulations; and\n(b) may select for auditing any other application for a kind of\nmedical device to be included in the Register.\nNote:\nAn application audit assessment fee is payable in respect of any\napplication that the Secretary must select for auditing: see Part 4-10.\n(2) If an application is selected for auditing:\n(a) the Secretary must give the applicant a written notice (the\nselection notice) that:\n(i) informs the applicant of the selection; and\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
