      },
      "cml:operator": "Applicable",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines temporal intervals for suspension and cancellation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Suspension and cancellation occur under certain circumstances.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Temporal intervals are defined"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ga",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GA Suspension of kinds of medical devices from the Register",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ga"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register,\nsuspend the kind of device from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(i) there is a potential risk of death, serious illness or\nserious injury if the kind of device continues to be\nincluded in the Register; and\n(ii) it is likely that the person will, within the period of the\nsuspension, be able to take the action necessary to\nensure that the kind of device would not cause a\npotential risk of death, serious illness or serious injury if\nit were to continue to be included in the Register; or\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that it is likely that there are grounds\nfor cancelling the entry of the kind of device from the\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register,\nsuspend the kind of device from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(i) there is a potential risk of death, serious illness or\nserious injury if the kind of device continues to be\nincluded in the Register; and\n(ii) it is likely that the person will, within the period of the\nsuspension, be able to take the action necessary to\nensure that the kind of device would not cause a\npotential risk of death, serious illness or serious injury if\nit were to continue to be included in the Register; or\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that it is likely that there are grounds\nfor cancelling the entry of the kind of device from the\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ga-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ga-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ga-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "334da9fac63999f10b5a25474cd4dd41808679e038039ae7605bc3648811ba08",
      "skos:note": "Suspension of medical devices from the Register"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ga",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GA Suspension of kinds of medical devices from the Register",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to the person in relation\nto whom a kind of medical device is included in the Register,\nsuspend the kind of device from the Register if:\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(i) there is a potential risk of death, serious illness or\nserious injury if the kind of device continues to be\nincluded in the Register; and\n(ii) it is likely that the person will, within the period of the\nsuspension, be able to take the action necessary to\nensure that the kind of device would not cause a\npotential risk of death, serious illness or serious injury if\nit were to continue to be included in the Register; or\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that it is likely that there are grounds\nfor cancelling the entry of the kind of device from the\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
