    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gd",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GD Revocation of suspension",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gd"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must revoke the suspension if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the kind of medical device concerned\nwas suspended from the Register no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the kind of device\nfrom the Register.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary must revoke the suspension if the Secretary is\nsatisfied that:\n(a) the ground on which the kind of medical device concerned\nwas suspended from the Register no longer applies; and\n(b) there are no other grounds for suspending the kind of device\nfrom the Register.\n(2) The Secretary’s power to revoke the suspension may be exercised:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
