    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ge",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GE Treating applications for revocation as having been refused",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ge"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for the suspension to be revoked may give the\nSecretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the\napplication as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dd) for the\nSecretary to make a decision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the Secretary has not made a\ndecision.\n(2) The notice may be given at any time before the Secretary makes a\ndecision on the application.\n(3) If a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to revoke the suspension; and\n(b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3)\nconfirming the decision of the Secretary; and\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nSuspension and cancellation from the Register  Part 4-6\nSuspension from the Register  Division 1\nSection 41GF\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which\nnotice was given to the Secretary.\nSubdivision B—Suspension as a result of suspension of\nconformity assessment document",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The applicant for the suspension to be revoked may give the\nSecretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the\napplication as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dd) for the\nSecretary to make a decision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the Secretary has not made a\ndecision.\n(2) The notice may be given at any time before the Secretary makes a\ndecision on the application.\n(3) If a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to revoke the suspension; and\n(b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3)\nconfirming the decision of the Secretary; and\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nSuspension and cancellation from the Register  Part 4-6\nSuspension from the Register  Division 1\nSection 41GF\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which\nnotice was given to the Secretary.\nSubdivision B—Suspension as a result of suspension of\nconformity assessment document",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ge-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ge-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ge-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "49291b0135bc94842bb4bccc4f22e30c1008a87c807d39d32a3846e85a190176"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ge",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GE Treating applications for revocation as having been refused",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The applicant for the suspension to be revoked may give the\nSecretary written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the\napplication as having been refused if:\n(a) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dd) for the\nSecretary to make a decision on the application; and\n(b) at the end of the period, the Secretary has not made a\ndecision.\n(2) The notice may be given at any time before the Secretary makes a\ndecision on the application.\n(3) If a notice has been given, this Act (except for subsection 60(5)) has\neffect as if:\n(a) the Secretary had decided not to revoke the suspension; and\n(b) the Minister had made a decision under subsection 60(3)\nconfirming the decision of the Secretary; and\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nSuspension and cancellation from the Register  Part 4-6\nSuspension from the Register  Division 1\nSection 41GF\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) the Minister’s decision had been made on the day on which\nnotice was given to the Secretary.\nSubdivision B—Suspension as a result of suspension of\nconformity assessment document"
    },
