    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gj",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GJ Powers of cancellation from Register unaffected",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gj"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Subdivision does not affect the Secretary’s powers to cancel\nthe entry of kinds of medical devices from the Register under",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This Subdivision does not affect the Secretary’s powers to cancel\nthe entry of kinds of medical devices from the Register under",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gj-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aeed5f9971e1f789ce2ab41c7f40d24cbb3b5fd59a8eb1636856dc8f89ada54c",
      "skos:note": "Does not affect Secretary's powers to cancel medical device entries from Register"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gj",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GJ Powers of cancellation from Register unaffected",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 99,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This Subdivision does not affect the Secretary’s powers to cancel\nthe entry of kinds of medical devices from the Register under"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gj-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gj"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gk",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GK Automatic cancellation of entries of kinds of medical devices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gk"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.100",
      "values:originalText": "from the Register\n(1) The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in\nrelation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the\nRegister, cancel the entry of the kind of device from the Register\nif:\n(a) the kind of device has been suspended from the Register\nunder section 41GA, and the period applying to the\nsuspension under subsection 41GA(3) or 41GC(3) (as the\ncase requires) expires before the suspension is revoked under\nsection 41GD; or\n(b) a conformity assessment certificate applying to that kind of\ndevice is revoked under Division 4 of Part 4-4.\n(2) The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in\nrelation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the\nRegister, cancel the entry of the kind of device from the Register if\nthe Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—imports into Australia,\nexports from Australia, the manufacture in Australia or\nsupplies in Australia of the kind of device would contravene\none or more of those prohibitions; or\n(b) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—\nimports into Australia, exports from Australia, the\nmanufacture in Australia or supplies in Australia of the kind\nof device would contravene one or more of those conditions.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nSuspension and cancellation from the Register  Part 4-6\nCancellation of entries from the Register  Division 2\nSection 41GL\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "from the Register\n(1) The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in\nrelation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the\nRegister, cancel the entry of the kind of device from the Register\nif:\n(a) the kind of device has been suspended from the Register\nunder section 41GA, and the period applying to the\nsuspension under subsection 41GA(3) or 41GC(3) (as the\ncase requires) expires before the suspension is revoked under\nsection 41GD; or\n(b) a conformity assessment certificate applying to that kind of\ndevice is revoked under Division 4 of Part 4-4.\n(2) The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in\nrelation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the\nRegister, cancel the entry of the kind of device from the Register if\nthe Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—imports into Australia,\nexports from Australia, the manufacture in Australia or\nsupplies in Australia of the kind of device would contravene\none or more of those prohibitions; or\n(b) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—\nimports into Australia, exports from Australia, the\nmanufacture in Australia or supplies in Australia of the kind\nof device would contravene one or more of those conditions.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nSuspension and cancellation from the Register  Part 4-6\nCancellation of entries from the Register  Division 2\nSection 41GL\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gk-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gk-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c6d86f1a6923df492080f306eb2d82402bad8a5777b2a89543a293bddc8a7a85"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GK Automatic cancellation of entries of kinds of medical devices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 100,
      "values:originalText": "from the Register\n(1) The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in\nrelation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the\nRegister, cancel the entry of the kind of device from the Register\nif:\n(a) the kind of device has been suspended from the Register\nunder section 41GA, and the period applying to the\nsuspension under subsection 41GA(3) or 41GC(3) (as the\ncase requires) expires before the suspension is revoked under\nsection 41GD; or\n(b) a conformity assessment certificate applying to that kind of\ndevice is revoked under Division 4 of Part 4-4.\n(2) The Secretary must, by written notice given to the person in\nrelation to whom a kind of medical device is included in the\nRegister, cancel the entry of the kind of device from the Register if\nthe Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) if there are one or more absolute prohibitions in force for the\npurposes of subsection 9K(1) or (3)—imports into Australia,\nexports from Australia, the manufacture in Australia or\nsupplies in Australia of the kind of device would contravene\none or more of those prohibitions; or\n(b) if there are one or more prohibitions in force for the purposes\nof subsection 9K(1) or (3) that are subject to conditions—\nimports into Australia, exports from Australia, the\nmanufacture in Australia or supplies in Australia of the kind\nof device would contravene one or more of those conditions.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nSuspension and cancellation from the Register  Part 4-6\nCancellation of entries from the Register  Division 2\nSection 41GL\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
