      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Minister may exempt certain medical devices",
      "cml:conclusionText": "from various provisions of this Chapter"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gr-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Interval",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Conditional commencement of exemptions",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Minister may exempt certain medical devices from various provisions of this Chapter so that the devices may be stockpiled to deal with possible future emergencies or made available urgently to deal with actual emergencies.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Note 1:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gr-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurring Trace",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recurring trace of exemptions under Part 41GR",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Minister may exempt certain medical devices from various provisions of this Chapter so that the devices may be stockpiled to deal with possible future emergencies or made available urgently to deal with actual emergencies.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Note 2:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gr-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide information about exemptions under Part 41GR",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Some of the other provisions of this Act about medical devices exempt under this Part are:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(a) section 41JCA (providing information to the Secretary); and (b) section 41KA (public notification and recall of medical devices);"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gr-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to provide information about exemptions under Part 41GR",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Some of the other provisions of this Act about medical devices exempt under this Part are:",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(c) section 46A (search of premises)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gs",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GS Minister may make exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gs"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.108",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister may, by writing, exempt specified kinds of medical\ndevices from the operation of the following:\n(a) Division 1 of Part 4-2 (essential principles);\n(b) Division 1 of Part 4-3 (conformity assessment procedures);\n(c) Part 4-4 (conformity assessment certificates);\n(d) Part 4-5 (including medical devices in the Register).\n(1A) The Minister may exempt devices under subsection (1) only if the\nMinister is satisfied of the matter in subsection (2) or (2A).\n(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest, the\nexemption should be made so that:\n(a) the devices may be stockpiled as quickly as possible in order\nto create a preparedness to deal with a potential threat to\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GS\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\npublic health that may be caused by a possible future\nemergency; or\n(b) the devices can be made available urgently in Australia in\norder to deal with an actual threat to public health caused by\nan emergency that has occurred.\n(2A) The matter in this subsection is that:\n(a) a national emergency declaration is in force; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the exemption should be made so that the devices may\nbe stockpiled to deal with a potential threat to public\nhealth that may be caused by the emergency to which\nthe national emergency declaration relates;\n(ii) the exemption should be made so that the devices can be\nmade available urgently in Australia in order to deal\nwith an actual threat to public health caused by the\nemergency to which the national emergency declaration\nrelates; and\n(c) the Minister is satisfied that the exemption is in the national\ninterest.\nPeriod of exemption\n(3) An exemption under subsection (1) comes into force:\n(a) on the day the exemption is made; or\n(b) on a later day specified in the exemption.\n(4) An exemption under subsection (1) remains in force for the period\nspecified in the exemption, unless revoked earlier.\nNote:\nSection 41GU deals with variation and revocation of the exemption.\nEffect of inclusion of kind of medical device in the Register\n(5) An exemption under subsection (1) ceases to have effect in relation\nto a particular kind of medical device when that kind of medical\ndevice becomes included in the Register under Part 4-5.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister may, by writing, exempt specified kinds of medical\ndevices from the operation of the following:\n(a) Division 1 of Part 4-2 (essential principles);\n(b) Division 1 of Part 4-3 (conformity assessment procedures);\n(c) Part 4-4 (conformity assessment certificates);\n(d) Part 4-5 (including medical devices in the Register).\n(1A) The Minister may exempt devices under subsection (1) only if the\nMinister is satisfied of the matter in subsection (2) or (2A).\n(2) The matter in this subsection is that in the national interest, the\nexemption should be made so that:\n(a) the devices may be stockpiled as quickly as possible in order\nto create a preparedness to deal with a potential threat to\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GS\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\npublic health that may be caused by a possible future\nemergency; or\n(b) the devices can be made available urgently in Australia in\norder to deal with an actual threat to public health caused by\nan emergency that has occurred.\n(2A) The matter in this subsection is that:\n(a) a national emergency declaration is in force; and\n(b) either of the following apply:\n(i) the exemption should be made so that the devices may\nbe stockpiled to deal with a potential threat to public\nhealth that may be caused by the emergency to which\nthe national emergency declaration relates;\n(ii) the exemption should be made so that the devices can be\nmade available urgently in Australia in order to deal\nwith an actual threat to public health caused by the\nemergency to which the national emergency declaration\nrelates; and\n(c) the Minister is satisfied that the exemption is in the national\ninterest.\nPeriod of exemption\n(3) An exemption under subsection (1) comes into force:\n(a) on the day the exemption is made; or\n(b) on a later day specified in the exemption.\n(4) An exemption under subsection (1) remains in force for the period\nspecified in the exempti",
      "cml:hasPart": [
