    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gt",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GT Conditions of exemptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gt"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.110",
      "values:originalText": "An exemption under section 41GS is subject to conditions\nspecified in the exemption about any of the following:\n(a) the quantity of medical devices that are exempt;\n(b) the source of those medical devices;\n(c) the persons or class of persons who may import,\nmanufacture, supply or export those medical devices;\n(d) the supply of those medical devices (including the persons or\nclass of persons to whom medical devices may be supplied\nfor use and the circumstances under which a stockpile of\nmedical devices may be supplied for use);\n(e) the storage and security of those medical devices;\n(ea) compliance with the requirements referred to in\nsubsection 41CA(3) (about unique device identifiers of\nmedical devices);\n(f) the keeping and disclosure of, and access to, records about\nthose medical devices;\n(g) the disposal of those medical devices;\n(h) the manner in which any of those medical devices are to be\ndealt with if a condition of the exemption is breached;\n(i) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\nWhether or not medical devices are exempt under section 41GS is\nnot affected by whether or not there is a breach of a condition\nunder this section in relation to those medical devices.\nNote 1:\nThere are offences and civil penalty provisions related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see Division 3A of Part 4-11.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GU\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 2:\nSection 41GU deals with variation and revocation of the conditions.",
      "skos:definition": "An exemption under section 41GS is subject to conditions\nspecified in the exemption about any of the following:\n(a) the quantity of medical devices that are exempt;\n(b) the source of those medical devices;\n(c) the persons or class of persons who may import,\nmanufacture, supply or export those medical devices;\n(d) the supply of those medical devices (including the persons or\nclass of persons to whom medical devices may be supplied\nfor use and the circumstances under which a stockpile of\nmedical devices may be supplied for use);\n(e) the storage and security of those medical devices;\n(ea) compliance with the requirements referred to in\nsubsection 41CA(3) (about unique device identifiers of\nmedical devices);\n(f) the keeping and disclosure of, and access to, records about\nthose medical devices;\n(g) the disposal of those medical devices;\n(h) the manner in which any of those medical devices are to be\ndealt with if a condition of the exemption is breached;\n(i) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\nWhether or not medical devices are exempt under section 41GS is\nnot affected by whether or not there is a breach of a condition\nunder this section in relation to those medical devices.\nNote 1:\nThere are offences and civil penalty provisions related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see Division 3A of Part 4-11.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GU\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 2:\nSection 41GU deals with variation and revocation of the conditions.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gt-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gt-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gt-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a2f20c9a6d16e2b346d4805fcfebca92fa2232f36749b6566b2334812bd7ff46",
      "skos:note": "Conditions for exemptions under section 41GS"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gt",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GT Conditions of exemptions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 110,
      "values:originalText": "An exemption under section 41GS is subject to conditions\nspecified in the exemption about any of the following:\n(a) the quantity of medical devices that are exempt;\n(b) the source of those medical devices;\n(c) the persons or class of persons who may import,\nmanufacture, supply or export those medical devices;\n(d) the supply of those medical devices (including the persons or\nclass of persons to whom medical devices may be supplied\nfor use and the circumstances under which a stockpile of\nmedical devices may be supplied for use);\n(e) the storage and security of those medical devices;\n(ea) compliance with the requirements referred to in\nsubsection 41CA(3) (about unique device identifiers of\nmedical devices);\n(f) the keeping and disclosure of, and access to, records about\nthose medical devices;\n(g) the disposal of those medical devices;\n(h) the manner in which any of those medical devices are to be\ndealt with if a condition of the exemption is breached;\n(i) any other matters that the Minister thinks appropriate.\nWhether or not medical devices are exempt under section 41GS is\nnot affected by whether or not there is a breach of a condition\nunder this section in relation to those medical devices.\nNote 1:\nThere are offences and civil penalty provisions related to the breach of\na condition of an exemption: see Division 3A of Part 4-11.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GU\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 2:\nSection 41GU deals with variation and revocation of the conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gt-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
