    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GU(4) Variation or revocation of exemption",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gu-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.111",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect:\n(a) if the Minister states in the variation or revocation that the\nvariation or revocation is necessary to prevent imminent risk\nof death, serious illness or serious injury—on the day the\nvariation or revocation is made; or\n(b) in any other case—on a later day specified in the variation or\nrevocation (which must not be earlier than 28 days after the\nday the variation or revocation is made).\n41GV  Informing persons of exemption etc.\nIf the Minister makes an exemption under section 41GS, the\nMinister must take reasonable steps to give a copy of the following\nto each person covered by paragraph 41GT(c):\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect:\n(a) if the Minister states in the variation or revocation that the\nvariation or revocation is necessary to prevent imminent risk\nof death, serious illness or serious injury—on the day the\nvariation or revocation is made; or\n(b) in any other case—on a later day specified in the variation or\nrevocation (which must not be earlier than 28 days after the\nday the variation or revocation is made).\n41GV  Informing persons of exemption etc.\nIf the Minister makes an exemption under section 41GS, the\nMinister must take reasonable steps to give a copy of the following\nto each person covered by paragraph 41GT(c):\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1969042fd28a9628f08eeb75ecf16b167d072c97140d3f56f5c1f8cc0a551a3e",
      "skos:note": "Variation or revocation of exemption takes effect under specified conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gu-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GU(4) Variation or revocation of exemption",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 111,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect:\n(a) if the Minister states in the variation or revocation that the\nvariation or revocation is necessary to prevent imminent risk\nof death, serious illness or serious injury—on the day the\nvariation or revocation is made; or\n(b) in any other case—on a later day specified in the variation or\nrevocation (which must not be earlier than 28 days after the\nday the variation or revocation is made).\n41GV  Informing persons of exemption etc.\nIf the Minister makes an exemption under section 41GS, the\nMinister must take reasonable steps to give a copy of the following\nto each person covered by paragraph 41GT(c):\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "necessity",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Necessity condition for variation or revocation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect:\n(a) if the Minister states in the variation or revocation that the\nvariation or revocation is necessary to prevent imminent risk\nof death, serious illness or serious injury—on the day the\nvariation or revocation is made;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The variation or revocation must be necessary to prevent imminent risk of death, serious illness or serious injury."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gu-ss-4-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "possibility",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Possibility condition for variation or revocation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) A variation or revocation under this section takes effect:\n(b) in any other case—on a later day specified in the variation or\nrevocation (which must not be earlier than 28 days after the\nday the variation or revocation is made).",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The variation or revocation may occur on a later day."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GW Notification and tabling",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gw"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "Notification\n(1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day\non which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However,\nthe exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely\nbecause of a failure to comply with this subsection.\nTabling\n(2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days\nof that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply\nwith this subsection.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GY\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "Notification\n(1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day\non which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However,\nthe exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely\nbecause of a failure to comply with this subsection.\nTabling\n(2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days\nof that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply\nwith this subsection.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GY\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7d31b83313991d4c969b95ff28385ff891514dbe7a93c93c5db8145ad031420f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gw",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GW Notification and tabling",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "Notification\n(1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day\non which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However,\nthe exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely\nbecause of a failure to comply with this subsection.\nTabling\n(2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days\nof that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply\nwith this subsection.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GY\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GW(1) Notification and tabling",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gw-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day\non which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However,\nthe exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely\nbecause of a failure to comply with this subsection.\nTabling",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day\non which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However,\nthe exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely\nbecause of a failure to comply with this subsection.\nTabling",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-1-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "29f9f12af4236a1244485a3ed5640c3b83ac59254f7fd0961b4ce4f336a461fe",
      "skos:note": "Publish notice in Gazette within 5 working days after exemption, variation or revocation is made.",
      "dc:description": "Notice setting out particulars of exemption, variation or revocation"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gw-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GW(1) Notification and tabling",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must cause a notice setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be published in the Gazette within 5 working days after the day\non which the exemption, variation or revocation is made. However,\nthe exemption, variation or revocation is not invalid merely\nbecause of a failure to comply with this subsection.\nTabling"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-1-norm",
