    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GW(2) Notification and tabling",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gw-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.112",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days\nof that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply\nwith this subsection.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GY\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days\nof that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply\nwith this subsection.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GY\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gw-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b0cfa78d6c799a7c3a5e90b8595a9a77e89a701a27ef546659861844729cc045",
      "skos:note": "Minister must table document within 5 sitting days of exemption, variation or revocation made."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gw-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GW(2) Notification and tabling",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 112,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Minister must cause a document setting out particulars of the\nfollowing:\n(a) an exemption made under section 41GS because of\nparagraph 41GS(2)(b) or subparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\n(b) a variation or revocation under section 41GU, to the extent\nthat the variation or revocation relates to an exemption made\nunder section 41GS because of paragraph 41GS(2)(b) or\nsubparagraph (2A)(b)(ii);\nto be tabled in each House of the Parliament within 5 sitting days\nof that House after the day on which the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is made. However, the exemption, variation or\nrevocation is not invalid merely because of a failure to comply\nwith this subsection.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nExempting medical devices to deal with emergencies  Part 4-6A\n\nSection 41GY\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
