    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41GY Disposal of unused medical devices",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.113",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a medical device if:\n(a) an exemption under section 41GS in relation to that kind of\nmedical device ceases to have effect otherwise than because\nthat kind of medical device becomes included in the Register\nunder Part 4-5; and\n(b) the medical device has not been used before the exemption so\nceases to have effect.\n(2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of the medical device\nin accordance with the regulations.\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out\nthe methods by which the medical device is to be stored, supplied,\ndestroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of.\n(4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not\nenable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including\nthe Commonwealth) other than the owner of the medical device.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies to a medical device if:\n(a) an exemption under section 41GS in relation to that kind of\nmedical device ceases to have effect otherwise than because\nthat kind of medical device becomes included in the Register\nunder Part 4-5; and\n(b) the medical device has not been used before the exemption so\nceases to have effect.\n(2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of the medical device\nin accordance with the regulations.\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out\nthe methods by which the medical device is to be stored, supplied,\ndestroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of.\n(4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not\nenable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including\nthe Commonwealth) other than the owner of the medical device.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gy-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gy-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gy-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41gy-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "44fd65c308b3327cf3b12513f6f701cf105f61f02f3736de667f5816e9a2c60a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41gy",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41GY Disposal of unused medical devices",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 113,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies to a medical device if:\n(a) an exemption under section 41GS in relation to that kind of\nmedical device ceases to have effect otherwise than because\nthat kind of medical device becomes included in the Register\nunder Part 4-5; and\n(b) the medical device has not been used before the exemption so\nceases to have effect.\n(2) The Secretary may arrange for the disposal of the medical device\nin accordance with the regulations.\n(3) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (2) may set out\nthe methods by which the medical device is to be stored, supplied,\ndestroyed, exported or otherwise disposed of.\n(4) A method set out in the regulations under subsection (3) must not\nenable or permit any benefit to be conferred on a person (including\nthe Commonwealth) other than the owner of the medical device.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
