    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41H What this Part is about",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.114",
      "values:originalText": "In addition to Part 4-6A, there are 4 other kinds of exemptions\nfrom the prohibitions in Division 3 of Part 4-11 on dealing in\nmedical devices that are not included in the Register:\n(a)\nmedical devices exempted under the regulations;\n(b)\napproval for medical devices to be used for special\ntreatment of individuals or for experimental purposes;\n(c)\nauthorisation of health practitioners to supply specified\nmedical devices;\n(d)\nmedical devices exempted if substitutes are unavailable\nor in short supply or may, in the reasonably foreseeable\nfuture, become unavailable or be in short supply.",
      "skos:definition": "In addition to Part 4-6A, there are 4 other kinds of exemptions\nfrom the prohibitions in Division 3 of Part 4-11 on dealing in\nmedical devices that are not included in the Register:\n(a)\nmedical devices exempted under the regulations;\n(b)\napproval for medical devices to be used for special\ntreatment of individuals or for experimental purposes;\n(c)\nauthorisation of health practitioners to supply specified\nmedical devices;\n(d)\nmedical devices exempted if substitutes are unavailable\nor in short supply or may, in the reasonably foreseeable\nfuture, become unavailable or be in short supply.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41h-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d0b9f3fba29013895845d7e6c428848ca9b2b43ce8d240438dc86a9e56a72764",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from prohibitions on dealing in medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41H What this Part is about",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 114,
      "values:originalText": "In addition to Part 4-6A, there are 4 other kinds of exemptions\nfrom the prohibitions in Division 3 of Part 4-11 on dealing in\nmedical devices that are not included in the Register:\n(a)\nmedical devices exempted under the regulations;\n(b)\napproval for medical devices to be used for special\ntreatment of individuals or for experimental purposes;\n(c)\nauthorisation of health practitioners to supply specified\nmedical devices;\n(d)\nmedical devices exempted if substitutes are unavailable\nor in short supply or may, in the reasonably foreseeable\nfuture, become unavailable or be in short supply."
    },
