    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41HC(4) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41hc-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given:\n(a) to a medical practitioner included in a class of medical\npractitioners prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of\nthis paragraph; and\n(b) to a medical practitioner who has the approval of an ethics\ncommittee to supply the specified kinds of medical devices\nor the specified class of such devices; and\n(c) in relation to a class or classes of recipients prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph.\nHowever, the regulations may prescribe circumstances in which\nparagraph (b) does not apply.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given:\n(a) to a medical practitioner included in a class of medical\npractitioners prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of\nthis paragraph; and\n(b) to a medical practitioner who has the approval of an ethics\ncommittee to supply the specified kinds of medical devices\nor the specified class of such devices; and\n(c) in relation to a class or classes of recipients prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph.\nHowever, the regulations may prescribe circumstances in which\nparagraph (b) does not apply.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1408ad811ceeab1bae29cde67bccf0e6c49ecbe1c04509f16f4c44064f33fc1",
      "skos:note": "Authority for health practitioners may only be given under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41hc-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41HC(4) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "(4) An authority under subsection (1) may only be given:\n(a) to a medical practitioner included in a class of medical\npractitioners prescribed by the regulations for the purposes of\nthis paragraph; and\n(b) to a medical practitioner who has the approval of an ethics\ncommittee to supply the specified kinds of medical devices\nor the specified class of such devices; and\n(c) in relation to a class or classes of recipients prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph.\nHowever, the regulations may prescribe circumstances in which\nparagraph (b) does not apply."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-4-norm",
