    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41HC(6) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41hc-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.118",
      "values:originalText": "(6) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nauthorising any health practitioner who is included in a specified\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOther exemptions from including medical devices in the Register  Part 4-7\n\nSection 41HC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nclass of health practitioners to supply a specified kind of medical\ndevice, for use in the treatment of humans, to the class or classes of\nrecipients specified in those rules, so long as:\n(a) that kind of medical device is supplied in the circumstances\nspecified in those rules; and\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in those rules are satisfied.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nauthorising any health practitioner who is included in a specified\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOther exemptions from including medical devices in the Register  Part 4-7\n\nSection 41HC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nclass of health practitioners to supply a specified kind of medical\ndevice, for use in the treatment of humans, to the class or classes of\nrecipients specified in those rules, so long as:\n(a) that kind of medical device is supplied in the circumstances\nspecified in those rules; and\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in those rules are satisfied.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41hc-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a016e316ef1eef411c484cd78dd143922d11ef471445b79d7be7a588475fd4b8",
      "skos:note": "The Minister may make rules authorising health practitioners to supply medical devices."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41hc-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41HC(6) Authorities for health practitioners",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 118,
      "values:originalText": "(6) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, make rules\nauthorising any health practitioner who is included in a specified\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOther exemptions from including medical devices in the Register  Part 4-7\n\nSection 41HC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nclass of health practitioners to supply a specified kind of medical\ndevice, for use in the treatment of humans, to the class or classes of\nrecipients specified in those rules, so long as:\n(a) that kind of medical device is supplied in the circumstances\nspecified in those rules; and\n(b) the conditions (if any) specified in those rules are satisfied."
    },
