    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41JB Complying with the Secretary’s requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41jb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.129",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The person must give the information or documents to the\nSecretary:\n(a) within such reasonable time, being not less than 10 working\ndays from the day on which the notice is given, as is\nspecified in the notice; and\n(b) in such form as is specified in the notice.\n(2) The form may require or permit information to be given in\naccordance with specified software requirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.\nOffence for failing to comply with a notice\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 41JA; and\n(aa) the person is covered by paragraph 41JA(1)(b), (ba), (d) or\n(da) or subsection 41JA(1E); and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty: 500 penalty units.\nNote:\nFailure to comply with the notice might also lead to suspension or\nrevocation of a conformity assessment certificate (see Divisions 3 and\n4 of Part 4-4) or suspension or cancellation of the entry of a kind of\nmedical device in the Register (see Part 4-6).\n(3A) Subsection (3) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3A): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The person must give the information or documents to the\nSecretary:\n(a) within such reasonable time, being not less than 10 working\ndays from the day on which the notice is given, as is\nspecified in the notice; and\n(b) in such form as is specified in the notice.\n(2) The form may require or permit information to be given in\naccordance with specified software requirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.\nOffence for failing to comply with a notice\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 41JA; and\n(aa) the person is covered by paragraph 41JA(1)(b), (ba), (d) or\n(da) or subsection 41JA(1E); and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty: 500 penalty units.\nNote:\nFailure to comply with the notice might also lead to suspension or\nrevocation of a conformity assessment certificate (see Divisions 3 and\n4 of Part 4-4) or suspension or cancellation of the entry of a kind of\nmedical device in the Register (see Part 4-6).\n(3A) Subsection (3) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3A): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jb-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41jb-ss-3a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7c5dcd77fedc7193a5a240a7c8f623071e6a2acd6d3527f322b7be284ba26017"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41jb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41JB Complying with the Secretary’s requirements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 129,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The person must give the information or documents to the\nSecretary:\n(a) within such reasonable time, being not less than 10 working\ndays from the day on which the notice is given, as is\nspecified in the notice; and\n(b) in such form as is specified in the notice.\n(2) The form may require or permit information to be given in\naccordance with specified software requirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.\nOffence for failing to comply with a notice\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 41JA; and\n(aa) the person is covered by paragraph 41JA(1)(b), (ba), (d) or\n(da) or subsection 41JA(1E); and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the notice.\nPenalty: 500 penalty units.\nNote:\nFailure to comply with the notice might also lead to suspension or\nrevocation of a conformity assessment certificate (see Divisions 3 and\n4 of Part 4-4) or suspension or cancellation of the entry of a kind of\nmedical device in the Register (see Part 4-6).\n(3A) Subsection (3) does not apply if the person has a reasonable\nexcuse.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (3A): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
