    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41kc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41KC Criminal offences for failing to comply with requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41kc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "relating to a kind of medical device\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "relating to a kind of medical device\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41kc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41kc-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "cc623b1a646f0826f5bc60985ff3799fc4259d93357a40f0168ac3e2e9348317"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41kc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41KC Criminal offences for failing to comply with requirements",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 149,
      "values:originalText": "relating to a kind of medical device\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41kc-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41KC(1) Criminal offences for failing to comply with requirements",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41kc-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.149",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person does an act or omits to do an act; and\n(b) the act or omission breaches a requirement imposed on the\nperson under section 41KA; and\n(c) the act or omission has resulted in, will result in, or is likely\nto result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41kc"
      },
