    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41lc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41LC Payment of assessment fee by instalments",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41lc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may provide for the payment of an assessment fee\nto be made by such instalments and at such times as are ascertained\nin accordance with the regulations, and the assessment fee is due\nand payable accordingly.\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may provide\nthat a person is not allowed to pay an assessment fee by instalments\nif any part of an instalment of:\n(a) that or any other assessment fee payable by the person; or\n(b) any evaluation fee under section 24 payable by the person;\nwas unpaid immediately after the time when it became due for\npayment.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may provide for the payment of an assessment fee\nto be made by such instalments and at such times as are ascertained\nin accordance with the regulations, and the assessment fee is due\nand payable accordingly.\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may provide\nthat a person is not allowed to pay an assessment fee by instalments\nif any part of an instalment of:\n(a) that or any other assessment fee payable by the person; or\n(b) any evaluation fee under section 24 payable by the person;\nwas unpaid immediately after the time when it became due for\npayment.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection (1).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41lc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41lc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41lc-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "aef933d8b59ce22e3178bc6120c54a052c95f4a1829e3c99a2588b6ded05f171"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41lc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41LC Payment of assessment fee by instalments",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may provide for the payment of an assessment fee\nto be made by such instalments and at such times as are ascertained\nin accordance with the regulations, and the assessment fee is due\nand payable accordingly.\n(2) Regulations made for the purposes of subsection (1) may provide\nthat a person is not allowed to pay an assessment fee by instalments\nif any part of an instalment of:\n(a) that or any other assessment fee payable by the person; or\n(b) any evaluation fee under section 24 payable by the person;\nwas unpaid immediately after the time when it became due for\npayment.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit the generality of subsection (1)."
    },
