    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ld",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41LD Recovery of assessment fee",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ld"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.152",
      "values:originalText": "An assessment fee may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a\ndebt due to the Commonwealth.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nAssessment fees  Part 4-10\n\nSection 41LE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "An assessment fee may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a\ndebt due to the Commonwealth.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nAssessment fees  Part 4-10\n\nSection 41LE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ld-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ld-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "245abdc32c690758fc507b40452950dd9c5ba5ab1f90188f789f215920ed0229",
      "skos:note": "Recovery of assessment fee"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41ld",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41LD Recovery of assessment fee",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 152,
      "values:originalText": "An assessment fee may be recovered by the Commonwealth as a\ndebt due to the Commonwealth.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nAssessment fees  Part 4-10\n\nSection 41LE\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ld-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ld"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ld-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "can",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Can recover assessment fee",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41le",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41LE Reduction of conformity assessment fee where decision not",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41le"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.153",
      "values:originalText": "made within prescribed period\n(1) Nothing in section 41LA, 41LB or 41LC requires the applicant to\npay more than 3/4 of the conformity assessment fee before the\nmaking of the decision if:\n(a) the application is for the issuing of a conformity assessment\ncertificate under Part 4-4; and\n(b) consideration of the application will involve an examination\nof the design of medical devices; and\n(c) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application.\n(2) If the decision is not made within that period, the conformity\nassessment fee is 3/4 of the fee that, apart from this subsection,\nwould have been the conformity assessment fee.\n(3) If:\n(a) the decision is made within that period; and\n(b) part of the conformity assessment fee under section 41LA is,\nbecause of subsection (1) of this section, unpaid when the\ndecision is made;\nthat part becomes due and payable on the making of the decision.\n(4) For the purposes of this section, a decision is taken to be made on\nthe application when the applicant is notified under\nsubsection 41EE(1) of the Secretary’s decision on the application.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "made within prescribed period\n(1) Nothing in section 41LA, 41LB or 41LC requires the applicant to\npay more than 3/4 of the conformity assessment fee before the\nmaking of the decision if:\n(a) the application is for the issuing of a conformity assessment\ncertificate under Part 4-4; and\n(b) consideration of the application will involve an examination\nof the design of medical devices; and\n(c) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application.\n(2) If the decision is not made within that period, the conformity\nassessment fee is 3/4 of the fee that, apart from this subsection,\nwould have been the conformity assessment fee.\n(3) If:\n(a) the decision is made within that period; and\n(b) part of the conformity assessment fee under section 41LA is,\nbecause of subsection (1) of this section, unpaid when the\ndecision is made;\nthat part becomes due and payable on the making of the decision.\n(4) For the purposes of this section, a decision is taken to be made on\nthe application when the applicant is notified under\nsubsection 41EE(1) of the Secretary’s decision on the application.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41le-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41le-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41le-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41le-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "18180237252b64227757cffba307f718493f8d4ff089c0d677057d0a142b99c8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41le",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41LE Reduction of conformity assessment fee where decision not",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 153,
      "values:originalText": "made within prescribed period\n(1) Nothing in section 41LA, 41LB or 41LC requires the applicant to\npay more than 3/4 of the conformity assessment fee before the\nmaking of the decision if:\n(a) the application is for the issuing of a conformity assessment\ncertificate under Part 4-4; and\n(b) consideration of the application will involve an examination\nof the design of medical devices; and\n(c) a period is prescribed under paragraph 63(2)(dc) for making a\ndecision on the application.\n(2) If the decision is not made within that period, the conformity\nassessment fee is 3/4 of the fee that, apart from this subsection,\nwould have been the conformity assessment fee.\n(3) If:\n(a) the decision is made within that period; and\n(b) part of the conformity assessment fee under section 41LA is,\nbecause of subsection (1) of this section, unpaid when the\ndecision is made;\nthat part becomes due and payable on the making of the decision.\n(4) For the purposes of this section, a decision is taken to be made on\nthe application when the applicant is notified under\nsubsection 41EE(1) of the Secretary’s decision on the application.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
