    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MB Exceptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 41MA and 41MAA do not apply if:\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nNon-compliance with essential principles  Division 1\nSection 41MC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential\nprinciples only in respect of a part or parts of the essential\nprinciples to which that medical device standard, or one or\nmore of those medical device standards, relate.\nNote:\nMedical device standards are determined under Division 2 of Part 4-2.\n(2) For the purposes of this section, a medical device standard relates\nto a part or parts of the essential principles only if the standard\nspecifies that part or parts.\nNote 1:\nIn the prosecution for an offence, the defendant bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matters in this section (see subsection 13.3(3)\nof the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nIn proceedings for the contravention of a civil penalty provision, the\ndefendant must prove the matters in this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 41MA and 41MAA do not apply if:\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nNon-compliance with essential principles  Division 1\nSection 41MC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential\nprinciples only in respect of a part or parts of the essential\nprinciples to which that medical device standard, or one or\nmore of those medical device standards, relate.\nNote:\nMedical device standards are determined under Division 2 of Part 4-2.\n(2) For the purposes of this section, a medical device standard relates\nto a part or parts of the essential principles only if the standard\nspecifies that part or parts.\nNote 1:\nIn the prosecution for an offence, the defendant bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matters in this section (see subsection 13.3(3)\nof the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nIn proceedings for the contravention of a civil penalty provision, the\ndefendant must prove the matters in this section.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4a22dd5d9f0ad4a2ca149f53d414411fe8a832d8f9678d59326350072eed36a3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MB Exceptions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 41MA and 41MAA do not apply if:\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nNon-compliance with essential principles  Division 1\nSection 41MC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential\nprinciples only in respect of a part or parts of the essential\nprinciples to which that medical device standard, or one or\nmore of those medical device standards, relate.\nNote:\nMedical device standards are determined under Division 2 of Part 4-2.\n(2) For the purposes of this section, a medical device standard relates\nto a part or parts of the essential principles only if the standard\nspecifies that part or parts.\nNote 1:\nIn the prosecution for an offence, the defendant bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matters in this section (see subsection 13.3(3)\nof the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nIn proceedings for the contravention of a civil penalty provision, the\ndefendant must prove the matters in this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MB(1) Exceptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mb-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 41MA and 41MAA do not apply if:\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nNon-compliance with essential principles  Division 1\nSection 41MC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential\nprinciples only in respect of a part or parts of the essential\nprinciples to which that medical device standard, or one or\nmore of those medical device standards, relate.\nNote:\nMedical device standards are determined under Division 2 of Part 4-2.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Sections 41MA and 41MAA do not apply if:\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nNon-compliance with essential principles  Division 1\nSection 41MC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential\nprinciples only in respect of a part or parts of the essential\nprinciples to which that medical device standard, or one or\nmore of those medical device standards, relate.\nNote:\nMedical device standards are determined under Division 2 of Part 4-2.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-ltl-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "53d099984c456943da4fcf632a44a1b0ca0c270c02bb388206c4cfad9f17ef0d",
      "skos:note": "Exceptions for medical devices that comply with standards and fail to comply only in respect of specific principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mb-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MB(1) Exceptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Sections 41MA and 41MAA do not apply if:\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nNon-compliance with essential principles  Division 1\nSection 41MC\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device\nstandards that apply to it; and\n(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential\nprinciples only in respect of a part or parts of the essential\nprinciples to which that medical device standard, or one or\nmore of those medical device standards, relate.\nNote:\nMedical device standards are determined under Division 2 of Part 4-2."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "<",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the temporal interval for which the exemption applies.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device standards that apply to it;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exemption is valid only if the medical device meets the specified standard."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-ltl-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "<",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Specifies the temporal relationship between the exemption and the non-compliance.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential principles only in respect of a part or parts of the essential principles.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exemption is valid only if the non-compliance occurs within the specified interval."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-deontic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the type of duty or obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the medical device complies with one or more medical device standards that apply to it;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exemption is a permission for the medical device to comply with specific standards."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-1-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Classifies the type of duty or obligation.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the medical device fails to comply with the essential principles only in respect of a part or parts of the essential principles.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The exemption is a permission for the medical device to fail to comply with specific principles."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MB(2) Exceptions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mb-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.160",
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of this section, a medical device standard relates\nto a part or parts of the essential principles only if the standard\nspecifies that part or parts.\nNote 1:\nIn the prosecution for an offence, the defendant bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matters in this section (see subsection 13.3(3)\nof the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nIn proceedings for the contravention of a civil penalty provision, the\ndefendant must prove the matters in this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) For the purposes of this section, a medical device standard relates\nto a part or parts of the essential principles only if the standard\nspecifies that part or parts.\nNote 1:\nIn the prosecution for an offence, the defendant bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matters in this section (see subsection 13.3(3)\nof the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nIn proceedings for the contravention of a civil penalty provision, the\ndefendant must prove the matters in this section.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-2-logic-epistemic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "38d7f895eb2dd8fdde51a1820a8fd3c17de21946e14365cf3ff2375a2b60b9e3",
      "skos:note": "Defendant bears evidential burden in prosecution for offence.",
      "dc:description": "Evidence of matters in section 13.3(3) of Criminal Code."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mb-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MB(2) Exceptions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 160,
      "values:originalText": "(2) For the purposes of this section, a medical device standard relates\nto a part or parts of the essential principles only if the standard\nspecifies that part or parts.\nNote 1:\nIn the prosecution for an offence, the defendant bears an evidential\nburden in relation to the matters in this section (see subsection 13.3(3)\nof the Criminal Code).\nNote 2:\nIn proceedings for the contravention of a civil penalty provision, the\ndefendant must prove the matters in this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mb-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
