    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mh",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MH Criminal offence for making false statements in declarations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mh"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.170",
      "values:originalText": "A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a\ndeclaration, relating to the application of conformity\nassessment procedures, or the application of requirements\ncomparable to those procedures, to a medical device that the\nperson has manufactured; and\n(b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nFailure to apply conformity assessment procedures  Division 2\nSection 41MHA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n41MHA  Civil penalty for making false statements in declarations\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person manufactures a medical device; and\n(b) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a\ndeclaration relating to the application of conformity\nassessment procedures, or the application of requirements\ncomparable to those procedures, to the device; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a\ndeclaration, relating to the application of conformity\nassessment procedures, or the application of requirements\ncomparable to those procedures, to a medical device that the\nperson has manufactured; and\n(b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nFailure to apply conformity assessment procedures  Division 2\nSection 41MHA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n41MHA  Civil penalty for making false statements in declarations\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person manufactures a medical device; and\n(b) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a\ndeclaration relating to the application of conformity\nassessment procedures, or the application of requirements\ncomparable to those procedures, to the device; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mh-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mh-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1a64bffa7442bdd9fc7ed83bf732c2ce641760dac5eef034050dbfe9a9944505",
      "skos:note": "Making false statements in declarations is a criminal offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mh",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MH Criminal offence for making false statements in declarations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 170,
      "values:originalText": "A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a\ndeclaration, relating to the application of conformity\nassessment procedures, or the application of requirements\ncomparable to those procedures, to a medical device that the\nperson has manufactured; and\n(b) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nFailure to apply conformity assessment procedures  Division 2\nSection 41MHA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n41MHA  Civil penalty for making false statements in declarations\nA person contravenes this section if:\n(a) the person manufactures a medical device; and\n(b) the person makes a statement in or in connection with a\ndeclaration relating to the application of conformity\nassessment procedures, or the application of requirements\ncomparable to those procedures, to the device; and\n(c) the statement is false or misleading in a material particular.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—3,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—30,000 penalty units.\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mh-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mh"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
