    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mi",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MI Criminal offences for importing, exporting, supplying or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mi"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.172",
      "values:originalText": "manufacturing a medical device not included in the\nRegister\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register in\nrelation to the person;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the device has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the device, if the device were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nMedical devices not included in the Register and related matters  Division 3\nSection 41MI\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register in\nrelation to the person;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "manufacturing a medical device not included in the\nRegister\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register in\nrelation to the person;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the device has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the device, if the device were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nMedical devices not included in the Register and related matters  Division 3\nSection 41MI\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind ",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mi-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mi-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mi-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "efc501e51c71d5c391eaad0b7e591236ce7c9f03219fecedfd7da26eeed3c237"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mi",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MI Criminal offences for importing, exporting, supplying or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 172,
      "values:originalText": "manufacturing a medical device not included in the\nRegister\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register in\nrelation to the person;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the device has resulted in, will result in, or is\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the device, if the device were used, would\nresult in, or would be likely to result in, harm or injury\nto any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nMedical devices not included in the Register and related matters  Division 3\nSection 41MI\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nNote 1:\nA jury may acquit a person of an offence against this subsection and\nmay convict the person of an offence against subsection (4) instead:\nsee section 53A.\nNote 2:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register in\nrelation to the person;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(5) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) imports a medical device into Australia; or\n(ii) exports a medical device from Australia; or\n(iii) supplies a medical device in Australia; or\n(iv) manufactures a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mi-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MI(1) Criminal offences for importing, exporting, supplying or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
