        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.178",
      "values:originalText": "Register\nA person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person supplies a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson; and\n(c) the person to whom the device is supplied is not the ultimate\nconsumer of the device.\nPenalty: 120 penalty units.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nMedical devices not included in the Register and related matters  Division 3\nSection 41ML\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "Register\nA person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person supplies a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson; and\n(c) the person to whom the device is supplied is not the ultimate\nconsumer of the device.\nPenalty: 120 penalty units.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nMedical devices not included in the Register and related matters  Division 3\nSection 41ML\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mk-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mk-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f7551261f0543b2d1c74a5eba2175c6fad281599de2fc30f60c8a1a7ec0c7d9b",
      "skos:note": "Supplying medical devices not included in the Register is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mk",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MK Wholesale supply of medical devices not included in the",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 178,
      "values:originalText": "Register\nA person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person supplies a medical device in Australia; and\n(b) none of the following subparagraphs applies in relation to the\ndevice:\n(i) the device is of a kind included in the Register;\n(ia) the device is of a kind covered by an exemption in force\nunder section 41GS;\n(ii) the device is an exempt device;\n(iii) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsection 41HB or an authority under section 41HC;\n(iv) the device is the subject of an approval under\nsubsection 41HD(1), (1A) or (2) that is held by the\nperson; and\n(c) the person to whom the device is supplied is not the ultimate\nconsumer of the device.\nPenalty: 120 penalty units.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nMedical devices not included in the Register and related matters  Division 3\nSection 41ML\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mk-norm",
