      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person, by any means, advertises a medical device as\nbeing for a purpose; and\n(b) the device is of a kind included in the Register; and\n(c) the purpose is not a purpose accepted in relation to that\ninclusion.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "(The advertising must occur after registration.)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41ml-ss-3-logic-ltl-4",
