    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mo-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MO(4A) Criminal offences for misusing medical devices exempted for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mo-ss-4a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.190",
      "values:originalText": "(4A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is a health practitioner; and\n(b) the person is included in a class of health practitioners\nspecified in subsection 41HC(6) rules; and\n(c) the person supplies a medical device of a kind specified in\nthose rules; and\n(d) any of the following applies:\n(i) the supply is not in accordance with those rules;\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "skos:definition": "(4A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is a health practitioner; and\n(b) the person is included in a class of health practitioners\nspecified in subsection 41HC(6) rules; and\n(c) the person supplies a medical device of a kind specified in\nthose rules; and\n(d) any of the following applies:\n(i) the supply is not in accordance with those rules;\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mo"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
