        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mo-ss-4a-logic-argumentation-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "21b8fea6cbba4689a10e6460ef625d0a83a38d750d99b5d1ebf6422d1b711cc0",
      "skos:note": "Misusing medical devices is prohibited for specified health practitioners."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mo-ss-4a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MO(4A) Criminal offences for misusing medical devices exempted for",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 190,
      "values:originalText": "(4A) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is a health practitioner; and\n(b) the person is included in a class of health practitioners\nspecified in subsection 41HC(6) rules; and\n(c) the person supplies a medical device of a kind specified in\nthose rules; and\n(d) any of the following applies:\n(i) the supply is not in accordance with those rules;\n\nChapter 4  Medical devices"
    },
    {
