      "cml:conclusionText": "...the person commits an offence if..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41MQ Notification of adverse events etc. where application",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mq"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "withdrawn or lapses\n(1) If an application for inclusion of a kind of medical device in the\nRegister is withdrawn or lapses, the Secretary may give the\napplicant written notice requiring the applicant:\n(a) to inform the Secretary in writing whether the applicant is\naware of any information of a kind mentioned in\nsubsection 41MP(2) or 41MPA(2) relating to the kind of\ndevice; and\n(b) if the applicant is aware of such information, to give the\ninformation to the Secretary in writing.\n(2) Notice under subsection (1) may only be given within 10 working\ndays after an application is withdrawn or lapses.\n(3) A person commits an offence if the person fails to comply with the\nrequirements of a notice under subsection (1) within 20 working\ndays after the notice is given to the person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person gives information in purported compliance with a\nnotice under this section; and\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nOther offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4\nSection 41MR\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "withdrawn or lapses\n(1) If an application for inclusion of a kind of medical device in the\nRegister is withdrawn or lapses, the Secretary may give the\napplicant written notice requiring the applicant:\n(a) to inform the Secretary in writing whether the applicant is\naware of any information of a kind mentioned in\nsubsection 41MP(2) or 41MPA(2) relating to the kind of\ndevice; and\n(b) if the applicant is aware of such information, to give the\ninformation to the Secretary in writing.\n(2) Notice under subsection (1) may only be given within 10 working\ndays after an application is withdrawn or lapses.\n(3) A person commits an offence if the person fails to comply with the\nrequirements of a notice under subsection (1) within 20 working\ndays after the notice is given to the person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person gives information in purported compliance with a\nnotice under this section; and\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nOther offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4\nSection 41MR\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "93376f2dbbcc61c63c801535701930dcb75f809357e4e8beb1d0a27bc70524ce"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mq",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MQ Notification of adverse events etc. where application",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "withdrawn or lapses\n(1) If an application for inclusion of a kind of medical device in the\nRegister is withdrawn or lapses, the Secretary may give the\napplicant written notice requiring the applicant:\n(a) to inform the Secretary in writing whether the applicant is\naware of any information of a kind mentioned in\nsubsection 41MP(2) or 41MPA(2) relating to the kind of\ndevice; and\n(b) if the applicant is aware of such information, to give the\ninformation to the Secretary in writing.\n(2) Notice under subsection (1) may only be given within 10 working\ndays after an application is withdrawn or lapses.\n(3) A person commits an offence if the person fails to comply with the\nrequirements of a notice under subsection (1) within 20 working\ndays after the notice is given to the person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person gives information in purported compliance with a\nnotice under this section; and\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nOther offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4\nSection 41MR\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
