      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.198",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person gives information in purported compliance with a\nnotice under this section; and\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nOther offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4\nSection 41MR\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person gives information in purported compliance with a\nnotice under this section; and\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nOther offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4\nSection 41MR\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41mq-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3135d014c47ec912a070a5c43ec54b3bbba6312e51e894a8822fde120a2a9a23",
      "skos:note": "Giving false information in response to a notice is an offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41mq-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41MQ(4) Notification of adverse events etc. where application",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 198,
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person gives information in purported compliance with a\nnotice under this section; and\n(b) the information is false or misleading in a material particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n\nMedical devices  Chapter 4\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to medical devices  Part 4-11\nOther offences and civil penalty provisions  Division 4\nSection 41MR\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
