      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41Q Offences and civil penalty provision—importing vaping goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.204",
      "values:originalText": "into Australia\nOffences\n(1) A person commits an offence if the person imports vaping goods\ninto Australia.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person imports\nvaping goods into Australia.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalty provision\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person imports vaping\ngoods into Australia.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units.\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate\ncontravention of that subsection in respect of each unit of vaping\ngoods imported by the person into Australia.\nNote:\nFor unit of vaping goods, see subsection 3(1).\n\nVaping goods  Chapter 4A\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to vaping goods  Part 4A-2\nGeneral  Division 1\nSection 41QA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nException\n(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping\ngoods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901.\nNote:\nThe person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsection 41QE of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "into Australia\nOffences\n(1) A person commits an offence if the person imports vaping goods\ninto Australia.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person imports\nvaping goods into Australia.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalty provision\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person imports vaping\ngoods into Australia.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units.\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate\ncontravention of that subsection in respect of each unit of vaping\ngoods imported by the person into Australia.\nNote:\nFor unit of vaping goods, see subsection 3(1).\n\nVaping goods  Chapter 4A\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to vaping goods  Part 4A-2\nGeneral  Division 1\nSection 41QA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nException\n(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping\ngoods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901.\nNote:\nThe person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsection 41QE of this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8b405996892544c4e5929d35ca68d582158dded01ee5c7d0c531c8d2ed6f418c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41Q Offences and civil penalty provision—importing vaping goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 204,
      "values:originalText": "into Australia\nOffences\n(1) A person commits an offence if the person imports vaping goods\ninto Australia.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person imports\nvaping goods into Australia.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalty provision\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person imports vaping\ngoods into Australia.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units.\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate\ncontravention of that subsection in respect of each unit of vaping\ngoods imported by the person into Australia.\nNote:\nFor unit of vaping goods, see subsection 3(1).\n\nVaping goods  Chapter 4A\nOffences and civil penalty provisions relating to vaping goods  Part 4A-2\nGeneral  Division 1\nSection 41QA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nException\n(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping\ngoods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901.\nNote:\nThe person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsection 41QE of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-1",
