    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41Q(5) Offences and civil penalty provision—importing vaping goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41q-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.204",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping\ngoods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901.\nNote:\nThe person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsection 41QE of this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping\ngoods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901.\nNote:\nThe person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsection 41QE of this Act.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ff7804e1eec2aa6b8c27ad54cbf802a47f7aecc87ee1760be2a4911e649fa44a",
      "skos:note": "Exemptions from subsections (1) to (4)"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41q-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41Q(5) Offences and civil penalty provision—importing vaping goods",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 204,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Subsections (1) to (4) do not apply if the importation of the vaping\ngoods is not prohibited under the Customs Act 1901.\nNote:\nThe person bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in\nsubsection (5): see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code and\nsection 41QE of this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41q-ss-5-norm",
