      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41QA Offences and civil penalty provision—manufacturing vaping",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41qa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.205",
      "values:originalText": "goods in Australia\nOffences\n(1) A person commits an offence if the person manufactures, or carries\nout a step in the manufacture of, vaping goods in Australia.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person\nmanufactures, or carries out a step in the manufacture of, vaping\ngoods in Australia.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalty provision\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person manufactures, or\ncarries out a step in the manufacture of, vaping goods in Australia.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units.\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate\ncontravention of that subsection in respect of the manufacture, or\nthe carrying out of the step in the manufacture, by the person of\neach unit of vaping goods.\n\nChapter 4A  Vaping goods",
      "skos:definition": "goods in Australia\nOffences\n(1) A person commits an offence if the person manufactures, or carries\nout a step in the manufacture of, vaping goods in Australia.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 7 years or 5,000 penalty units, or both.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence of strict liability if the person\nmanufactures, or carries out a step in the manufacture of, vaping\ngoods in Australia.\nPenalty: 200 penalty units.\nCivil penalty provision\n(3) A person contravenes this subsection if the person manufactures, or\ncarries out a step in the manufacture of, vaping goods in Australia.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—7,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—70,000 penalty units.\n(4) A person who contravenes subsection (3) commits a separate\ncontravention of that subsection in respect of the manufacture, or\nthe carrying out of the step in the manufacture, by the person of\neach unit of vaping goods.\n\nChapter 4A  Vaping goods",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qa-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qa-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qa-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41qa-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b775ca97317081f36d1a0ea0e8f65625fac7c7fda620f9d15ba77db7fd1da6b3"
    },
    {
