    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41rc-ss-2c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "41RC(2C) Secretary may give consent",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41rc-ss-2c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.222",
      "values:originalText": "(2C) Without limiting subsection (2B), the decision-making principles\nmay set out any of the following:\n(a) circumstances in which a consent under subsection (1) must\nnot be given;\n(b) matters that must be taken into account in making a decision\nunder subsection (1);\n(c) matters that must not be taken into account in making a\ndecision under subsection (1);\n(d) matters that may be taken into account in making a decision\nunder subsection (1).",
      "skos:definition": "(2C) Without limiting subsection (2B), the decision-making principles\nmay set out any of the following:\n(a) circumstances in which a consent under subsection (1) must\nnot be given;\n(b) matters that must be taken into account in making a decision\nunder subsection (1);\n(c) matters that must not be taken into account in making a\ndecision under subsection (1);\n(d) matters that may be taken into account in making a decision\nunder subsection (1).",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41rc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41rc-ss-2c-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-41rc-ss-2c-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6d073cc73c6233749d657e7e239981cca2c8912933a130db8cfa498c09f77008",
      "skos:note": "Secretary may give consent under certain circumstances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-41rc-ss-2c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "41RC(2C) Secretary may give consent",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 222,
      "values:originalText": "(2C) Without limiting subsection (2B), the decision-making principles\nmay set out any of the following:\n(a) circumstances in which a consent under subsection (1) must\nnot be given;\n(b) matters that must be taken into account in making a decision\nunder subsection (1);\n(c) matters that must not be taken into account in making a\ndecision under subsection (1);\n(d) matters that may be taken into account in making a decision\nunder subsection (1)."
    },
