      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.228",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an instrument\nunder subsection (1) of this section may make provision in relation\nto a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without\nmodification, any matter contained in an instrument or other\nwriting as in force or existing from time to time.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, an instrument\nunder subsection (1) of this section may make provision in relation\nto a matter by applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without\nmodification, any matter contained in an instrument or other\nwriting as in force or existing from time to time.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "values:partOf": {
