    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DF Approval of use of restricted representation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42df"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.231",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an application for approval of the use of a restricted\nrepresentation is made, the Secretary must approve the use of the\nrestricted representation if the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) the representation is accurate and balanced; and\n(b) the representation is not misleading or likely to be\nmisleading.\n(2) Otherwise, the Secretary must refuse to approve the use of the\nrestricted representation.\n(3) An approval may be subject to conditions imposed by the\nSecretary.\n(4) In deciding whether to approve or refuse to approve the use of a\nrestricted representation, the Secretary must take into\nconsideration:\n(b) any advice of a committee that is established under the\nregulations and is prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph; and\n(c) the public interest criteria mentioned in the part of the\nTherapeutic Goods Advertising Code dealing with restricted\nrepresentations.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If an application for approval of the use of a restricted\nrepresentation is made, the Secretary must approve the use of the\nrestricted representation if the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) the representation is accurate and balanced; and\n(b) the representation is not misleading or likely to be\nmisleading.\n(2) Otherwise, the Secretary must refuse to approve the use of the\nrestricted representation.\n(3) An approval may be subject to conditions imposed by the\nSecretary.\n(4) In deciding whether to approve or refuse to approve the use of a\nrestricted representation, the Secretary must take into\nconsideration:\n(b) any advice of a committee that is established under the\nregulations and is prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph; and\n(c) the public interest criteria mentioned in the part of the\nTherapeutic Goods Advertising Code dealing with restricted\nrepresentations.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "624fda3e478b3cf67b1abafa0da6c19b235ff7113fd82797be48efc538954d1d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42df",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DF Approval of use of restricted representation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 231,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If an application for approval of the use of a restricted\nrepresentation is made, the Secretary must approve the use of the\nrestricted representation if the Secretary is satisfied that:\n(a) the representation is accurate and balanced; and\n(b) the representation is not misleading or likely to be\nmisleading.\n(2) Otherwise, the Secretary must refuse to approve the use of the\nrestricted representation.\n(3) An approval may be subject to conditions imposed by the\nSecretary.\n(4) In deciding whether to approve or refuse to approve the use of a\nrestricted representation, the Secretary must take into\nconsideration:\n(b) any advice of a committee that is established under the\nregulations and is prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph; and\n(c) the public interest criteria mentioned in the part of the\nTherapeutic Goods Advertising Code dealing with restricted\nrepresentations.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"
    },
