    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DF(4) Approval of use of restricted representation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42df-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.231",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In deciding whether to approve or refuse to approve the use of a\nrestricted representation, the Secretary must take into\nconsideration:\n(b) any advice of a committee that is established under the\nregulations and is prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph; and\n(c) the public interest criteria mentioned in the part of the\nTherapeutic Goods Advertising Code dealing with restricted\nrepresentations.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In deciding whether to approve or refuse to approve the use of a\nrestricted representation, the Secretary must take into\nconsideration:\n(b) any advice of a committee that is established under the\nregulations and is prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph; and\n(c) the public interest criteria mentioned in the part of the\nTherapeutic Goods Advertising Code dealing with restricted\nrepresentations.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "466a0b3ea3095f44f9b14d2222619bbb627e27a1b5f946950ea0167e62c510a1",
      "skos:note": "Secretary must consider certain factors when deciding to approve or refuse the use of a restricted representation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42df-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DF(4) Approval of use of restricted representation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 231,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In deciding whether to approve or refuse to approve the use of a\nrestricted representation, the Secretary must take into\nconsideration:\n(b) any advice of a committee that is established under the\nregulations and is prescribed by the regulations for the\npurposes of this paragraph; and\n(c) the public interest criteria mentioned in the part of the\nTherapeutic Goods Advertising Code dealing with restricted\nrepresentations.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42df-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
