      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Secretary has an obligation to consider certain factors.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dg",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DG Notice of approval or refusal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dg"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.232",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must give written notice to the applicant of the\napproval of, or of the refusal to approve, the use of a restricted\nrepresentation.\n(2) If written notice is not given to the applicant within the period of\n60 days after the day on which the application was made (or within\nsuch longer period as the Secretary specifies by written notice to\nthe applicant before the end of that period), the Secretary is taken\nto have approved the use of the restricted representation at the end\nof the period.\n(3) If an approval is subject to conditions, the conditions must be set\nout in the notice.\n(4) A notice of refusal to approve the use of a restricted representation\nmust:\n(a) give the Secretary’s reasons for the refusal; and\n(b) inform the applicant of the applicant’s right to have the\nSecretary’s decision reviewed by the Minister under\nsection 60.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary must give written notice to the applicant of the\napproval of, or of the refusal to approve, the use of a restricted\nrepresentation.\n(2) If written notice is not given to the applicant within the period of\n60 days after the day on which the application was made (or within\nsuch longer period as the Secretary specifies by written notice to\nthe applicant before the end of that period), the Secretary is taken\nto have approved the use of the restricted representation at the end\nof the period.\n(3) If an approval is subject to conditions, the conditions must be set\nout in the notice.\n(4) A notice of refusal to approve the use of a restricted representation\nmust:\n(a) give the Secretary’s reasons for the refusal; and\n(b) inform the applicant of the applicant’s right to have the\nSecretary’s decision reviewed by the Minister under\nsection 60.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dg-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dg-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dg-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dg-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9b3a6996124fa635eccdd75a83a168035ea51403d41e8676b1d169a2f87ea01"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dg",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DG Notice of approval or refusal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 232,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary must give written notice to the applicant of the\napproval of, or of the refusal to approve, the use of a restricted\nrepresentation.\n(2) If written notice is not given to the applicant within the period of\n60 days after the day on which the application was made (or within\nsuch longer period as the Secretary specifies by written notice to\nthe applicant before the end of that period), the Secretary is taken\nto have approved the use of the restricted representation at the end\nof the period.\n(3) If an approval is subject to conditions, the conditions must be set\nout in the notice.\n(4) A notice of refusal to approve the use of a restricted representation\nmust:\n(a) give the Secretary’s reasons for the refusal; and\n(b) inform the applicant of the applicant’s right to have the\nSecretary’s decision reviewed by the Minister under\nsection 60."
    },
