    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42di",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DI Withdrawal of approval",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42di"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.232",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary, by written notice, may withdraw the approval of the\nuse of a restricted representation if:\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that:\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nGeneral provisions about advertising therapeutic goods  Division 3\nSection 42DJ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(i) information given by the applicant in the application\nwas false or incorrect and the Secretary, or the Minister\non review of a decision of the Secretary under\nsection 42DF or 42DH, relied on the information in\ndeciding to approve the use of the representation; or\n(ii) the restricted representation has become a prohibited\nrepresentation; or\n(iii) there has been a breach of a condition of approval; or\n(b) both:\n(i) additional information about the safety or efficacy of the\ntherapeutic goods becomes available; and\n(ii) the Secretary is satisfied that, if that information had\nbeen available at the time of the approval, the Secretary\nwould not have approved the use of the restricted\nrepresentation; or\n(c) the use of the restricted representation is permitted under\nsubsection 42DK(1).\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) give the Secretary’s reasons for the withdrawal; and\n(b) inform the approval holder of the approval holder’s right to\nhave the Secretary’s decision reviewed by the Minister under\nsection 60.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary, by written notice, may withdraw the approval of the\nuse of a restricted representation if:\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that:\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nGeneral provisions about advertising therapeutic goods  Division 3\nSection 42DJ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(i) information given by the applicant in the application\nwas false or incorrect and the Secretary, or the Minister\non review of a decision of the Secretary under\nsection 42DF or 42DH, relied on the information in\ndeciding to approve the use of the representation; or\n(ii) the restricted representation has become a prohibited\nrepresentation; or\n(iii) there has been a breach of a condition of approval; or\n(b) both:\n(i) additional information about the safety or efficacy of the\ntherapeutic goods becomes available; and\n(ii) the Secretary is satisfied that, if that information had\nbeen available at the time of the approval, the Secretary\nwould not have approved the use of the restricted\nrepresentation; or\n(c) the use of the restricted representation is permitted under\nsubsection 42DK(1).\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) give the Secretary’s reasons for the withdrawal; and\n(b) inform the approval holder of the approval holder’s right to\nhave the Secretary’s decision reviewed by the Minister under\nsection 60.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42di-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42di-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c134bf65089c4538deeed4c329e2ac919e4fab55ff35442d8c4784d1adcc5e17"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42di",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DI Withdrawal of approval",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 232,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary, by written notice, may withdraw the approval of the\nuse of a restricted representation if:\n(a) the Secretary is satisfied that:\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nGeneral provisions about advertising therapeutic goods  Division 3\nSection 42DJ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(i) information given by the applicant in the application\nwas false or incorrect and the Secretary, or the Minister\non review of a decision of the Secretary under\nsection 42DF or 42DH, relied on the information in\ndeciding to approve the use of the representation; or\n(ii) the restricted representation has become a prohibited\nrepresentation; or\n(iii) there has been a breach of a condition of approval; or\n(b) both:\n(i) additional information about the safety or efficacy of the\ntherapeutic goods becomes available; and\n(ii) the Secretary is satisfied that, if that information had\nbeen available at the time of the approval, the Secretary\nwould not have approved the use of the restricted\nrepresentation; or\n(c) the use of the restricted representation is permitted under\nsubsection 42DK(1).\n(2) The notice must:\n(a) give the Secretary’s reasons for the withdrawal; and\n(b) inform the approval holder of the approval holder’s right to\nhave the Secretary’s decision reviewed by the Minister under\nsection 60."
    },
