      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.235",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic\ngoods; and\n(b) subsection (5), (6), (7), (8), (9), (10), (11) or (12) applies to\nthe advertisement; and\n(c) either:\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic\ngoods; and\n(b) subsection (5), (6), (7), (8), (9), (10), (11) or (12) applies to\nthe advertisement; and\n(c) either:\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "cml:asserts": [
