    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DM Offences—non-compliance with the Therapeutic Goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dm"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.243",
      "values:originalText": "Advertising Code\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic\ngoods; and\n(b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic\nGoods Advertising Code; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement has\nresulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm\nor injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement, if\nthe goods were so used, would result in, or would be\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic\ngoods; and\n(b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic\nGoods Advertising Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "Advertising Code\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic\ngoods; and\n(b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic\nGoods Advertising Code; and\n(c) either:\n(i) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement has\nresulted in, will result in, or is likely to result in, harm\nor injury to any person; or\n(ii) the use of the goods in reliance on the advertisement, if\nthe goods were so used, would result in, or would be\nlikely to result in, harm or injury to any person.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 5 years or 4,000 penalty units, or both.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) causes the advertising, by any means, of therapeutic\ngoods; and\n(b) the advertisement does not comply with the Therapeutic\nGoods Advertising Code.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n(3) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person:\n(i) advertises, by any means, therapeutic goods; or\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dm-ss-2"
