    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DP Offences—dissemination of generic information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dp"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.246",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information\nabout therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the dissemination of that generic information does not\ncomply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the\npurposes of section 42DO.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nGeneric information about ingredients or components of therapeutic goods  Division 4\nSection 42DQ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information\nabout therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the dissemination of that generic information does not\ncomply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the\npurposes of section 42DO.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information\nabout therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the dissemination of that generic information does not\ncomply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the\npurposes of section 42DO.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nGeneric information about ingredients or components of therapeutic goods  Division 4\nSection 42DQ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information\nabout therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the dissemination of that generic information does not\ncomply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the\npurposes of section 42DO.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dp-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "761f9fe9d7758baeb94c994517171b62534f87ab7823c519511ee2098f7854a2"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dp",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DP Offences—dissemination of generic information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 246,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information\nabout therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the dissemination of that generic information does not\ncomply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the\npurposes of section 42DO.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nGeneric information about ingredients or components of therapeutic goods  Division 4\nSection 42DQ\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person disseminates, by any means, generic information\nabout therapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the dissemination of that generic information does not\ncomply with the provisions of the Therapeutic Goods\nAdvertising Code that are prescribed by regulations for the\npurposes of section 42DO.\nPenalty: 100 penalty units.\n(3) An offence against subsection (2) is an offence of strict liability."
    },
