      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.248",
      "values:originalText": "(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 42DR; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person is given a notice under section 42DR; and\n(b) the person gives information or produces a document in\ncompliance or purported compliance with the notice; and\n(c) the information or document is false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dr"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dr-ss-4-norm"
        },
