    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42du",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DU Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42du"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.250",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 42DR on the ground that the information\nor the production of the document might tend to incriminate the\nperson or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 42DS(4) or (5); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 42DT.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nDirections about advertisements or generic information  Division 6\nSection 42DV\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 42DR on the ground that the information\nor the production of the document might tend to incriminate the\nperson or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 42DS(4) or (5); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 42DT.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nDirections about advertisements or generic information  Division 6\nSection 42DV\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42du-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42du-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "778387bc099dead7c513a64476e3d1d3a5437061c36f6a32040953663fac44d1"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42du",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DU Self-incrimination",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 250,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person is not excused from giving information or producing a\ndocument under section 42DR on the ground that the information\nor the production of the document might tend to incriminate the\nperson or expose the person to a penalty.\n(2) However, in the case of an individual:\n(a) the information given or the document produced; and\n(b) giving the information or producing the document; and\n(c) any information, document or thing obtained as a direct or\nindirect consequence of giving the information or producing\nthe document;\nare not admissible in evidence against the individual:\n(d) in criminal proceedings, except proceedings for an offence\nagainst subsection 42DS(4) or (5); or\n(e) in civil proceedings, except proceedings under section 42Y\nfor a contravention of section 42DT.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nAdvertising and generic information  Part 5-1\nDirections about advertisements or generic information  Division 6\nSection 42DV\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
