    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dv",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DV Directions about advertisements or generic information",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dv"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.251",
      "values:originalText": "Advertisements\n(1) If, in relation to the advertising of therapeutic goods, the Secretary\nis satisfied that there has been a contravention of this Act or the\nregulations, the Secretary may, in writing, direct a person\napparently responsible for advertising the therapeutic goods, or for\ncausing the advertising of the therapeutic goods, to do one or more\nof the following:\n(a) cease the advertisement;\n(b) make a retraction;\n(c) make a correction;\n(d) recover any advertisement that is still in circulation;\n(e) destroy the advertisement;\n(f) cease making a particular claim or representation made by\nthe advertisement.\nGeneric information\n(2) If, in relation to the dissemination of generic information about\ntherapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public, the\nSecretary is satisfied that there has been a contravention of this Act\nor the regulations, the Secretary may, in writing, direct a person\napparently responsible for the dissemination, or for causing the\ndissemination, to do one or more of the following:\n(a) withdraw the generic information;\n(b) make a retraction;\n(c) make a correction;\n(d) recover any generic information that is still in circulation;\n(e) destroy the generic information;\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "Advertisements\n(1) If, in relation to the advertising of therapeutic goods, the Secretary\nis satisfied that there has been a contravention of this Act or the\nregulations, the Secretary may, in writing, direct a person\napparently responsible for advertising the therapeutic goods, or for\ncausing the advertising of the therapeutic goods, to do one or more\nof the following:\n(a) cease the advertisement;\n(b) make a retraction;\n(c) make a correction;\n(d) recover any advertisement that is still in circulation;\n(e) destroy the advertisement;\n(f) cease making a particular claim or representation made by\nthe advertisement.\nGeneric information\n(2) If, in relation to the dissemination of generic information about\ntherapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public, the\nSecretary is satisfied that there has been a contravention of this Act\nor the regulations, the Secretary may, in writing, direct a person\napparently responsible for the dissemination, or for causing the\ndissemination, to do one or more of the following:\n(a) withdraw the generic information;\n(b) make a retraction;\n(c) make a correction;\n(d) recover any generic information that is still in circulation;\n(e) destroy the generic information;\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dv-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dv-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f60f07a4d550cfae0f22b38e69e609a4d6b1123d9c70bfda65811934d13d8efa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dv",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DV Directions about advertisements or generic information",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 251,
      "values:originalText": "Advertisements\n(1) If, in relation to the advertising of therapeutic goods, the Secretary\nis satisfied that there has been a contravention of this Act or the\nregulations, the Secretary may, in writing, direct a person\napparently responsible for advertising the therapeutic goods, or for\ncausing the advertising of the therapeutic goods, to do one or more\nof the following:\n(a) cease the advertisement;\n(b) make a retraction;\n(c) make a correction;\n(d) recover any advertisement that is still in circulation;\n(e) destroy the advertisement;\n(f) cease making a particular claim or representation made by\nthe advertisement.\nGeneric information\n(2) If, in relation to the dissemination of generic information about\ntherapeutic goods to the public or a section of the public, the\nSecretary is satisfied that there has been a contravention of this Act\nor the regulations, the Secretary may, in writing, direct a person\napparently responsible for the dissemination, or for causing the\ndissemination, to do one or more of the following:\n(a) withdraw the generic information;\n(b) make a retraction;\n(c) make a correction;\n(d) recover any generic information that is still in circulation;\n(e) destroy the generic information;\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"
    },
