    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dy",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42DY Secretary may issue a public warning notice",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dy"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.255",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may issue to the public a written notice containing a\nwarning about therapeutic goods if:\n(a) the Secretary reasonably suspects that there has been a\ncontravention of this Act or the regulations in relation to:\n(i) the advertising of the therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) the dissemination of generic information about the\ntherapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that it is in the public interest to\nissue the notice.\n(2) If:\n(a) the Secretary gives a person a notice (the substantiation\nnotice) under subsection 42DR(1) or (2); and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the substantiation notice; and\n(c) the Secretary is satisfied that it is in the public interest to\nissue a notice under this subsection;\nthe Secretary may issue to the public a written notice containing a\nwarning that the person has failed to comply with the\nsubstantiation notice, and specifying the matter to which the\nsubstantiation notice related.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n(4) A notice under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may issue to the public a written notice containing a\nwarning about therapeutic goods if:\n(a) the Secretary reasonably suspects that there has been a\ncontravention of this Act or the regulations in relation to:\n(i) the advertising of the therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) the dissemination of generic information about the\ntherapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that it is in the public interest to\nissue the notice.\n(2) If:\n(a) the Secretary gives a person a notice (the substantiation\nnotice) under subsection 42DR(1) or (2); and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the substantiation notice; and\n(c) the Secretary is satisfied that it is in the public interest to\nissue a notice under this subsection;\nthe Secretary may issue to the public a written notice containing a\nwarning that the person has failed to comply with the\nsubstantiation notice, and specifying the matter to which the\nsubstantiation notice related.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n(4) A notice under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dy-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dy-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dy-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42dy-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ed8b55fccac54c9df194a8c727445216416df10e4427b230c637538c9792132"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42dy",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42DY Secretary may issue a public warning notice",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 255,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may issue to the public a written notice containing a\nwarning about therapeutic goods if:\n(a) the Secretary reasonably suspects that there has been a\ncontravention of this Act or the regulations in relation to:\n(i) the advertising of the therapeutic goods; or\n(ii) the dissemination of generic information about the\ntherapeutic goods to the public or a section of the\npublic; and\n(b) the Secretary is satisfied that it is in the public interest to\nissue the notice.\n(2) If:\n(a) the Secretary gives a person a notice (the substantiation\nnotice) under subsection 42DR(1) or (2); and\n(b) the person fails to comply with the substantiation notice; and\n(c) the Secretary is satisfied that it is in the public interest to\nissue a notice under this subsection;\nthe Secretary may issue to the public a written notice containing a\nwarning that the person has failed to comply with the\nsubstantiation notice, and specifying the matter to which the\nsubstantiation notice related.\n(3) Subsection (2) does not limit subsection (1).\n(4) A notice under this section is not a legislative instrument.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering"
    },
