    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42F Customs treatment of counterfeit therapeutic goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.272",
      "values:originalText": "Imported counterfeit therapeutic goods\n(1) If the Secretary notifies the Comptroller-General of Customs in\nwriting that the Secretary wishes the Customs Act 1901 to apply to\nan import of counterfeit therapeutic goods, that Act has effect as if\nthe goods included in the import were goods described as forfeited\nto the Crown under section 229 of that Act because they were\nprohibited imports within the meaning of that Act.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nCounterfeit therapeutic goods  Part 5-2\n\nSection 42F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nExported counterfeit therapeutic goods\n(2) If the Secretary notifies the Comptroller-General of Customs in\nwriting that the Secretary wishes the Customs Act 1901 to apply to\nan export of counterfeit therapeutic goods, that Act has effect as if\nthe goods included in the export were goods described as forfeited\nto the Crown under section 229 of that Act because they were\nprohibited exports within the meaning of that Act.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "Imported counterfeit therapeutic goods\n(1) If the Secretary notifies the Comptroller-General of Customs in\nwriting that the Secretary wishes the Customs Act 1901 to apply to\nan import of counterfeit therapeutic goods, that Act has effect as if\nthe goods included in the import were goods described as forfeited\nto the Crown under section 229 of that Act because they were\nprohibited imports within the meaning of that Act.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nCounterfeit therapeutic goods  Part 5-2\n\nSection 42F\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nExported counterfeit therapeutic goods\n(2) If the Secretary notifies the Comptroller-General of Customs in\nwriting that the Secretary wishes the Customs Act 1901 to apply to\nan export of counterfeit therapeutic goods, that Act has effect as if\nthe goods included in the export were goods described as forfeited\nto the Crown under section 229 of that Act because they were\nprohibited exports within the meaning of that Act.\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42f-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42f-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c05a7a133de5dcfa786ea495d8d6c5ee5f67dd5ad0ee171e7f3892177d3d8896"
    },
    {
