    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42t-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42T(3) Notifying of actual or potential tampering",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 274,
      "values:originalText": "(3) For the purposes of subparagraph (2)(c)(ii), the person is only\ntaken to be negligent as to the fact that the information or demand\nis of the kind referred to in that subparagraph if:\n(a) the person’s acts or omissions involve such a great falling\nshort of the standard of care that a reasonable person would\nexercise in the circumstances; and\n(b) there is such a high risk that the information or demand is of\nthat kind;\nthat the acts or omissions merit criminal punishment."
    },
    {
