    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42va",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42VA Civil penalty relating to the recall of therapeutic goods",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42va"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.278",
      "values:originalText": "because of actual or potential tampering\nA person contravenes this section if the person fails to comply with\na requirement under subsection 42V(1) in relation to a supply of\ntherapeutic goods.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.",
      "skos:definition": "because of actual or potential tampering\nA person contravenes this section if the person fails to comply with\na requirement under subsection 42V(1) in relation to a supply of\ntherapeutic goods.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42va-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42va-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "945ecb8c26aa743a479f5b981e0d72e4edbbf2f81f3a1b67330006eeeda86471",
      "skos:note": "Failure to comply with requirements for therapeutic goods supply"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42va",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42VA Civil penalty relating to the recall of therapeutic goods",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 278,
      "values:originalText": "because of actual or potential tampering\nA person contravenes this section if the person fails to comply with\na requirement under subsection 42V(1) in relation to a supply of\ntherapeutic goods.\nMaximum civil penalty:\n(a) for an individual—5,000 penalty units; and\n(b) for a body corporate—50,000 penalty units."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42va-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42va"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42va-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of non-compliance",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Failure to comply with requirements",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Contravenes section"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42vb",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42VB Relief from liability for contraventions relating to the recall of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42vb"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.278",
      "values:originalText": "therapeutic goods because of actual or potential\ntampering\n(1) If:\n(a) proceedings for the contravention of section 42VA (a civil\npenalty provision) are brought against a person; and\n(b) in the proceedings it appears to the Court that the person has,\nor may have, contravened that section but that:\n(i) the person has acted honestly; and\n(ii) having regard to all the circumstances of the case, the\nperson ought fairly to be excused for the contravention;\nthe Court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from a\nliability to which the person would otherwise be subject, or that\nmight otherwise be imposed on the person, because of the\ncontravention.\n(2) If a person thinks that proceedings for the contravention of\nsection 42VA will or may be begun against them, they may apply\nto the Court for relief.\n(3) On an application under subsection (2), the Court may grant relief\nunder subsection (1) as if proceedings had been begun in the Court.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nProduct tampering  Part 5-3\n\nSection 42W\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (2) as applying for the purposes of a\ncase tried by a judge with a jury:\n(a) a reference in that subsection to the Court is a reference to\nthe judge; and\n(b) the relief that may be granted includes withdrawing the case\nin whole or in part from the jury and directing judgment to be\nentered for the person on such terms as to costs as the judge\nthinks appropriate.",
      "skos:definition": "therapeutic goods because of actual or potential\ntampering\n(1) If:\n(a) proceedings for the contravention of section 42VA (a civil\npenalty provision) are brought against a person; and\n(b) in the proceedings it appears to the Court that the person has,\nor may have, contravened that section but that:\n(i) the person has acted honestly; and\n(ii) having regard to all the circumstances of the case, the\nperson ought fairly to be excused for the contravention;\nthe Court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from a\nliability to which the person would otherwise be subject, or that\nmight otherwise be imposed on the person, because of the\ncontravention.\n(2) If a person thinks that proceedings for the contravention of\nsection 42VA will or may be begun against them, they may apply\nto the Court for relief.\n(3) On an application under subsection (2), the Court may grant relief\nunder subsection (1) as if proceedings had been begun in the Court.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nProduct tampering  Part 5-3\n\nSection 42W\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (2) as applying for the purposes of a\ncase tried by a judge with a jury:\n(a) a reference in that subsection to the Court is a reference to\nthe judge; and\n(b) the relief that may be granted includes withdrawing the case\nin whole or in part from the jury and directing judgment to be\nentered for the person on such terms as to costs as the judge\nthinks appropriate.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42vb-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42vb-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42vb-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42vb-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8bfec45cc6a836eb96b9895d577de34cadbedc0a85f61140710f65a1effee643"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42vb",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42VB Relief from liability for contraventions relating to the recall of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 278,
      "values:originalText": "therapeutic goods because of actual or potential\ntampering\n(1) If:\n(a) proceedings for the contravention of section 42VA (a civil\npenalty provision) are brought against a person; and\n(b) in the proceedings it appears to the Court that the person has,\nor may have, contravened that section but that:\n(i) the person has acted honestly; and\n(ii) having regard to all the circumstances of the case, the\nperson ought fairly to be excused for the contravention;\nthe Court may relieve the person either wholly or partly from a\nliability to which the person would otherwise be subject, or that\nmight otherwise be imposed on the person, because of the\ncontravention.\n(2) If a person thinks that proceedings for the contravention of\nsection 42VA will or may be begun against them, they may apply\nto the Court for relief.\n(3) On an application under subsection (2), the Court may grant relief\nunder subsection (1) as if proceedings had been begun in the Court.\n\nAdvertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering  Chapter 5\nProduct tampering  Part 5-3\n\nSection 42W\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (2) as applying for the purposes of a\ncase tried by a judge with a jury:\n(a) a reference in that subsection to the Court is a reference to\nthe judge; and\n(b) the relief that may be granted includes withdrawing the case\nin whole or in part from the jury and directing judgment to be\nentered for the person on such terms as to costs as the judge\nthinks appropriate."
    },
