    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42w",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42W Supply etc. of therapeutic goods that are subject to recall",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42w"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.279",
      "values:originalText": "requirements\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person supplies therapeutic goods in Australia; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a\nkind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which\nrequirements have been imposed under section 42V, on\nthat person or another person, to recall therapeutic\ngoods; or\n(ii) the therapeutic goods are of such a kind, or are included\nin such a batch, and the person is reckless as to that fact;\nand\n(c) the Secretary has not consented in writing to the supply.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports therapeutic goods from Australia; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a\nkind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which\nrequirements have been imposed under section 42V, on\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
      "skos:definition": "requirements\n(1) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person supplies therapeutic goods in Australia; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a\nkind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which\nrequirements have been imposed under section 42V, on\nthat person or another person, to recall therapeutic\ngoods; or\n(ii) the therapeutic goods are of such a kind, or are included\nin such a batch, and the person is reckless as to that fact;\nand\n(c) the Secretary has not consented in writing to the supply.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 12 months or 1,000 penalty units, or\nboth.\nNote:\nFor the liability of an executive officer of a body corporate, see\nsections 54B and 54BA.\n(2) A person commits an offence if:\n(a) the person exports therapeutic goods from Australia; and\n(b) either:\n(i) the person knows that the therapeutic goods are of a\nkind, or are included in a batch, in respect of which\nrequirements have been imposed under section 42V, on\n\nChapter 5  Advertising, counterfeit therapeutic goods and product tampering",
