    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42Y Federal Court may order person to pay pecuniary penalty for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42y"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.281",
      "values:originalText": "contravening civil penalty provision\nApplication for order\n(1) Within 6 years of a person (the wrongdoer) contravening a civil\npenalty provision, the Secretary may apply on behalf of the\nCommonwealth to the Federal Court for an order that the\nwrongdoer pay the Commonwealth a pecuniary penalty.\nCourt may order wrongdoer to pay pecuniary penalty\n(2) If the Court is satisfied that the wrongdoer has contravened a civil\npenalty provision, the Court may order the wrongdoer to pay to the\nCommonwealth for each contravention the pecuniary penalty that\nthe Court determines is appropriate (but not more than the\nmaximum amount specified for the provision).\nDetermining amount of pecuniary penalty\n(3) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement",
      "skos:definition": "contravening civil penalty provision\nApplication for order\n(1) Within 6 years of a person (the wrongdoer) contravening a civil\npenalty provision, the Secretary may apply on behalf of the\nCommonwealth to the Federal Court for an order that the\nwrongdoer pay the Commonwealth a pecuniary penalty.\nCourt may order wrongdoer to pay pecuniary penalty\n(2) If the Court is satisfied that the wrongdoer has contravened a civil\npenalty provision, the Court may order the wrongdoer to pay to the\nCommonwealth for each contravention the pecuniary penalty that\nthe Court determines is appropriate (but not more than the\nmaximum amount specified for the provision).\nDetermining amount of pecuniary penalty\n(3) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e87c0ec939fd8e6eadbf09bfac450b20b64c5abcbec3a0facadf698d832f455e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42y",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42Y Federal Court may order person to pay pecuniary penalty for",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 281,
      "values:originalText": "contravening civil penalty provision\nApplication for order\n(1) Within 6 years of a person (the wrongdoer) contravening a civil\npenalty provision, the Secretary may apply on behalf of the\nCommonwealth to the Federal Court for an order that the\nwrongdoer pay the Commonwealth a pecuniary penalty.\nCourt may order wrongdoer to pay pecuniary penalty\n(2) If the Court is satisfied that the wrongdoer has contravened a civil\npenalty provision, the Court may order the wrongdoer to pay to the\nCommonwealth for each contravention the pecuniary penalty that\nthe Court determines is appropriate (but not more than the\nmaximum amount specified for the provision).\nDetermining amount of pecuniary penalty\n(3) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement"
    },
