    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42Y(2) Federal Court may order person to pay pecuniary penalty for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42y-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.281",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the Court is satisfied that the wrongdoer has contravened a civil\npenalty provision, the Court may order the wrongdoer to pay to the\nCommonwealth for each contravention the pecuniary penalty that\nthe Court determines is appropriate (but not more than the\nmaximum amount specified for the provision).\nDetermining amount of pecuniary penalty",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the Court is satisfied that the wrongdoer has contravened a civil\npenalty provision, the Court may order the wrongdoer to pay to the\nCommonwealth for each contravention the pecuniary penalty that\nthe Court determines is appropriate (but not more than the\nmaximum amount specified for the provision).\nDetermining amount of pecuniary penalty",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
