    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42Y(3) Federal Court may order person to pay pecuniary penalty for",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42y-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.281",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In determining the pecuniary penalty, the Court must have regard\nto all relevant matters, including:\n(a) the nature and extent of the contravention; and\n(b) the nature and extent of any loss or damage suffered as a\nresult of the contravention; and\n(c) the circumstances in which the contravention took place; and\n(d) whether the person has previously been found by the Court in\nproceedings under this Act to have engaged in any similar\nconduct.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42y"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
