    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ya",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42YA What is a civil penalty provision?",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42ya"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.282",
      "values:originalText": "A subsection of this Act (or a section of this Act that is not divided\ninto subsections) is a civil penalty provision if the words “civil\npenalty” and one or more amounts in penalty units are set out at the\nfoot of the subsection (or section).",
      "skos:definition": "A subsection of this Act (or a section of this Act that is not divided\ninto subsections) is a civil penalty provision if the words “civil\npenalty” and one or more amounts in penalty units are set out at the\nfoot of the subsection (or section).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ya-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ya-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "440b0c533d29838f277721fc589819d7169a2f642ccccb75fd7e30736bb8e941",
      "skos:note": "Defines civil penalty provision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42ya",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42YA What is a civil penalty provision?",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 282,
      "values:originalText": "A subsection of this Act (or a section of this Act that is not divided\ninto subsections) is a civil penalty provision if the words “civil\npenalty” and one or more amounts in penalty units are set out at the\nfoot of the subsection (or section)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ya-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ya"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42ya-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "is defined as",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines a concept",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:conclusionText": "civil penalty provision"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yc",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42YC Persons involved in contravening civil penalty provision",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42yc"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.282",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not:\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of a civil\npenalty provision; or\n(b) induce (by threats, promises or otherwise) a contravention of\na civil penalty provision; or\n(c) conspire to contravene a civil penalty provision.\n(2) This Act applies to a person who contravenes subsection (1) in\nrelation to a civil penalty provision as if the person had\ncontravened the civil penalty provision.\n\nEnforcement  Chapter 5A\nCivil penalties  Part 5A-1\nObtaining an order for a civil penalty  Division 1\nSection 42YCA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n42YCA  Continuing contraventions of civil penalty provisions\n(1) If an act or thing is required under a civil penalty provision to be\ndone:\n(a) within a particular period; or\n(b) before a particular time;\nthen the obligation to do that act or thing continues until the act or\nthing is done (even if the period has expired or the time has\npassed).\n(2) A person who contravenes a civil penalty provision that requires an\nact or thing to be done:\n(a) within a particular period; or\n(b) before a particular time;\ncommits a separate contravention of that provision in respect of\neach day during which the contravention occurs (including the day\nthe order under subsection 42Y(2) is made or any later day).",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not:\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of a civil\npenalty provision; or\n(b) induce (by threats, promises or otherwise) a contravention of\na civil penalty provision; or\n(c) conspire to contravene a civil penalty provision.\n(2) This Act applies to a person who contravenes subsection (1) in\nrelation to a civil penalty provision as if the person had\ncontravened the civil penalty provision.\n\nEnforcement  Chapter 5A\nCivil penalties  Part 5A-1\nObtaining an order for a civil penalty  Division 1\nSection 42YCA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n42YCA  Continuing contraventions of civil penalty provisions\n(1) If an act or thing is required under a civil penalty provision to be\ndone:\n(a) within a particular period; or\n(b) before a particular time;\nthen the obligation to do that act or thing continues until the act or\nthing is done (even if the period has expired or the time has\npassed).\n(2) A person who contravenes a civil penalty provision that requires an\nact or thing to be done:\n(a) within a particular period; or\n(b) before a particular time;\ncommits a separate contravention of that provision in respect of\neach day during which the contravention occurs (including the day\nthe order under subsection 42Y(2) is made or any later day).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yc-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yc-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yc-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9b272aaa772afa9b77041f5010f6d970ec1ed32903a47bdc6a925fabf2c5788a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42yc",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42YC Persons involved in contravening civil penalty provision",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 282,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not:\n(a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of a civil\npenalty provision; or\n(b) induce (by threats, promises or otherwise) a contravention of\na civil penalty provision; or\n(c) conspire to contravene a civil penalty provision.\n(2) This Act applies to a person who contravenes subsection (1) in\nrelation to a civil penalty provision as if the person had\ncontravened the civil penalty provision.\n\nEnforcement  Chapter 5A\nCivil penalties  Part 5A-1\nObtaining an order for a civil penalty  Division 1\nSection 42YCA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n42YCA  Continuing contraventions of civil penalty provisions\n(1) If an act or thing is required under a civil penalty provision to be\ndone:\n(a) within a particular period; or\n(b) before a particular time;\nthen the obligation to do that act or thing continues until the act or\nthing is done (even if the period has expired or the time has\npassed).\n(2) A person who contravenes a civil penalty provision that requires an\nact or thing to be done:\n(a) within a particular period; or\n(b) before a particular time;\ncommits a separate contravention of that provision in respect of\neach day during which the contravention occurs (including the day\nthe order under subsection 42Y(2) is made or any later day)."
    },
