    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42YL(5) Enforcement of undertakings",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42yl-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.295",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Court is satisfied that the person has breached a term of the\nundertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n(a) an order directing the person to comply with that term of the\nundertaking;\n(b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the\nperson has obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the breach;\n(c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the\nperson to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n(d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If the Court is satisfied that the person has breached a term of the\nundertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n(a) an order directing the person to comply with that term of the\nundertaking;\n(b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the\nperson has obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the breach;\n(c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the\nperson to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n(d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da8a864732f059b045c128da653b95f49fe84883ee6e0a3a165a9fcbec844145",
      "skos:note": "Court may make orders to enforce undertaking breach"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42yl-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42YL(5) Enforcement of undertakings",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 295,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If the Court is satisfied that the person has breached a term of the\nundertaking, the Court may make all or any of the following\norders:\n(a) an order directing the person to comply with that term of the\nundertaking;\n(b) an order directing the person to pay to the Commonwealth an\namount up to the amount of any financial benefit that the\nperson has obtained directly or indirectly and that is\nreasonably attributable to the breach;\n(c) any order that the Court considers appropriate directing the\nperson to compensate any other person who has suffered loss\nor damage as a result of the breach;\n(d) any other order that the Court considers appropriate.\n\nChapter 5A  Enforcement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yl-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
