      "values:originalText": "(1) If a person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct in contravention of this Act or the regulations, the Federal\nCourt or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmay, on application by the Secretary, grant an injunction:\n(a) restraining the person from engaging in the conduct; and\n(b) if, in the court’s opinion, it is desirable to do so—requiring\nthe person to do a thing.\nPerformance injunctions",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a person has engaged, is engaging or is proposing to engage, in\nconduct in contravention of this Act or the regulations, the Federal\nCourt or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia (Division 2)\nmay, on application by the Secretary, grant an injunction:\n(a) restraining the person from engaging in the conduct; and\n(b) if, in the court’s opinion, it is desirable to do so—requiring\nthe person to do a thing.\nPerformance injunctions",
