    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yo",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "42YO Interim injunctions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42yo"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.297",
      "values:originalText": "Grant of interim injunctions\n(1) Before deciding an application for an injunction under\nsection 42YN, the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2) may grant an interim injunction:\n(a) restraining a person from engaging in conduct; or\n(b) requiring a person to do a thing.\nNo undertakings as to damages\n(2) The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) must not require the Secretary to give an undertaking\nas to damages as a condition of granting an interim injunction.",
      "skos:definition": "Grant of interim injunctions\n(1) Before deciding an application for an injunction under\nsection 42YN, the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2) may grant an interim injunction:\n(a) restraining a person from engaging in conduct; or\n(b) requiring a person to do a thing.\nNo undertakings as to damages\n(2) The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) must not require the Secretary to give an undertaking\nas to damages as a condition of granting an interim injunction.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yo-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-42yo-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f4949595625000bdae8f6ffe6c4c76b3a8b946481c3fe5058026fcac4fb69cd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-42yo",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "42YO Interim injunctions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 297,
      "values:originalText": "Grant of interim injunctions\n(1) Before deciding an application for an injunction under\nsection 42YN, the Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family\nCourt of Australia (Division 2) may grant an interim injunction:\n(a) restraining a person from engaging in conduct; or\n(b) requiring a person to do a thing.\nNo undertakings as to damages\n(2) The Federal Court or Federal Circuit and Family Court of Australia\n(Division 2) must not require the Secretary to give an undertaking\nas to damages as a condition of granting an interim injunction."
    },
