    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44 Time for payment of charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.301",
      "values:originalText": "Annual registration charge, annual listing charge or annual\ncharge for inclusion in the Register\n(1) An annual registration charge, annual listing charge or annual\ncharge for inclusion in the Register for a financial year becomes\npayable:\n(a) if the registration, listing or inclusion in the Register of the\ntherapeutic goods concerned commenced in that financial\nyear—on the day worked out under the regulations; and\n(b) in any other case:\n(i) on 1 October in that year; or\n(ii) if the regulations specify another day for the purposes of\nthis subparagraph—on that other day in that year.\nThis subsection is subject to subsection (3).\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "Annual registration charge, annual listing charge or annual\ncharge for inclusion in the Register\n(1) An annual registration charge, annual listing charge or annual\ncharge for inclusion in the Register for a financial year becomes\npayable:\n(a) if the registration, listing or inclusion in the Register of the\ntherapeutic goods concerned commenced in that financial\nyear—on the day worked out under the regulations; and\n(b) in any other case:\n(i) on 1 October in that year; or\n(ii) if the regulations specify another day for the purposes of\nthis subparagraph—on that other day in that year.\nThis subsection is subject to subsection (3).\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "977e3c9571f343d532a7a03ac9b32e1423abf755ab774feecd0a43a7ac706d67",
      "skos:note": "Annual registration charge becomes payable on a specific date."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44 Time for payment of charges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 301,
      "values:originalText": "Annual registration charge, annual listing charge or annual\ncharge for inclusion in the Register\n(1) An annual registration charge, annual listing charge or annual\ncharge for inclusion in the Register for a financial year becomes\npayable:\n(a) if the registration, listing or inclusion in the Register of the\ntherapeutic goods concerned commenced in that financial\nyear—on the day worked out under the regulations; and\n(b) in any other case:\n(i) on 1 October in that year; or\n(ii) if the regulations specify another day for the purposes of\nthis subparagraph—on that other day in that year.\nThis subsection is subject to subsection (3).\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44A Exemptions from liability to pay charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.302",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to:\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nPayment of charges  Part 6-1\n\nSection 44A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) exempting a person from liability to pay annual registration\ncharge, annual listing charge or annual charge for inclusion\nin the Register for a financial year (the current year) if the\nperson’s turnover of the therapeutic goods concerned for the\nfinancial year specified in the regulations is of low value; and\n(b) the making of an application for an exemption and requiring\npayment of that charge for the current year if the application\nis refused; and\n(c) cancelling an exemption and requiring payment of that\ncharge for the current year.\nFees\n(2) The regulations may require applications for exemptions to be\naccompanied by a specified fee. A fee must not be such as to\namount to taxation.\nStatements prepared by approved persons\n(3) The regulations may require a person who is applying for an\nexemption, or who has been granted an exemption, to provide a\nstatement:\n(a) that is prepared by an approved person; and\n(b) that specifies whether the person’s turnover of the therapeutic\ngoods concerned for the financial year concerned is of low\nvalue.\nAdditional information\n(4) The regulations may provide for the obtaining of additional\ninformation or documents from applicants for exemptions or\npersons granted exemptions.\nMerits review\n(5) The regulations may provide for review by the Administrative\nReview Tribunal of decisions of the Secretary to refuse\napplications for exemptions or to cancel exemptions.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to:\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nPayment of charges  Part 6-1\n\nSection 44A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) exempting a person from liability to pay annual registration\ncharge, annual listing charge or annual charge for inclusion\nin the Register for a financial year (the current year) if the\nperson’s turnover of the therapeutic goods concerned for the\nfinancial year specified in the regulations is of low value; and\n(b) the making of an application for an exemption and requiring\npayment of that charge for the current year if the application\nis refused; and\n(c) cancelling an exemption and requiring payment of that\ncharge for the current year.\nFees\n(2) The regulations may require applications for exemptions to be\naccompanied by a specified fee. A fee must not be such as to\namount to taxation.\nStatements prepared by approved persons\n(3) The regulations may require a person who is applying for an\nexemption, or who has been granted an exemption, to provide a\nstatement:\n(a) that is prepared by an approved person; and\n(b) that specifies whether the person’s turnover of the therapeutic\ngoods concerned for the financial year concerned is of low\nvalue.\nAdditional information\n(4) The regulations may provide for the obtaining of additional\ninformation or documents from applicants for exemptions or\npersons granted exemptions.\nMerits review\n(5) The regulations may provide for review by the Administrative\nReview Tribunal of decisions of the Secretary to refuse\napplications for exemptions or to cancel exemptions.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e6a4a7f71c2371dceb80b98daeb837fdffc7f5142bb2de5a7673977354f1b2c3"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44A Exemptions from liability to pay charges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 302,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The regulations may make provision for and in relation to:\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nPayment of charges  Part 6-1\n\nSection 44A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) exempting a person from liability to pay annual registration\ncharge, annual listing charge or annual charge for inclusion\nin the Register for a financial year (the current year) if the\nperson’s turnover of the therapeutic goods concerned for the\nfinancial year specified in the regulations is of low value; and\n(b) the making of an application for an exemption and requiring\npayment of that charge for the current year if the application\nis refused; and\n(c) cancelling an exemption and requiring payment of that\ncharge for the current year.\nFees\n(2) The regulations may require applications for exemptions to be\naccompanied by a specified fee. A fee must not be such as to\namount to taxation.\nStatements prepared by approved persons\n(3) The regulations may require a person who is applying for an\nexemption, or who has been granted an exemption, to provide a\nstatement:\n(a) that is prepared by an approved person; and\n(b) that specifies whether the person’s turnover of the therapeutic\ngoods concerned for the financial year concerned is of low\nvalue.\nAdditional information\n(4) The regulations may provide for the obtaining of additional\ninformation or documents from applicants for exemptions or\npersons granted exemptions.\nMerits review\n(5) The regulations may provide for review by the Administrative\nReview Tribunal of decisions of the Secretary to refuse\napplications for exemptions or to cancel exemptions.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44A(1) Exemptions from liability to pay charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44a-ss-1"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
