    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44A(3) Exemptions from liability to pay charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44a-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.302",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The regulations may require a person who is applying for an\nexemption, or who has been granted an exemption, to provide a\nstatement:\n(a) that is prepared by an approved person; and\n(b) that specifies whether the person’s turnover of the therapeutic\ngoods concerned for the financial year concerned is of low\nvalue.\nAdditional information",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The regulations may require a person who is applying for an\nexemption, or who has been granted an exemption, to provide a\nstatement:\n(a) that is prepared by an approved person; and\n(b) that specifies whether the person’s turnover of the therapeutic\ngoods concerned for the financial year concerned is of low\nvalue.\nAdditional information",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
