    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "44B Recovery of unpaid charges",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.304",
      "values:originalText": "An amount of an annual registration charge, an annual listing\ncharge, an annual charge for inclusion in the Register, an annual\nlicensing charge or an annual conformity assessment body\ndetermination charge that remains unpaid at the end of the period\nof 28 days after the day on which the charge becomes payable may\nbe recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt due to the\nCommonwealth.\nNote:\nSection 44 sets out the day on which a charge becomes payable.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nPayment of charges  Part 6-1\n\nSection 45\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "An amount of an annual registration charge, an annual listing\ncharge, an annual charge for inclusion in the Register, an annual\nlicensing charge or an annual conformity assessment body\ndetermination charge that remains unpaid at the end of the period\nof 28 days after the day on which the charge becomes payable may\nbe recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt due to the\nCommonwealth.\nNote:\nSection 44 sets out the day on which a charge becomes payable.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nPayment of charges  Part 6-1\n\nSection 45\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44b-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44b-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "31ba6f81b31f77db1c377a455200e1a54ae84bcc24c97f128af4bac6e07bf0c9",
      "skos:note": "Recovery of unpaid charges after 28 days"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-44b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "44B Recovery of unpaid charges",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 304,
      "values:originalText": "An amount of an annual registration charge, an annual listing\ncharge, an annual charge for inclusion in the Register, an annual\nlicensing charge or an annual conformity assessment body\ndetermination charge that remains unpaid at the end of the period\nof 28 days after the day on which the charge becomes payable may\nbe recovered by the Commonwealth as a debt due to the\nCommonwealth.\nNote:\nSection 44 sets out the day on which a charge becomes payable.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nPayment of charges  Part 6-1\n\nSection 45\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44b-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44b"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-44b-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to recover unpaid charges",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Charge becomes payable after 28 days",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Recovery of charge due to Commonwealth"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45 Therapeutic Goods Administration Account",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.305",
      "values:originalText": "(1) There is continued in existence the Therapeutic Goods\nAdministration Account.\nNote:\nThe Account was established by subsection 5(3) of the Financial\nManagement Legislation Amendment Act 1999.\n(2) The Account is a special account for the purposes of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\n(3) There must be credited to the Account amounts equal to:\n(a) amounts received by the Commonwealth by way of annual\nregistration charge, annual listing charge, annual charge for\ninclusion in the Register, annual licensing charge and annual\nconformity assessment body determination charge; and\n(b) interest received by the Commonwealth from the investment\nof an amount standing to the credit of the Account; and\n(c) money received by the Commonwealth in relation to property\npaid for after a debit from the Account; and\n(d) money received by the Commonwealth for services provided\nor to be provided, by or on behalf of the Commonwealth,\nusing amounts standing to the credit of the Account\n(including amounts received by way of fees payable under\nthe regulations); and\n(e) donations for the furtherance of a purpose of the Account that\nare received by the Commonwealth; and\n(f) receipts relating to the recovery of debts (other than debts in\nrespect of statutory fines and penalties) by the\nCommonwealth that are associated with expenditure of an\namount standing to the credit of the Account.\nNote:\nAn Appropriation Act provides for amounts to be credited to a special\naccount if any of the purposes of the special account is a purpose that\nis covered by an item in the Appropriation Act.\n(4) The purposes of the Account are to make payments:\n(a) to further the objects of this Act (as set out in section 4); and\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) There is continued in existence the Therapeutic Goods\nAdministration Account.\nNote:\nThe Account was established by subsection 5(3) of the Financial\nManagement Legislation Amendment Act 1999.\n(2) The Account is a special account for the purposes of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\n(3) There must be credited to the Account amounts equal to:\n(a) amounts received by the Commonwealth by way of annual\nregistration charge, annual listing charge, annual charge for\ninclusion in the Register, annual licensing charge and annual\nconformity assessment body determination charge; and\n(b) interest received by the Commonwealth from the investment\nof an amount standing to the credit of the Account; and\n(c) money received by the Commonwealth in relation to property\npaid for after a debit from the Account; and\n(d) money received by the Commonwealth for services provided\nor to be provided, by or on behalf of the Commonwealth,\nusing amounts standing to the credit of the Account\n(including amounts received by way of fees payable under\nthe regulations); and\n(e) donations for the furtherance of a purpose of the Account that\nare received by the Commonwealth; and\n(f) receipts relating to the recovery of debts (other than debts in\nrespect of statutory fines and penalties) by the\nCommonwealth that are associated with expenditure of an\namount standing to the credit of the Account.\nNote:\nAn Appropriation Act provides for amounts to be credited to a special\naccount if any of the purposes of the special account is a purpose that\nis covered by an item in the Appropriation Act.\n(4) The purposes of the Account are to make payments:\n(a) to further the objects of this Act (as set out in section 4); and\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1855d5af7f5961b4a7cb20242e36e1a58407de7e61107c819ff5b34c907a8214"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 Therapeutic Goods Administration Account",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 305,
      "values:originalText": "(1) There is continued in existence the Therapeutic Goods\nAdministration Account.\nNote:\nThe Account was established by subsection 5(3) of the Financial\nManagement Legislation Amendment Act 1999.\n(2) The Account is a special account for the purposes of the Public\nGovernance, Performance and Accountability Act 2013.\n(3) There must be credited to the Account amounts equal to:\n(a) amounts received by the Commonwealth by way of annual\nregistration charge, annual listing charge, annual charge for\ninclusion in the Register, annual licensing charge and annual\nconformity assessment body determination charge; and\n(b) interest received by the Commonwealth from the investment\nof an amount standing to the credit of the Account; and\n(c) money received by the Commonwealth in relation to property\npaid for after a debit from the Account; and\n(d) money received by the Commonwealth for services provided\nor to be provided, by or on behalf of the Commonwealth,\nusing amounts standing to the credit of the Account\n(including amounts received by way of fees payable under\nthe regulations); and\n(e) donations for the furtherance of a purpose of the Account that\nare received by the Commonwealth; and\n(f) receipts relating to the recovery of debts (other than debts in\nrespect of statutory fines and penalties) by the\nCommonwealth that are associated with expenditure of an\namount standing to the credit of the Account.\nNote:\nAn Appropriation Act provides for amounts to be credited to a special\naccount if any of the purposes of the special account is a purpose that\nis covered by an item in the Appropriation Act.\n(4) The purposes of the Account are to make payments:\n(a) to further the objects of this Act (as set out in section 4); and\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
