    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ab",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AB Secretary may require information or documents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45ab"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.308",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to a person, require the\nperson to give to the Secretary any information, or produce to the\nSecretary any documents, specified in the notice that are relevant\nto a contravention, or possible contravention, of a provision of this\nAct or the regulations.\n(2) The notice must specify a reasonable period within which the\nperson must comply with the notice. The period must be at least 14\ndays starting on the day on which the notice is given.\n(3) The notice must set out the effect of the following:\n(a) section 45AC (about failure to comply with notice);\n(b) section 45AD (about giving false or misleading information\nor documents);\n(c) section 137.1 of the Criminal Code (about giving false or\nmisleading information);\n(d) section 137.2 of the Criminal Code (about producing false or\nmisleading documents).\n(4) The notice may require the information to be given, or the\ndocuments to be produced, in accordance with specified software\nrequirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may, by written notice given to a person, require the\nperson to give to the Secretary any information, or produce to the\nSecretary any documents, specified in the notice that are relevant\nto a contravention, or possible contravention, of a provision of this\nAct or the regulations.\n(2) The notice must specify a reasonable period within which the\nperson must comply with the notice. The period must be at least 14\ndays starting on the day on which the notice is given.\n(3) The notice must set out the effect of the following:\n(a) section 45AC (about failure to comply with notice);\n(b) section 45AD (about giving false or misleading information\nor documents);\n(c) section 137.1 of the Criminal Code (about giving false or\nmisleading information);\n(d) section 137.2 of the Criminal Code (about producing false or\nmisleading documents).\n(4) The notice may require the information to be given, or the\ndocuments to be produced, in accordance with specified software\nrequirements:\n(a) on a specified kind of data processing device; or\n(b) by way of a specified kind of electronic transmission.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ab-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ab-ss-2"
