      "cml:operator": "Prohibition",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prevents admissibility of self-incriminating information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) However: ...; (d) subsection 45AC(1) or (2); or (e) subsection 45AD(1) or (2); or (f) section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:conclusionText": "... not admissible in evidence against the individual in criminal proceedings other than proceedings for an offence against Administration Chapter 6 Information gathering powers Part 6-1A Obtaining information or documents Division 2 Section 45AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permission",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Allows for exceptions to the prohibition on self-incrimination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(f) section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code in relation to giving the information or producing the document.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "... proceedings for an offence against Administration Chapter 6 Information gathering powers Part 6-1A Obtaining information or documents Division 2 Section 45AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the temporal scope of admissible evidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) However: ...; (d) subsection 45AC(1) or (2); or (e) subsection 45AD(1) or (2); or (f) section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:conclusionText": "... criminal proceedings other than proceedings for an offence against Administration Chapter 6 Information gathering powers Part 6-1A Obtaining information or documents Division 2 Section 45AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-2-logic-ltl-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Repeats",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the repetition of admissible evidence",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) the information given or document produced; and (b) the giving of the information or the production of the document;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "... criminal proceedings other than proceedings for an offence against Administration Chapter 6 Information gathering powers Part 6-1A Obtaining information or documents Division 2 Section 45AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-2-logic-deontic-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Establishes the duty to protect against self-incrimination",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) However: ...; (d) subsection 45AC(1) or (2); or (e) subsection 45AD(1) or (2); or (f) section 137.1 or 137.2 of the Criminal Code",
      "cml:conclusionText": "... against the individual in criminal proceedings other than proceedings for an offence against Administration Chapter 6 Information gathering powers Part 6-1A Obtaining information or documents Division 2 Section 45AE Therapeutic Goods Act 1989"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45AE(3) Self-incrimination",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45ae-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.310",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, at general law, an individual would otherwise be able to claim\nthe privilege against self-exposure to a penalty (other than a\npenalty for an offence) in relation to giving information or\nproducing a document under section 45AB, the individual is not\nexcused from giving the information or producing the document\nunder that provision on that ground.\nNote:\nA body corporate is not entitled to claim the privilege against\nself-exposure to a penalty.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If, at general law, an individual would otherwise be able to claim\nthe privilege against self-exposure to a penalty (other than a\npenalty for an offence) in relation to giving information or\nproducing a document under section 45AB, the individual is not\nexcused from giving the information or producing the document\nunder that provision on that ground.\nNote:\nA body corporate is not entitled to claim the privilege against\nself-exposure to a penalty.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7b417cc1d1b4bc644dfa9afbd6631b274f9f46e48c75c699f377bf8c7147f3db",
      "skos:note": "No claim of privilege against self-exposure to penalty for giving information or producing document under section 45AB."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45ae-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45AE(3) Self-incrimination",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 310,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If, at general law, an individual would otherwise be able to claim\nthe privilege against self-exposure to a penalty (other than a\npenalty for an offence) in relation to giving information or\nproducing a document under section 45AB, the individual is not\nexcused from giving the information or producing the document\nunder that provision on that ground.\nNote:\nA body corporate is not entitled to claim the privilege against\nself-exposure to a penalty.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45ae-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
