    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45A Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.313",
      "values:originalText": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\nevidential material means:\n(a) in respect of an offence against this Act:\n(i) any thing with respect to which the offence has been\ncommitted or is suspected, on reasonable grounds, to\nhave been committed; or\n(ii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it will afford evidence as to the\ncommission of the offence; or\n(iii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it is intended to be used for the purpose\nof committing the offence; and\n(b) in respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision:\n(i) any thing with respect to which the civil penalty\nprovision has been contravened or is suspected, on\nreasonable grounds, of having been contravened; or\n(ii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it will afford evidence as to the\ncontravention of the civil penalty provision; or\n(iii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it is intended to be used for the purpose\nof contravening the civil penalty provision.\noccupier, in relation to premises, includes a person present at the\npremises who is in apparent control of the premises.\nperson assisting, in relation to an authorised person: see\nsubsection 48AAA(2).\nseize includes secure against interference.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\nevidential material means:\n(a) in respect of an offence against this Act:\n(i) any thing with respect to which the offence has been\ncommitted or is suspected, on reasonable grounds, to\nhave been committed; or\n(ii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it will afford evidence as to the\ncommission of the offence; or\n(iii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it is intended to be used for the purpose\nof committing the offence; and\n(b) in respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision:\n(i) any thing with respect to which the civil penalty\nprovision has been contravened or is suspected, on\nreasonable grounds, of having been contravened; or\n(ii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it will afford evidence as to the\ncontravention of the civil penalty provision; or\n(iii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it is intended to be used for the purpose\nof contravening the civil penalty provision.\noccupier, in relation to premises, includes a person present at the\npremises who is in apparent control of the premises.\nperson assisting, in relation to an authorised person: see\nsubsection 48AAA(2).\nseize includes secure against interference.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45a-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-45a-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6e89edc95cfd7fdad23a161d98a6056cd34fa9b0b57b55e9f685a34b5dc4b3d4",
      "skos:note": "Defines evidential material and occupier for this Part."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-45a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45A Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 313,
      "values:originalText": "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\nevidential material means:\n(a) in respect of an offence against this Act:\n(i) any thing with respect to which the offence has been\ncommitted or is suspected, on reasonable grounds, to\nhave been committed; or\n(ii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it will afford evidence as to the\ncommission of the offence; or\n(iii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it is intended to be used for the purpose\nof committing the offence; and\n(b) in respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision:\n(i) any thing with respect to which the civil penalty\nprovision has been contravened or is suspected, on\nreasonable grounds, of having been contravened; or\n(ii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it will afford evidence as to the\ncontravention of the civil penalty provision; or\n(iii) any thing as to which there are reasonable grounds for\nsuspecting that it is intended to be used for the purpose\nof contravening the civil penalty provision.\noccupier, in relation to premises, includes a person present at the\npremises who is in apparent control of the premises.\nperson assisting, in relation to an authorised person: see\nsubsection 48AAA(2).\nseize includes secure against interference.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
