        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Searches to monitor compliance with Act or regulations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.314",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), an authorised person may, for\nthe purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations have\nbeen complied with:\n(a) enter any premises; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection 48(1) and\nsection 48BA.\n(2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 49.\n(3) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised\nperson to produce his or her identity card for inspection by\nthe occupier; and\n(b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), an authorised person may, for\nthe purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations have\nbeen complied with:\n(a) enter any premises; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection 48(1) and\nsection 48BA.\n(2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 49.\n(3) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised\nperson to produce his or her identity card for inspection by\nthe occupier; and\n(b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6ba97533934ea0266b6699062ad9ea819bba637d1ced3cd01851ecc73309f77c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Searches to monitor compliance with Act or regulations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 314,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), an authorised person may, for\nthe purpose of finding out whether this Act or the regulations have\nbeen complied with:\n(a) enter any premises; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection 48(1) and\nsection 48BA.\n(2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 49.\n(3) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised\nperson to produce his or her identity card for inspection by\nthe occupier; and\n(b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement."
    },
