      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 316,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if an authorised person has reasonable\ngrounds for suspecting that:\n(a) there may be on any premises a particular thing in respect of\nwhich this Act or the regulations have not been complied\nwith; and\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 47\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) it is necessary in the interests of public health to exercise\npowers under this section in order to avoid an imminent risk\nof death, serious illness or serious injury;\nthe authorised person may, to the extent that it is reasonably\nnecessary for the purpose of avoiding an imminent risk of death,\nserious illness or serious injury, enter the premises and do any of\nthe following:\n(c) search the premises for the thing;\n(d) if the authorised person finds the thing on the premises—\nseize it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition on entering premises.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) there may be on any premises a particular thing in respect of which this Act or the regulations have not been complied",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorised person may not enter the premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Temporal Interval",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Temporal interval for exercising powers under this section.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) search the premises for the thing;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorised person may enter the premises within a reasonable time frame to search for the item."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Recurring Trace",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Recurring trace of searches and seizures on public health grounds.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(d) if the authorised person finds the thing on the premises—seize it;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorised person may seize the item repeatedly within a reasonable time frame."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to exercise powers under this section in certain circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) it is necessary in the interests of public health to exercise powers under this section in order to avoid an imminent risk of death, serious illness or serious injury;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorised person has an obligation to exercise their powers if there is a risk to public health."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-1-logic-argumentation-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Inference",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Inference from the text that the authorised person may enter premises and seize items under certain circumstances.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) there may be on any premises a particular thing in respect of which this Act or the regulations have not been complied (b) it is necessary in the interests of public health to exercise powers under this section in order to avoid an imminent risk of death, serious illness or serious injury;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The authorised person may enter premises and seize items if there is a risk to public health."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46B(2) Searches and seizures on public health grounds",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-46b-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.316",
      "values:originalText": "(2) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised\nperson to produce his or her identity card for inspection by\nthe occupier; and\n(b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised\nperson to produce his or her identity card for inspection by\nthe occupier; and\n(b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b93def83a19431a61d68cf2dfb4e1adeb4fd3c5337537f238ca4dec482d9591a",
      "skos:note": "Authorized person cannot exercise powers under subsection (1) in relation to premises if occupier requires identity card inspection."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-46b-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46B(2) Searches and seizures on public health grounds",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 316,
      "values:originalText": "(2) An authorised person is not entitled to exercise any powers under\nsubsection (1) in relation to premises if:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has required the authorised\nperson to produce his or her identity card for inspection by\nthe occupier; and\n(b) the authorised person fails to comply with the requirement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-2-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-46b-ss-2"
