      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-47",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47 Searches and seizures related to offences and civil penalty",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-47"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.317",
      "values:originalText": "provisions\n(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), if an authorised person has\nreasonable grounds for suspecting that there may be evidential\nmaterial in respect of an offence against this Act, in respect of a\ncontravention of a civil penalty provision or in respect of both on\nany premises, the authorised person may:\n(a) enter the premises; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection (4),\nsubsection 48(1) and section 48C; and\n(c) if the authorised person finds the thing on the premises—\nseize it.\n(2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 50.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "provisions\n(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), if an authorised person has\nreasonable grounds for suspecting that there may be evidential\nmaterial in respect of an offence against this Act, in respect of a\ncontravention of a civil penalty provision or in respect of both on\nany premises, the authorised person may:\n(a) enter the premises; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection (4),\nsubsection 48(1) and section 48C; and\n(c) if the authorised person finds the thing on the premises—\nseize it.\n(2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 50.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-47-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-47-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "59216e616e82741c8a6f6cd8707084e74bd8aacfdfd30fa506e233e17992700f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-47",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "47 Searches and seizures related to offences and civil penalty",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 317,
      "values:originalText": "provisions\n(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), if an authorised person has\nreasonable grounds for suspecting that there may be evidential\nmaterial in respect of an offence against this Act, in respect of a\ncontravention of a civil penalty provision or in respect of both on\nany premises, the authorised person may:\n(a) enter the premises; and\n(b) exercise the powers set out in subsection (4),\nsubsection 48(1) and section 48C; and\n(c) if the authorised person finds the thing on the premises—\nseize it.\n(2) The authorised person must not enter the premises unless:\n(a) the occupier of the premises has consented to the entry; or\n(b) the entry is made under a warrant issued under section 50.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-47-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "47(1) Searches and seizures related to offences and civil penalty",
