    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48ba-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48BA(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises for monitoring",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 322,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the authorised person believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) information relevant to determining whether this Act or the\nregulations have been complied with may be accessible by\noperating electronic equipment at the premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\ninformation may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48ba-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
