    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48C(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises relating to offences and",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48c-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.324",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the authorised person believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) evidential material in respect of an offence against this Act,\nin respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision or in\nrespect of both may be accessible by operating electronic\nequipment at the premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If the authorised person believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) evidential material in respect of an offence against this Act,\nin respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision or in\nrespect of both may be accessible by operating electronic\nequipment at the premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48c-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "752409f0bfc34fddb81506cee9e8803349c9680e9a7cc0c46570c64284085f8d",
      "skos:note": "Authorized person may take necessary actions to secure electronic equipment."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48c-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48C(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises relating to offences and",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 324,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the authorised person believes on reasonable grounds that:\n(a) evidential material in respect of an offence against this Act,\nin respect of a contravention of a civil penalty provision or in\nrespect of both may be accessible by operating electronic\nequipment at the premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise."
    },
