    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48D Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48d"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.326",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) damage is caused to equipment as a result of it being\noperated as mentioned in section 48BA or 48C; and\n(b) the damage was caused as a result of:\n(i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the equipment; or\n(ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating\nthe equipment;\ncompensation for the damage is payable to the owner of the\nequipment.\n(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament for the purpose.\n(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the\nequipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) damage is caused to equipment as a result of it being\noperated as mentioned in section 48BA or 48C; and\n(b) the damage was caused as a result of:\n(i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the equipment; or\n(ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating\nthe equipment;\ncompensation for the damage is payable to the owner of the\nequipment.\n(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament for the purpose.\n(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the\nequipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5d20c860749de208b03d195857138e0322d3061dc56ce75ddc31269467d7887b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48d",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48D Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 326,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) damage is caused to equipment as a result of it being\noperated as mentioned in section 48BA or 48C; and\n(b) the damage was caused as a result of:\n(i) insufficient care being exercised in selecting the person\nwho was to operate the equipment; or\n(ii) insufficient care being exercised by the person operating\nthe equipment;\ncompensation for the damage is payable to the owner of the\nequipment.\n(2) Compensation is payable out of money appropriated by the\nParliament for the purpose.\n(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the\nequipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
