      "skos:prefLabel": "48D(3) Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48d-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.326",
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the\nequipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the\nequipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "07285c55838625e1b42c8cf82ca617a278754a10968f319e06b6f8ef0e0243e6",
      "skos:note": "Occupier must provide warning or guidance about equipment operation.",
      "dc:description": "warning or guidance"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48d-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48D(3) Compensation for damage to electronic equipment",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 326,
      "values:originalText": "(3) In determining the amount of compensation payable, regard is to\nbe had to whether the occupier of the premises and his or her\nemployees and agents, if they were available at the time, had\nprovided any warning or guidance as to the operation of the\nequipment that was appropriate in the circumstances.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48E\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48d-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
