    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48e",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48E Copies of seized things to be provided",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48e"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.327",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if an authorised person seizes, under a\nwarrant relating to premises:\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe authorised person must, if requested to do so by the occupier of\nthe premises or another person who apparently represents the\noccupier and who is present when the warrant is executed, give a\ncopy of the thing or the information to that person as soon as\npracticable after the seizure.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if possession of the document, film,\ncomputer file, thing or information by the occupier could constitute\nan offence against a law of the Commonwealth or contravention of\na civil penalty provision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if an authorised person seizes, under a\nwarrant relating to premises:\n(a) a document, film, computer file or other thing that can be\nreadily copied; or\n(b) a storage device the information in which can be readily\ncopied;\nthe authorised person must, if requested to do so by the occupier of\nthe premises or another person who apparently represents the\noccupier and who is present when the warrant is executed, give a\ncopy of the thing or the information to that person as soon as\npracticable after the seizure.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply if possession of the document, film,\ncomputer file, thing or information by the occupier could constitute\nan offence against a law of the Commonwealth or contravention of\na civil penalty provision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48e-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48e-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0376d86dc0c9de93b5a86fa3e34ca43a7b0ba265c33237cb3084b2deb134b299"
    },
    {
