    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48H(2) Retention of seized things",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48h-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.328",
      "values:originalText": "(2) At the end of the 120 days specified in subsection (1), an\nauthorised person must take reasonable steps to return the thing to\nthe person from whom it was seized, unless:\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 120 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n(b) an authorised person may retain the thing because of an order\nunder section 48J; or\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48J\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) an authorised person is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an\norder of a court, of the Commonwealth or of a State or\nTerritory) to retain, destroy or dispose of the thing.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) At the end of the 120 days specified in subsection (1), an\nauthorised person must take reasonable steps to return the thing to\nthe person from whom it was seized, unless:\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 120 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n(b) an authorised person may retain the thing because of an order\nunder section 48J; or\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48J\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) an authorised person is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an\norder of a court, of the Commonwealth or of a State or\nTerritory) to retain, destroy or dispose of the thing.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48h-ss-2-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5a2e5a793ce063adb2ba630fd8c1b930a8880a3249e2c8702b6d3fdafeffe6a9",
      "skos:note": "Return seized things after 120 days unless proceedings are ongoing or authorized by law."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48h-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48H(2) Retention of seized things",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 328,
      "values:originalText": "(2) At the end of the 120 days specified in subsection (1), an\nauthorised person must take reasonable steps to return the thing to\nthe person from whom it was seized, unless:\n(a) proceedings in respect of which the thing may afford\nevidence were instituted before the end of the 120 days and\nhave not been completed (including an appeal to a court in\nrelation to those proceedings); or\n(b) an authorised person may retain the thing because of an order\nunder section 48J; or\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 48J\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(c) an authorised person is otherwise authorised (by a law, or an\norder of a court, of the Commonwealth or of a State or\nTerritory) to retain, destroy or dispose of the thing."
    },
