    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48J Issuing officer may permit a thing to be retained",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48j"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.329",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised person may apply to an issuing officer for an order\nthat he or she may retain the thing for a further period if:\n(a) before the end of 120 days after the seizure; or\n(b) before the end of a period previously specified in an order of\nan issuing officer under this section;\nproceedings in respect of which the thing may afford evidence\nhave not commenced.\n(2) If the issuing officer is satisfied that it is necessary for an\nauthorised person to continue to retain the thing:\n(a) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether an offence\nagainst this Act has been committed; or\n(b) to enable evidence of an offence against this Act to be\nsecured for the purposes of a prosecution; or\n(c) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether a civil\npenalty provision has been contravened; or\n(d) to enable evidence of a contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision to be secured for the purposes of civil proceedings;\nthe issuing officer may order that an authorised person may retain\nthe thing for a period (not being a period exceeding 3 years)\nspecified in the order.\n(3) Before making the application, the authorised person must:\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nretention of the thing; and\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authorised person may apply to an issuing officer for an order\nthat he or she may retain the thing for a further period if:\n(a) before the end of 120 days after the seizure; or\n(b) before the end of a period previously specified in an order of\nan issuing officer under this section;\nproceedings in respect of which the thing may afford evidence\nhave not commenced.\n(2) If the issuing officer is satisfied that it is necessary for an\nauthorised person to continue to retain the thing:\n(a) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether an offence\nagainst this Act has been committed; or\n(b) to enable evidence of an offence against this Act to be\nsecured for the purposes of a prosecution; or\n(c) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether a civil\npenalty provision has been contravened; or\n(d) to enable evidence of a contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision to be secured for the purposes of civil proceedings;\nthe issuing officer may order that an authorised person may retain\nthe thing for a period (not being a period exceeding 3 years)\nspecified in the order.\n(3) Before making the application, the authorised person must:\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nretention of the thing; and\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5fe0e954b49b5aef392692e5c4a71733b91d302d9ff248a8fe5958504848bd8c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48j",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48J Issuing officer may permit a thing to be retained",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 329,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised person may apply to an issuing officer for an order\nthat he or she may retain the thing for a further period if:\n(a) before the end of 120 days after the seizure; or\n(b) before the end of a period previously specified in an order of\nan issuing officer under this section;\nproceedings in respect of which the thing may afford evidence\nhave not commenced.\n(2) If the issuing officer is satisfied that it is necessary for an\nauthorised person to continue to retain the thing:\n(a) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether an offence\nagainst this Act has been committed; or\n(b) to enable evidence of an offence against this Act to be\nsecured for the purposes of a prosecution; or\n(c) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether a civil\npenalty provision has been contravened; or\n(d) to enable evidence of a contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision to be secured for the purposes of civil proceedings;\nthe issuing officer may order that an authorised person may retain\nthe thing for a period (not being a period exceeding 3 years)\nspecified in the order.\n(3) Before making the application, the authorised person must:\n(a) take reasonable steps to discover who has an interest in the\nretention of the thing; and\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
