      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Issuing officer may permit a thing to be retained",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Thing may be retained for a further period"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48J(2) Issuing officer may permit a thing to be retained",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48j-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.329",
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the issuing officer is satisfied that it is necessary for an\nauthorised person to continue to retain the thing:\n(a) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether an offence\nagainst this Act has been committed; or\n(b) to enable evidence of an offence against this Act to be\nsecured for the purposes of a prosecution; or\n(c) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether a civil\npenalty provision has been contravened; or\n(d) to enable evidence of a contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision to be secured for the purposes of civil proceedings;\nthe issuing officer may order that an authorised person may retain\nthe thing for a period (not being a period exceeding 3 years)\nspecified in the order.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) If the issuing officer is satisfied that it is necessary for an\nauthorised person to continue to retain the thing:\n(a) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether an offence\nagainst this Act has been committed; or\n(b) to enable evidence of an offence against this Act to be\nsecured for the purposes of a prosecution; or\n(c) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether a civil\npenalty provision has been contravened; or\n(d) to enable evidence of a contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision to be secured for the purposes of civil proceedings;\nthe issuing officer may order that an authorised person may retain\nthe thing for a period (not being a period exceeding 3 years)\nspecified in the order.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-48j-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fcfb9103cd38c950c8fe9e173203d968ec8173d56742dab5cd05a4157e74e0e4",
      "skos:note": "Issuing officer may permit an authorised person to retain a thing for a specified period."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-48j-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48J(2) Issuing officer may permit a thing to be retained",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 329,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the issuing officer is satisfied that it is necessary for an\nauthorised person to continue to retain the thing:\n(a) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether an offence\nagainst this Act has been committed; or\n(b) to enable evidence of an offence against this Act to be\nsecured for the purposes of a prosecution; or\n(c) for the purposes of an investigation as to whether a civil\npenalty provision has been contravened; or\n(d) to enable evidence of a contravention of a civil penalty\nprovision to be secured for the purposes of civil proceedings;\nthe issuing officer may order that an authorised person may retain\nthe thing for a period (not being a period exceeding 3 years)\nspecified in the order."
    },
