      "cml:integrityHash": "c263d42fb402c3841e33eb8fe5df87f8c0ce4af29db90b714bb0c1f69e0e860f",
      "skos:note": "Issuing officer must provide further information before issuing warrant.",
      "dc:description": "Further information"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-50-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50(3) Offence and civil penalty provision related warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 331,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The issuing officer must not issue the warrant unless the authorised\nperson or some other person has given to the issuing officer, either\norally or by affidavit, such further information (if any) as the\nissuing officer requires concerning the grounds on which the issue\nof the warrant is being sought."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Issuing officer must provide further information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50(4) Offence and civil penalty provision related warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-50-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.331",
      "values:originalText": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) name one or more authorised persons; and\n(b) authorise the persons so named, with such assistance and by\nsuch force as is necessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in subsections 47(4) and\n48(1) and section 48C; and\n(iii) to seize the evidential material; and\n(c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(d) specify the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) name one or more authorised persons; and\n(b) authorise the persons so named, with such assistance and by\nsuch force as is necessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in subsections 47(4) and\n48(1) and section 48C; and\n(iii) to seize the evidential material; and\n(c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(d) specify the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-50-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7376613b572136a9e0da603fca35d6bdacaef874504fc04a3fc5c24727b55e9c",
      "skos:note": "Warrant requirements for entry and seizure of evidential material"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-50-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50(4) Offence and civil penalty provision related warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 331,
      "values:originalText": "(4) The warrant must:\n(a) name one or more authorised persons; and\n(b) authorise the persons so named, with such assistance and by\nsuch force as is necessary and reasonable:\n(i) to enter the premises; and\n(ii) to exercise the powers set out in subsections 47(4) and\n48(1) and section 48C; and\n(iii) to seize the evidential material; and\n(c) state whether the entry is authorised to be made at any time\nof the day or night or during specified hours of the day or\nnight; and\n(d) specify the day (not more than one week after the issue of the\nwarrant) on which the warrant ceases to have effect; and\n(e) state the purpose for which the warrant is issued."
    },
