    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51A Inspections for purposes of Mutual Recognition Convention",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-51a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.333",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may request the Secretary to arrange for an authorised\nperson to inspect premises, and specified processes being carried\nout on those premises, for the purposes of paragraph 2 of Article 3\nof the Mutual Recognition Convention.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person may request the Secretary to arrange for an authorised\nperson to inspect premises, and specified processes being carried\nout on those premises, for the purposes of paragraph 2 of Article 3\nof the Mutual Recognition Convention.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51a-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8515f4b2230d33a1525abb2e0b996ff3d9850f9563b795b3445c2c00aa73c4c9",
      "skos:note": "Request for inspection under Mutual Recognition Convention"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-51a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51A Inspections for purposes of Mutual Recognition Convention",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 333,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person may request the Secretary to arrange for an authorised\nperson to inspect premises, and specified processes being carried\nout on those premises, for the purposes of paragraph 2 of Article 3\nof the Mutual Recognition Convention.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51a-norm",
      "@type": "values:Permission",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51a"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51B Offences relating to warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-51b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.334",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not make, in an application for a warrant, a\nstatement that the person knows to be false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n(2) A person must not:\n(a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant\nunder section 51 the name of an issuing officer unless that\nissuing officer issued the warrant; or\n(b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to\nthe person’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from\nthe form authorised by the issuing officer; or\n(c) purport to execute, or present to another person, a document\nthat purports to be a form of warrant under that section that\nthe first-mentioned person knows:\n(i) has not been approved by an issuing officer under that\nsection; or\n(ii) to depart in a material particular from the terms\nauthorised by an issuing officer under that section; or\n(d) give to an issuing officer a form of warrant under that section\nthat is not the form of warrant that the person purported to\nexecute.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person must not make, in an application for a warrant, a\nstatement that the person knows to be false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n(2) A person must not:\n(a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant\nunder section 51 the name of an issuing officer unless that\nissuing officer issued the warrant; or\n(b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to\nthe person’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from\nthe form authorised by the issuing officer; or\n(c) purport to execute, or present to another person, a document\nthat purports to be a form of warrant under that section that\nthe first-mentioned person knows:\n(i) has not been approved by an issuing officer under that\nsection; or\n(ii) to depart in a material particular from the terms\nauthorised by an issuing officer under that section; or\n(d) give to an issuing officer a form of warrant under that section\nthat is not the form of warrant that the person purported to\nexecute.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ae931bb7bc669fbe6bd7003ffaa00525b972c9fdeaffd59a4f3878da861eb847"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-51b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51B Offences relating to warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 334,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person must not make, in an application for a warrant, a\nstatement that the person knows to be false or misleading in a\nmaterial particular.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.\n(2) A person must not:\n(a) state in a document that purports to be a form of warrant\nunder section 51 the name of an issuing officer unless that\nissuing officer issued the warrant; or\n(b) state on a form of warrant under that section a matter that, to\nthe person’s knowledge, departs in a material particular from\nthe form authorised by the issuing officer; or\n(c) purport to execute, or present to another person, a document\nthat purports to be a form of warrant under that section that\nthe first-mentioned person knows:\n(i) has not been approved by an issuing officer under that\nsection; or\n(ii) to depart in a material particular from the terms\nauthorised by an issuing officer under that section; or\n(d) give to an issuing officer a form of warrant under that section\nthat is not the form of warrant that the person purported to\nexecute.\nPenalty: Imprisonment for 2 years."
    },
