    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51C Issuing officers—personal capacity",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-51c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.334",
      "values:originalText": "Powers conferred personally\n(1) A power conferred on an issuing officer by this Part is conferred on\nthe issuing officer:\n(a) in a personal capacity; and\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 52\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) not as a court, or as a member or an officer of a court.\nPowers need not be accepted\n(2) The issuing officer need not accept the power conferred.\nProtection and immunity\n(3) An issuing officer exercising a power conferred by this Part has the\nsame protection and immunity as if the issuing officer were\nexercising the power:\n(a) as the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an\nofficer; or\n(b) as a member or an officer of the court of which the issuing\nofficer is a member or an officer.",
      "skos:definition": "Powers conferred personally\n(1) A power conferred on an issuing officer by this Part is conferred on\nthe issuing officer:\n(a) in a personal capacity; and\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 52\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) not as a court, or as a member or an officer of a court.\nPowers need not be accepted\n(2) The issuing officer need not accept the power conferred.\nProtection and immunity\n(3) An issuing officer exercising a power conferred by this Part has the\nsame protection and immunity as if the issuing officer were\nexercising the power:\n(a) as the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an\nofficer; or\n(b) as a member or an officer of the court of which the issuing\nofficer is a member or an officer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a3d9ce38f203e8b183955c1df3c707be225fa24ea2ebd96628bb6f45dc1fcae0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-51c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51C Issuing officers—personal capacity",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 334,
      "values:originalText": "Powers conferred personally\n(1) A power conferred on an issuing officer by this Part is conferred on\nthe issuing officer:\n(a) in a personal capacity; and\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nEntry, searches and warrants  Part 6-2\n\nSection 52\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) not as a court, or as a member or an officer of a court.\nPowers need not be accepted\n(2) The issuing officer need not accept the power conferred.\nProtection and immunity\n(3) An issuing officer exercising a power conferred by this Part has the\nsame protection and immunity as if the issuing officer were\nexercising the power:\n(a) as the court of which the issuing officer is a member or an\nofficer; or\n(b) as a member or an officer of the court of which the issuing\nofficer is a member or an officer."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-51c-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
