    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52 Identity cards",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.335",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary is to ensure that each authorised person is issued\nwith an identity card that incorporates a recent photograph of the\nperson.\n(3) Where a person ceases to be an authorised person, the person must,\nas soon as practicable after so ceasing, return the person’s identity\ncard to the Secretary.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.\n(4) An offence under subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary is to ensure that each authorised person is issued\nwith an identity card that incorporates a recent photograph of the\nperson.\n(3) Where a person ceases to be an authorised person, the person must,\nas soon as practicable after so ceasing, return the person’s identity\ncard to the Secretary.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.\n(4) An offence under subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\nChapter 6  Administration",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df1f29dd77a548b96fc07a91708fc470a09a0ab123087dc9a49e2276e2086e4c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52 Identity cards",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 335,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary is to ensure that each authorised person is issued\nwith an identity card that incorporates a recent photograph of the\nperson.\n(3) Where a person ceases to be an authorised person, the person must,\nas soon as practicable after so ceasing, return the person’s identity\ncard to the Secretary.\nPenalty: 1 penalty unit.\n(4) An offence under subsection (3) is an offence of strict liability.\nNote:\nFor strict liability, see section 6.1 of the Criminal Code.\n\nChapter 6  Administration"
    },
    {
