    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52aa",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52AA Overview",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52aa"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.340",
      "values:originalText": "This Part provides the basis for a uniform system in Australia of\naccess controls for goods containing scheduled substances.\nThe scheduling of substances allows restrictions to be placed on\ntheir supply to the public, in the interests of public health and\nsafety. This is aimed at minimising the risks of poisoning from,\nand the misuse and abuse of, scheduled substances.",
      "skos:definition": "This Part provides the basis for a uniform system in Australia of\naccess controls for goods containing scheduled substances.\nThe scheduling of substances allows restrictions to be placed on\ntheir supply to the public, in the interests of public health and\nsafety. This is aimed at minimising the risks of poisoning from,\nand the misuse and abuse of, scheduled substances.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52aa-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52aa-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c9a15ab67ef9d6e197068006d1a55acffe6e3b242e8aa8af0053598495ca16aa",
      "skos:note": "Restrictions on supply of scheduled substances for public health and safety"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52aa",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52AA Overview",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 340,
      "values:originalText": "This Part provides the basis for a uniform system in Australia of\naccess controls for goods containing scheduled substances.\nThe scheduling of substances allows restrictions to be placed on\ntheir supply to the public, in the interests of public health and\nsafety. This is aimed at minimising the risks of poisoning from,\nand the misuse and abuse of, scheduled substances."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52aa-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52aa"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52aa-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imposes an obligation on the state to restrict supply",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52A Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.340",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\ncurrent Poisons Standard means:\n(a) if no document has been prepared under\nparagraph 52D(2)(b)—the first Poisons Standard; or\n(b) otherwise—the document last prepared under that\nparagraph (including as amended).\nfirst Poisons Standard means the latest edition at the\ncommencement of this Part of the document known as the\nStandard for the Uniform Scheduling of Drugs and Poisons\npublished by the Australian Health Ministers’ Advisory Council.\nscheduling, in relation to a substance, means determining the\nschedule or schedules to the current Poisons Standard in which the\nname or a description of the substance is to be included.\nsubstance means:\n(a) an ingredient, compound, material or preparation which, or\nthe use of which, may cause death, illness or injury to\npersons or animals; or\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nScheduling of substances  Part 6-3\n\nSection 52B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) an ingredient, compound, material or preparation specified\nunder subsection (2);\nand includes any ingredient, compound, material or preparation\nreferred to in a schedule to the current Poisons Standard (as in\nforce immediately before 1 July 2010).\n(2) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, specify an\ningredient, compound, material or preparation for the purposes of\nparagraph (b) of the definition of substance in subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\ncurrent Poisons Standard means:\n(a) if no document has been prepared under\nparagraph 52D(2)(b)—the first Poisons Standard; or\n(b) otherwise—the document last prepared under that\nparagraph (including as amended).\nfirst Poisons Standard means the latest edition at the\ncommencement of this Part of the document known as the\nStandard for the Uniform Scheduling of Drugs and Poisons\npublished by the Australian Health Ministers’ Advisory Council.\nscheduling, in relation to a substance, means determining the\nschedule or schedules to the current Poisons Standard in which the\nname or a description of the substance is to be included.\nsubstance means:\n(a) an ingredient, compound, material or preparation which, or\nthe use of which, may cause death, illness or injury to\npersons or animals; or\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nScheduling of substances  Part 6-3\n\nSection 52B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) an ingredient, compound, material or preparation specified\nunder subsection (2);\nand includes any ingredient, compound, material or preparation\nreferred to in a schedule to the current Poisons Standard (as in\nforce immediately before 1 July 2010).\n(2) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, specify an\ningredient, compound, material or preparation for the purposes of\nparagraph (b) of the definition of substance in subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52a-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c84949d62f463725ac9e31150e1062d9e0753ce555f9ad216b5ba10ac7152842"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52A Definitions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 340,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears:\ncurrent Poisons Standard means:\n(a) if no document has been prepared under\nparagraph 52D(2)(b)—the first Poisons Standard; or\n(b) otherwise—the document last prepared under that\nparagraph (including as amended).\nfirst Poisons Standard means the latest edition at the\ncommencement of this Part of the document known as the\nStandard for the Uniform Scheduling of Drugs and Poisons\npublished by the Australian Health Ministers’ Advisory Council.\nscheduling, in relation to a substance, means determining the\nschedule or schedules to the current Poisons Standard in which the\nname or a description of the substance is to be included.\nsubstance means:\n(a) an ingredient, compound, material or preparation which, or\nthe use of which, may cause death, illness or injury to\npersons or animals; or\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nScheduling of substances  Part 6-3\n\nSection 52B\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) an ingredient, compound, material or preparation specified\nunder subsection (2);\nand includes any ingredient, compound, material or preparation\nreferred to in a schedule to the current Poisons Standard (as in\nforce immediately before 1 July 2010).\n(2) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, specify an\ningredient, compound, material or preparation for the purposes of\nparagraph (b) of the definition of substance in subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003."
    },
