    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52A(2) Definitions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52a-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.340",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, specify an\ningredient, compound, material or preparation for the purposes of\nparagraph (b) of the definition of substance in subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, specify an\ningredient, compound, material or preparation for the purposes of\nparagraph (b) of the definition of substance in subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52a-ss-2-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6f14d7e5463215b42a24d5d28045a6762e1f1b5ec2b850aab05d901aa2fbdad4",
      "skos:note": "Secretary may specify ingredients for purposes of definition"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52a-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52A(2) Definitions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 340,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Secretary may, by legislative instrument, specify an\ningredient, compound, material or preparation for the purposes of\nparagraph (b) of the definition of substance in subsection (1).\nNote:\nFor specification by class, see subsection 13(3) of the Legislation Act\n2003."
    },
