      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52c",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52C Advisory Committee on Chemicals Scheduling",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52c"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.342",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Advisory Committee on Chemicals Scheduling is established\nby this section.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the Committee is to be constituted, and\nto hold meetings, in accordance with the regulations.\n(3) The Commonwealth, each State, the Australian Capital Territory\nand the Northern Territory are each entitled to nominate a member\nof the Committee in accordance with the regulations.\n(4) The functions of the Committee are as follows:\n(a) subject to subsection (5), to make recommendations to the\nSecretary in relation to the classification and scheduling of\nsubstances;\n(b) to make recommendations to the Secretary in relation to\nother changes to the current Poisons Standard (other than the\nschedules);\n(c) to reconsider a recommendation made under paragraph (a) or\n(b) at the request of the Secretary;\n(d) subject to subsection (5), to provide advice to the Secretary\nin relation to the restrictions (including restrictions as to\naccessibility and availability) to be imposed in respect of\nparticular substances;\n(e) to provide advice to the Secretary in relation to any matter\nreferred to it by the Secretary;\n(f) any other functions that are prescribed by the regulations.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nScheduling of substances  Part 6-3\n\nSection 52CA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(5) Paragraphs (4)(a) and (d) do not apply in relation to substances to\nthe extent that the substances are, or are included in, therapeutic\ngoods.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Advisory Committee on Chemicals Scheduling is established\nby this section.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the Committee is to be constituted, and\nto hold meetings, in accordance with the regulations.\n(3) The Commonwealth, each State, the Australian Capital Territory\nand the Northern Territory are each entitled to nominate a member\nof the Committee in accordance with the regulations.\n(4) The functions of the Committee are as follows:\n(a) subject to subsection (5), to make recommendations to the\nSecretary in relation to the classification and scheduling of\nsubstances;\n(b) to make recommendations to the Secretary in relation to\nother changes to the current Poisons Standard (other than the\nschedules);\n(c) to reconsider a recommendation made under paragraph (a) or\n(b) at the request of the Secretary;\n(d) subject to subsection (5), to provide advice to the Secretary\nin relation to the restrictions (including restrictions as to\naccessibility and availability) to be imposed in respect of\nparticular substances;\n(e) to provide advice to the Secretary in relation to any matter\nreferred to it by the Secretary;\n(f) any other functions that are prescribed by the regulations.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nScheduling of substances  Part 6-3\n\nSection 52CA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(5) Paragraphs (4)(a) and (d) do not apply in relation to substances to\nthe extent that the substances are, or are included in, therapeutic\ngoods.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52c-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52c-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52c-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52c-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52c-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1555a0adbc84ebb6a79d9a4d68b2036eae0bd6caee0219ab6d7cb20a42c91c6b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52c",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "52C Advisory Committee on Chemicals Scheduling",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 342,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Advisory Committee on Chemicals Scheduling is established\nby this section.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), the Committee is to be constituted, and\nto hold meetings, in accordance with the regulations.\n(3) The Commonwealth, each State, the Australian Capital Territory\nand the Northern Territory are each entitled to nominate a member\nof the Committee in accordance with the regulations.\n(4) The functions of the Committee are as follows:\n(a) subject to subsection (5), to make recommendations to the\nSecretary in relation to the classification and scheduling of\nsubstances;\n(b) to make recommendations to the Secretary in relation to\nother changes to the current Poisons Standard (other than the\nschedules);\n(c) to reconsider a recommendation made under paragraph (a) or\n(b) at the request of the Secretary;\n(d) subject to subsection (5), to provide advice to the Secretary\nin relation to the restrictions (including restrictions as to\naccessibility and availability) to be imposed in respect of\nparticular substances;\n(e) to provide advice to the Secretary in relation to any matter\nreferred to it by the Secretary;\n(f) any other functions that are prescribed by the regulations.\n\nAdministration  Chapter 6\nScheduling of substances  Part 6-3\n\nSection 52CA\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(5) Paragraphs (4)(a) and (d) do not apply in relation to substances to\nthe extent that the substances are, or are included in, therapeutic\ngoods."
    },
