    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-52f",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "52F Incorporation of current Poisons Standard",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-52f"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.346",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a legislative\ninstrument, or a notifiable instrument, under this Act may make\nprovision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or\nincorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained\nin the current Poisons Standard as in force or existing from time to\ntime.\n(2) Despite subsection 46AA(2) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, an\ninstrument under this Act (other than a legislative instrument or a\nnotifiable instrument) may make provision in relation to a matter\nby applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without\nmodification, any matter contained in the current Poisons Standard\nas in force or existing from time to time.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 52G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nChapter 7—Miscellaneous",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, a legislative\ninstrument, or a notifiable instrument, under this Act may make\nprovision in relation to a matter by applying, adopting or\nincorporating, with or without modification, any matter contained\nin the current Poisons Standard as in force or existing from time to\ntime.\n(2) Despite subsection 46AA(2) of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901, an\ninstrument under this Act (other than a legislative instrument or a\nnotifiable instrument) may make provision in relation to a matter\nby applying, adopting or incorporating, with or without\nmodification, any matter contained in the current Poisons Standard\nas in force or existing from time to time.\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 52G\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\nChapter 7—Miscellaneous",
      "cml:hasPart": [
