    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "54B(3) Personal liability of an executive officer of a body corporate—",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-54b-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.354",
      "values:originalText": "(3) An executive officer of a body corporate contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n(a) the body corporate contravenes a civil penalty provision; and\n(b) the officer knew that the contravention would occur; and\n(c) the officer was in a position to influence the conduct of the\nbody in relation to the contravention; and\n(d) the officer failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the\ncontravention.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) An executive officer of a body corporate contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n(a) the body corporate contravenes a civil penalty provision; and\n(b) the officer knew that the contravention would occur; and\n(c) the officer was in a position to influence the conduct of the\nbody in relation to the contravention; and\n(d) the officer failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the\ncontravention.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b-ss-3-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-54b-ss-3-logic-deontic-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "65211f4be3e156a861f091cb405c0115c99660caf892bfc69f5a90753f0a30af",
      "skos:note": "Executive officer must take reasonable steps to prevent contravention of civil penalty provision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-54b-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "54B(3) Personal liability of an executive officer of a body corporate—",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 354,
      "values:originalText": "(3) An executive officer of a body corporate contravenes this\nsubsection if:\n(a) the body corporate contravenes a civil penalty provision; and\n(b) the officer knew that the contravention would occur; and\n(c) the officer was in a position to influence the conduct of the\nbody in relation to the contravention; and\n(d) the officer failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent the\ncontravention."
    },
