    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55(4) Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-55-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.358",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a person other than a body\ncorporate (in this subsection called the employer) by an employee\nor agent of the employer within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority is to be taken, for the purposes of a prosecution\nfor an offence against this Act, or for a contravention of a civil\npenalty provision, to have been engaged in also by the employer\nunless the employer establishes that he or she took reasonable\nprecautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a person other than a body\ncorporate (in this subsection called the employer) by an employee\nor agent of the employer within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority is to be taken, for the purposes of a prosecution\nfor an offence against this Act, or for a contravention of a civil\npenalty provision, to have been engaged in also by the employer\nunless the employer establishes that he or she took reasonable\nprecautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bb2235be6dda6e76680cfd3045b1e68ca3175d0ea1db23e85c1965cf90f03328",
      "skos:note": "Employer liable for conduct of employee/agent within scope of authority"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-55-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55(4) Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 358,
      "values:originalText": "(4) Any conduct engaged in on behalf of a person other than a body\ncorporate (in this subsection called the employer) by an employee\nor agent of the employer within the scope of his or her actual or\napparent authority is to be taken, for the purposes of a prosecution\nfor an offence against this Act, or for a contravention of a civil\npenalty provision, to have been engaged in also by the employer\nunless the employer establishes that he or she took reasonable\nprecautions and exercised due diligence to avoid the conduct."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Liability",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Employer liable for conduct",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Employee/agent within scope of authority",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Employer must provide liability"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55(5) Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-55-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.358",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where:\n(a) a person other than a body corporate is convicted of an\noffence; and\n(b) the person would not have been convicted of the offence if\nsubsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted;\nthe person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that\noffence.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Where:\n(a) a person other than a body corporate is convicted of an\noffence; and\n(b) the person would not have been convicted of the offence if\nsubsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted;\nthe person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that\noffence.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-linearlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-deontic-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6fe882b570b32f6c05fd121a4ae143bb84077188002292139eb050dce5fd2d7b",
      "skos:note": "No imprisonment for certain offences if convicted by a non-corporate person"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-55-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55(5) Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 358,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Where:\n(a) a person other than a body corporate is convicted of an\noffence; and\n(b) the person would not have been convicted of the offence if\nsubsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted;\nthe person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that\noffence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:NaturalPerson"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: NaturalPerson"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "No imprisonment implies obligation to refrain from punishment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) Where: ... the person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If a person would not have been convicted of the offence if subsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted, then they are not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Permits",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Imprisonment permits other forms of punishment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) Where: ... the person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If a person would not have been convicted of the offence if subsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted, then they are permitted to receive other forms of punishment"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-linearlogic-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LinearLogic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "And",
      "cml:logicSummary": "No imprisonment implies obligation to refrain from punishment and permits other forms of punishment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::linear",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) Where: ... the person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If a person would not have been convicted of the offence if subsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted, then they are permitted to receive other forms of punishment"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-5-logic-deontic-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Justifies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to refrain from punishment justifies no imprisonment",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(5) Where: ... the person is not liable to be punished by imprisonment for that offence.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "If a person would not have been convicted of the offence if subsections (3) and (4) had not been enacted, then they are justified in refraining from punishment"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "55(6) Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-55-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.358",
      "values:originalText": "(6) A reference in subsection (1) or (3) to the state of mind of a person\nincludes a reference to:\n(a) the knowledge, intention, opinion, belief or purpose of the\nperson; and\n(b) the person’s reasons for the intention, opinion, belief or\npurpose.\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 56\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "skos:definition": "(6) A reference in subsection (1) or (3) to the state of mind of a person\nincludes a reference to:\n(a) the knowledge, intention, opinion, belief or purpose of the\nperson; and\n(b) the person’s reasons for the intention, opinion, belief or\npurpose.\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 56\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-logic-descriptionlogic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-logic-argumentation-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-logic-diffusion-6"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1315e6721d4b51124c656bce1be24f8086c4f37b4a4a0b06d6ed6f97a99d13e4",
      "skos:note": "Directors, employees and agents must have certain knowledge or reasons for their intentions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-55-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "55(6) Conduct by directors, employees and agents",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 358,
      "values:originalText": "(6) A reference in subsection (1) or (3) to the state of mind of a person\nincludes a reference to:\n(a) the knowledge, intention, opinion, belief or purpose of the\nperson; and\n(b) the person’s reasons for the intention, opinion, belief or\npurpose.\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 56\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-55-ss-6-norm",
