    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-57-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "57(5) Delegation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-57-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.364",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Without limiting the generality of matters that may be dealt with\nby regulations made for the purposes of subsection (3), the\nregulations may make provision in relation to the following:\n(a) the persons who may be delegates;\n(b) the circumstances in which delegates may grant approvals for\nthe purposes of paragraph 19(1)(a), 32CK(1)(d) or\n41HB(1)(d);\n(c) the conditions to which any approvals granted by delegates\nare to be subject;\n(d) requiring information to be given by delegates to the\nSecretary.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Without limiting the generality of matters that may be dealt with\nby regulations made for the purposes of subsection (3), the\nregulations may make provision in relation to the following:\n(a) the persons who may be delegates;\n(b) the circumstances in which delegates may grant approvals for\nthe purposes of paragraph 19(1)(a), 32CK(1)(d) or\n41HB(1)(d);\n(c) the conditions to which any approvals granted by delegates\nare to be subject;\n(d) requiring information to be given by delegates to the\nSecretary.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-57"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-57-ss-5-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "df7336e313cc9b63916b010f73ff6d0dbf49af5da7b1578591ee5b504a7b332c",
      "skos:note": "Regulations may make provision for delegates, approvals, and conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-57-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "57(5) Delegation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 364,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Without limiting the generality of matters that may be dealt with\nby regulations made for the purposes of subsection (3), the\nregulations may make provision in relation to the following:\n(a) the persons who may be delegates;\n(b) the circumstances in which delegates may grant approvals for\nthe purposes of paragraph 19(1)(a), 32CK(1)(d) or\n41HB(1)(d);\n(c) the conditions to which any approvals granted by delegates\nare to be subject;\n(d) requiring information to be given by delegates to the\nSecretary."
    },
