    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58 Export certifications",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-58"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.367",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may issue export certification for goods for\ntherapeutic use in humans, including certifications for the purposes\nof the World Health Organisation Certification Scheme on the\nQuality of Pharmaceutical Products Moving in International\nCommerce.\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 59\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for goods\nfor therapeutic use in humans.\n(2A) The Secretary may issue export certification for vaping goods for\nuse in humans that are not goods for which export certification\nmay be issued under subsection (1).\nNote:\nExport certification for vaping goods that are for therapeutic use in\nhumans may be issued under subsection (1).\n(2B) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for vaping\ngoods for which export certification may be issued under\nsubsection (2A).\n(3) Such fee as is prescribed is payable in respect of:\n(a) an application for a certification under this section; and\n(b) where an inspection of a manufacturing site is necessary for\nthe purposes of the issue of a certification under this\nsection—the inspection of that site.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Secretary may issue export certification for goods for\ntherapeutic use in humans, including certifications for the purposes\nof the World Health Organisation Certification Scheme on the\nQuality of Pharmaceutical Products Moving in International\nCommerce.\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 59\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for goods\nfor therapeutic use in humans.\n(2A) The Secretary may issue export certification for vaping goods for\nuse in humans that are not goods for which export certification\nmay be issued under subsection (1).\nNote:\nExport certification for vaping goods that are for therapeutic use in\nhumans may be issued under subsection (1).\n(2B) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for vaping\ngoods for which export certification may be issued under\nsubsection (2A).\n(3) Such fee as is prescribed is payable in respect of:\n(a) an application for a certification under this section; and\n(b) where an inspection of a manufacturing site is necessary for\nthe purposes of the issue of a certification under this\nsection—the inspection of that site.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-2a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-2b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-58-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "da2ca4530f906c76ff51f7195cdbae8083d3bd829a37bfbc25ab09fcdd6e3398"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-58",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58 Export certifications",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 367,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Secretary may issue export certification for goods for\ntherapeutic use in humans, including certifications for the purposes\nof the World Health Organisation Certification Scheme on the\nQuality of Pharmaceutical Products Moving in International\nCommerce.\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 59\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(2) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for goods\nfor therapeutic use in humans.\n(2A) The Secretary may issue export certification for vaping goods for\nuse in humans that are not goods for which export certification\nmay be issued under subsection (1).\nNote:\nExport certification for vaping goods that are for therapeutic use in\nhumans may be issued under subsection (1).\n(2B) A State or Territory must not issue export certifications for vaping\ngoods for which export certification may be issued under\nsubsection (2A).\n(3) Such fee as is prescribed is payable in respect of:\n(a) an application for a certification under this section; and\n(b) where an inspection of a manufacturing site is necessary for\nthe purposes of the issue of a certification under this\nsection—the inspection of that site."
    },
