      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n(a) the appellant applies to the Administrative Review Tribunal\nfor review of the decision on reconsideration and lodges\ninitial new information in support of that application; and\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 60A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the appellant does not lodge later new information in support\nof that application;\nthe Tribunal must not remit the matter under subsection (3) if all of\nthe initial new information is information that the Minister took\ninto account under paragraph (2)(a) in making the decision on\nreconsideration.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If:\n(a) the appellant applies to the Administrative Review Tribunal\nfor review of the decision on reconsideration and lodges\ninitial new information in support of that application; and\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 60A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the appellant does not lodge later new information in support\nof that application;\nthe Tribunal must not remit the matter under subsection (3) if all of\nthe initial new information is information that the Minister took\ninto account under paragraph (2)(a) in making the decision on\nreconsideration.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-logic-ltl-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f98abad1a8748f375a324a72f174b98e1570fc5e7bf9c6932ea4ed244a937e6",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal must not remit the matter under subsection (3) if all of initial new information is information that the Minister took into account."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60A(4) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If:\n(a) the appellant applies to the Administrative Review Tribunal\nfor review of the decision on reconsideration and lodges\ninitial new information in support of that application; and\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 60A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) the appellant does not lodge later new information in support\nof that application;\nthe Tribunal must not remit the matter under subsection (3) if all of\nthe initial new information is information that the Minister took\ninto account under paragraph (2)(a) in making the decision on\nreconsideration."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MustNot",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Tribunal must not remit the matter.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Appellant lodges initial new information.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Tribunal cannot remit the matter."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Overlaps",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Initial new information overlaps with the Minister's decision on reconsideration.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Appellant lodges initial new information.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Tribunal's discretion to remit is limited by this overlap."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-4-logic-ltl-3",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:LTL"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Repeats",
      "cml:logicSummary": "The Minister's decision on reconsideration repeats the initial new information.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::temporal_ltl",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Minister took initial new information into account.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Tribunal's discretion to remit is limited by this repetition."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60A(5) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n(a) the appellant lodges initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both) in support of an application to the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision\non reconsideration; and\n(b) the Tribunal does not remit the matter under subsection (3);\nthe Tribunal, in reviewing the decision on reconsideration:\n(c) may consider initial new information (if any) that the\nMinister took into account under paragraph (2)(a) in making\nthe decision on reconsideration; and\n(d) must not consider any other initial new information, except\ninitial new information that indicates that the quality, safety\nor efficacy of the therapeutic goods is unacceptable; and\n(e) must not consider any later new information, except later\nnew information that indicates that the quality, safety or\nefficacy of the therapeutic goods is unacceptable.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) If:\n(a) the appellant lodges initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both) in support of an application to the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision\non reconsideration; and\n(b) the Tribunal does not remit the matter under subsection (3);\nthe Tribunal, in reviewing the decision on reconsideration:\n(c) may consider initial new information (if any) that the\nMinister took into account under paragraph (2)(a) in making\nthe decision on reconsideration; and\n(d) must not consider any other initial new information, except\ninitial new information that indicates that the quality, safety\nor efficacy of the therapeutic goods is unacceptable; and\n(e) must not consider any later new information, except later\nnew information that indicates that the quality, safety or\nefficacy of the therapeutic goods is unacceptable.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "154dad67d61e08fea5643f23324efebc1c6678ab7a8aa8287493d535a94d0ee9",
      "skos:note": "Tribunal must consider initial new information that indicates unacceptable quality, safety or efficacy of therapeutic goods."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60A(5) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "(5) If:\n(a) the appellant lodges initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both) in support of an application to the\nAdministrative Review Tribunal for review of the decision\non reconsideration; and\n(b) the Tribunal does not remit the matter under subsection (3);\nthe Tribunal, in reviewing the decision on reconsideration:\n(c) may consider initial new information (if any) that the\nMinister took into account under paragraph (2)(a) in making\nthe decision on reconsideration; and\n(d) must not consider any other initial new information, except\ninitial new information that indicates that the quality, safety\nor efficacy of the therapeutic goods is unacceptable; and\n(e) must not consider any later new information, except later\nnew information that indicates that the quality, safety or\nefficacy of the therapeutic goods is unacceptable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
