      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Tribunal must consider initial new information",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (3)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Initial new information considered"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": ">=",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Tribunal must consider initial new information within a certain timeframe",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Subsection (3)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Initial new information considered within timeframe"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60A(6) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n(aa) the matter relates to a decision under section 25; and\n(a) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(b) the appellant has paid, as a further evaluation fee, the\nevaluation fee that the appellant would have to pay under\nsection 24 on making a new application for registration of the\ntherapeutic goods;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision under section 25,\ntaking into account the initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application\nfor registration had been made.\n(6AA) If:\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 60A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the matter relates to a decision under section 32DF or 32DG;\nand\n(b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(c) the appellant has paid, as a further evaluation fee, the\nevaluation fee that the appellant would have to pay under\nsection 32DI on making a new application for inclusion of\nthe biological in the Register;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision whether or not to\ninclude the biological in the Register, taking into account the initial\nnew information or later new information (or both), as the case\nmay be, as if a fresh application for inclusion of the biological in\nthe Register had been made.",
      "skos:definition": "(6) If:\n(aa) the matter relates to a decision under section 25; and\n(a) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(b) the appellant has paid, as a further evaluation fee, the\nevaluation fee that the appellant would have to pay under\nsection 24 on making a new application for registration of the\ntherapeutic goods;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision under section 25,\ntaking into account the initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application\nfor registration had been made.\n(6AA) If:\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 60A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the matter relates to a decision under section 32DF or 32DG;\nand\n(b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(c) the appellant has paid, as a further evaluation fee, the\nevaluation fee that the appellant would have to pay under\nsection 32DI on making a new application for inclusion of\nthe biological in the Register;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision whether or not to\ninclude the biological in the Register, taking into account the initial\nnew information or later new information (or both), as the case\nmay be, as if a fresh application for inclusion of the biological in\nthe Register had been made.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6-logic-dialectical-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6-logic-linearlogic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "218688f846807fb19e08426edf3d27f38cf6bab2f3e9106f1f261775304612ff",
      "skos:note": "Authorised delegate must make a decision under section 25 taking into account new information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60A(6) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "(6) If:\n(aa) the matter relates to a decision under section 25; and\n(a) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(b) the appellant has paid, as a further evaluation fee, the\nevaluation fee that the appellant would have to pay under\nsection 24 on making a new application for registration of the\ntherapeutic goods;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision under section 25,\ntaking into account the initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application\nfor registration had been made.\n(6AA) If:\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 60A\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(a) the matter relates to a decision under section 32DF or 32DG;\nand\n(b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(c) the appellant has paid, as a further evaluation fee, the\nevaluation fee that the appellant would have to pay under\nsection 32DI on making a new application for inclusion of\nthe biological in the Register;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision whether or not to\ninclude the biological in the Register, taking into account the initial\nnew information or later new information (or both), as the case\nmay be, as if a fresh application for inclusion of the biological in\nthe Register had been made."
    },
    {
