    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "60A(6A) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-6a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.374",
      "values:originalText": "(6A) If:\n(a) the matter relates to a decision under section 41EC; and\n(b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(c) the appellant has paid, as a further conformity assessment\nfee, the conformity assessment fee that the appellant would\nhave to pay under section 41LA on making a new application\nfor a conformity assessment certificate;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision under section 41EC,\ntaking into account the initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application\nfor a conformity assessment certificate had been made.",
      "skos:definition": "(6A) If:\n(a) the matter relates to a decision under section 41EC; and\n(b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(c) the appellant has paid, as a further conformity assessment\nfee, the conformity assessment fee that the appellant would\nhave to pay under section 41LA on making a new application\nfor a conformity assessment certificate;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision under section 41EC,\ntaking into account the initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application\nfor a conformity assessment certificate had been made.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6a-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-60a-ss-6a-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d86245ee5eb12dc4b56afa8aea8e0305cb51fbac0faed8e490c720d9027db4f3",
      "skos:note": "The authorised delegate must make a decision under section 41EC, taking into account the initial new information or later new information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-60a-ss-6a",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "60A(6A) New information on review—discretion to remit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 374,
      "values:originalText": "(6A) If:\n(a) the matter relates to a decision under section 41EC; and\n(b) the Minister or the Tribunal remits the matter; and\n(c) the appellant has paid, as a further conformity assessment\nfee, the conformity assessment fee that the appellant would\nhave to pay under section 41LA on making a new application\nfor a conformity assessment certificate;\nthe authorised delegate must make a decision under section 41EC,\ntaking into account the initial new information or later new\ninformation (or both), as the case may be, as if a fresh application\nfor a conformity assessment certificate had been made."
    },
