    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61A Immunity from civil actions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-61a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.385",
      "values:originalText": "(1) No civil action, suit or proceeding lies against:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) a protected person;\nin respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another\nperson as a result of anything done, or omitted to be done, by a\nprotected person in relation to the performance or purported\nperformance, or in relation to the exercise or purported exercise, of\na protected person’s functions, duties or powers under this Act or\nthe regulations.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to an act or omission in bad faith.\n(3) A reference in subsection (1) to anything omitted to be done\nincludes a reference to a failure to make a decision.\n(4) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) a person to whom powers or functions are delegated under\nsubsection 57(1) or (1A);\n(d) a member of a committee established under this Act or the\nregulations;\n(e) an authorised person in relation to a provision of this Act\n(other than this section);\n(f) an authorised officer (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(g) an authorised person (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(ga) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 62\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(h) a person assisting a person (a primary person) referred to in\nparagraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) or (ga) in relation to\nthe performance or purported performance, or in relation to\nthe exercise or purported exercise, of a primary person’s\nfunctions, duties or powers under this Act or the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) No civil action, suit or proceeding lies against:\n(a) the Commonwealth; or\n(b) a protected person;\nin respect of loss, damage or injury of any kind suffered by another\nperson as a result of anything done, or omitted to be done, by a\nprotected person in relation to the performance or purported\nperformance, or in relation to the exercise or purported exercise, of\na protected person’s functions, duties or powers under this Act or\nthe regulations.\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to an act or omission in bad faith.\n(3) A reference in subsection (1) to anything omitted to be done\nincludes a reference to a failure to make a decision.\n(4) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) a person to whom powers or functions are delegated under\nsubsection 57(1) or (1A);\n(d) a member of a committee established under this Act or the\nregulations;\n(e) an authorised person in relation to a provision of this Act\n(other than this section);\n(f) an authorised officer (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(g) an authorised person (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(ga) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 62\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(h) a person assisting a person (a primary person) referred to in\nparagraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) or (ga) in relation to\nthe performance or purported performance, or in relation to\nthe exercise or purported exercise, of a primary person’s\nfunctions, duties or powers under this Act or the regulations.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a-ss-2"
        },
