      "cml:conclusionText": "(3) A reference in subsection (1) to anything omitted to be done includes a reference to a failure to make a decision."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "61A(4) Immunity from civil actions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-61a-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.385",
      "values:originalText": "(4) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) a person to whom powers or functions are delegated under\nsubsection 57(1) or (1A);\n(d) a member of a committee established under this Act or the\nregulations;\n(e) an authorised person in relation to a provision of this Act\n(other than this section);\n(f) an authorised officer (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(g) an authorised person (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(ga) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 62\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(h) a person assisting a person (a primary person) referred to in\nparagraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) or (ga) in relation to\nthe performance or purported performance, or in relation to\nthe exercise or purported exercise, of a primary person’s\nfunctions, duties or powers under this Act or the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) a person to whom powers or functions are delegated under\nsubsection 57(1) or (1A);\n(d) a member of a committee established under this Act or the\nregulations;\n(e) an authorised person in relation to a provision of this Act\n(other than this section);\n(f) an authorised officer (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(g) an authorised person (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(ga) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 62\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(h) a person assisting a person (a primary person) referred to in\nparagraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) or (ga) in relation to\nthe performance or purported performance, or in relation to\nthe exercise or purported exercise, of a primary person’s\nfunctions, duties or powers under this Act or the regulations.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-61a-ss-4-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b28154014219d630aeb9f0dcac09c59bfc9255da7f269fea3dad6c50756eaf1c",
      "skos:note": "Protected persons are defined for immunity from civil actions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-61a-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "61A(4) Immunity from civil actions",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 385,
      "values:originalText": "(4) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) the Minister;\n(b) the Secretary;\n(c) a person to whom powers or functions are delegated under\nsubsection 57(1) or (1A);\n(d) a member of a committee established under this Act or the\nregulations;\n(e) an authorised person in relation to a provision of this Act\n(other than this section);\n(f) an authorised officer (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(g) an authorised person (within the meaning of the regulations);\n(ga) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations;\n\nChapter 7  Miscellaneous\n\nSection 62\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(h) a person assisting a person (a primary person) referred to in\nparagraph (a), (b), (c), (d), (e), (f), (g) or (ga) in relation to\nthe performance or purported performance, or in relation to\nthe exercise or purported exercise, of a primary person’s\nfunctions, duties or powers under this Act or the regulations."
    },
