    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-62",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "62 Protection from criminal responsibility",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-62"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.386",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A protected person who, for the purpose of finding out whether this\nAct or the regulations have been complied with, obtains, possesses\nor conveys, or facilitates the conveyance of, goods is not criminally\nresponsible for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or\na State law, relating to the obtaining, possession, conveyance or\nfacilitation of the conveyance of the goods.\n(2) If a protected person, in connection with finding out whether this\nAct or the regulations have been complied with, arranges for\nanother person to convey goods, the other person is not criminally\nresponsible for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or\na State law, relating to:\n(a) the possession of the goods by the other person, to the extent\nthe possession is in connection with that conveyance of the\ngoods; or\n(b) that conveyance of the goods.\n(3) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) an APS employee in the Department;\n(b) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A protected person who, for the purpose of finding out whether this\nAct or the regulations have been complied with, obtains, possesses\nor conveys, or facilitates the conveyance of, goods is not criminally\nresponsible for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or\na State law, relating to the obtaining, possession, conveyance or\nfacilitation of the conveyance of the goods.\n(2) If a protected person, in connection with finding out whether this\nAct or the regulations have been complied with, arranges for\nanother person to convey goods, the other person is not criminally\nresponsible for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or\na State law, relating to:\n(a) the possession of the goods by the other person, to the extent\nthe possession is in connection with that conveyance of the\ngoods; or\n(b) that conveyance of the goods.\n(3) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) an APS employee in the Department;\n(b) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-62-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-62-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-62-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "7c0de13d8923e821f57598c0330ba83e6925e24eee98207b7fd033d8b5b5a640"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-62",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "62 Protection from criminal responsibility",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 386,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A protected person who, for the purpose of finding out whether this\nAct or the regulations have been complied with, obtains, possesses\nor conveys, or facilitates the conveyance of, goods is not criminally\nresponsible for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or\na State law, relating to the obtaining, possession, conveyance or\nfacilitation of the conveyance of the goods.\n(2) If a protected person, in connection with finding out whether this\nAct or the regulations have been complied with, arranges for\nanother person to convey goods, the other person is not criminally\nresponsible for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, or\na State law, relating to:\n(a) the possession of the goods by the other person, to the extent\nthe possession is in connection with that conveyance of the\ngoods; or\n(b) that conveyance of the goods.\n(3) In this section:\nprotected person means any of the following:\n(a) an APS employee in the Department;\n(b) a person of a kind prescribed by the regulations."
    },
