    {
      "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "63(3) Regulations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-63-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.386",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The regulations may:\n(a) prescribe different fees under this Act in relation to:\n(i) different classes of goods; or\n(ii) in the case of fees under Part 3-3—different steps in the\nmanufacture of goods; or\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 63\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) provide for the refund, reduction or waiving of fees or\ncharges in cases identified in the regulations; or\n(c) specify the type of information relating to therapeutic goods\nmanufactured by licence holders that the Secretary may,\nunder subsection 37(2), require to be supplied by the holders\nof licences at the time of payment of annual licensing charges\nin respect of the licences.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The regulations may:\n(a) prescribe different fees under this Act in relation to:\n(i) different classes of goods; or\n(ii) in the case of fees under Part 3-3—different steps in the\nmanufacture of goods; or\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 63\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) provide for the refund, reduction or waiving of fees or\ncharges in cases identified in the regulations; or\n(c) specify the type of information relating to therapeutic goods\nmanufactured by licence holders that the Secretary may,\nunder subsection 37(2), require to be supplied by the holders\nof licences at the time of payment of annual licensing charges\nin respect of the licences.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63-ss-3-logic-descriptionlogic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f39e9ba585448cee707893c6484b65366333b2e99e86d7041991c3df9ffa6d2",
      "skos:note": "Regulations may prescribe different fees under this Act."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/therapeutic-goods-act-1989#sec-63-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "63(3) Regulations",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 386,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The regulations may:\n(a) prescribe different fees under this Act in relation to:\n(i) different classes of goods; or\n(ii) in the case of fees under Part 3-3—different steps in the\nmanufacture of goods; or\n\nMiscellaneous  Chapter 7\n\nSection 63\nTherapeutic Goods Act 1989\nCompilation date: 05/09/2025\n(b) provide for the refund, reduction or waiving of fees or\ncharges in cases identified in the regulations; or\n(c) specify the type of information relating to therapeutic goods\nmanufactured by licence holders that the Secretary may,\nunder subsection 37(2), require to be supplied by the holders\nof licences at the time of payment of annual licensing charges\nin respect of the licences."
    },
