      "dc:source": "therapeutic-goods-act-1989.pdf, p.386",
      "values:originalText": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, the\nregulations may make provision in relation to a matter by applying,\nadopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) Despite subsection 14(2) of the Legislation Act 2003, the\nregulations may make provision in relation to a matter by applying,\nadopting or incorporating, with or without modification, any matter\ncontained in an instrument or other writing as in force or existing\nfrom time to time.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:therapeutic-goods-act-1989-sec-63-ss-4-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ed51b78bd78fabaaba38f9c4eea6a86d46d2401316e24251ed71d6f317bda886",
      "skos:note": "Regulations may incorporate existing instruments or writings."
    },
    {
